3	Januvia 50mg Tablets for Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus (2 Blisters x 14 Tablets)	P01616	\N	\N	Merck	USA	577907.00	497000.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/ecommerce/20250520035300-0-P01616.png?versionId=3252Gx9bDUUJsJH8yxNxM5HRKwoq668r	Januvia 50mg tablets for type 2 diabetes mellitus (2 blisters x 14 tablets)	{"contraindications": ["JANUVIA is contraindicated in patients with hypersensitivity to any of its components (see Precautions, Hypersensitivity Reactions and Adverse Reactions, Postmarketing Experience)."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "MSD", "origin": "USA", "storage": "Store below 30°C, protect from moisture and light.", "packaging": "Box of 2 blisters x 14 tablets", "manufacturer": "Merck Sharp & Dohme Limited"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "The recommended dose of JANUVIA is 100mg once daily as monotherapy or in combination with metformin, a sulfonylurea, insulin (with or without metformin), a PPAR - agonist (e.g., thiazolidinediones), or metformin plus a sulfonylurea, or metformin plus a PPAR - agonist. JANUVIA can be taken with or without food. When JANUVIA is used in combination with a sulfonylurea or insulin, a lower dose of the sulfonylurea or insulin may be considered to reduce the risk of sulfonylurea-induced hypoglycemia (see Precautions, Hypersensitivity Reactions, Hypoglycemia in Combination with Sulfonylurea or Insulin).\\n\\nRenal Impairment Patients: For patients with mild renal impairment (creatinine clearance [CrCl] - 50 mL/min, approximately corresponding to serum creatinine - 1.7 mg/dL in men and - 1.5 mg/dL in women), no dosage adjustment of JANUVIA is required. For patients with moderate renal impairment (CrCl - 30 to <50 mL/min, approximately corresponding to serum creatinine >1.7 to - 3.0 mg/dL in men and >1.5 to - 2.5 mg/dL in women), the dose of JANUVIA is 50mg once daily. For patients with severe renal impairment (CrCl <30 mL/min, approximately corresponding to serum creatinine >3.0 mg/dL in men and >2.5 mg/dL in women) or with end-stage renal disease (ESRD) requiring hemodialysis or peritoneal dialysis, the dose of JANUVIA is 25mg once daily. JANUVIA may be administered regardless of the timing of dialysis. Because there is a dosage adjustment based upon renal function, assessment of renal function is recommended prior to initiation of JANUVIA and periodically thereafter."}, "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Microcrystalline cellulose, anhydrous dibasic calcium phosphate, croscarmellose sodium, magnesium stearate, and sodium stearyl fumarate. In addition, the film coating contains the following excipients: polyvinyl alcohol, polyethylene glycol (macrogol), talc, titanium dioxide, red iron oxide, and yellow iron oxide.", "activeIngredients": "Each JANUVIA tablet contains 64.25mg of sitagliptin phosphate monohydrate, equivalent to 50mg of free base."}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "In clinical studies, the safety and effectiveness of JANUVIA in the elderly ( - 65 years) were similar to those in younger patients (<65 years). No dosage adjustment is necessary based on age. Elderly patients are more likely to have renal impairment; as with other drugs, dose adjustment may be required if significant renal impairment is present (see Dosage and Administration, Patients with Renal Impairment).", "lactation": "Sitagliptin is secreted in the milk of lactating rats. It is not known whether sitagliptin is secreted in human breast milk. Therefore, JANUVIA should not be used in women who are breast-feeding.", "pediatric": "Safety and effectiveness of JANUVIA in pediatric patients under 18 years of age have not been established.", "pregnancy": "Sitagliptin was not teratogenic in rats at oral doses up to 250 mg/kg or in rabbits up to 125 mg/kg during organogenesis (up to 32 times and 22 times the human exposure based on the recommended daily adult dose of 100 mg/day, respectively). A slight increased incidence of fetal rib malformations (absent, hypoplastic and beaded ribs) was observed in rats at oral doses of 1000 mg/kg/day (approximately 100 times the human exposure based on the recommended daily adult dose of 100 mg/day). When maternal rats were dosed at 1000 mg/kg/day, the mean pre-weaning body weight of both male and female pups and the post-weaning body weight gain of male pups were slightly reduced. However, animal reproduction studies are not always predictive of human response. Because there are no adequate and well-controlled studies in pregnant women, the safety of JANUVIA in pregnant women is not known. As with other oral antihyperglycemic agents, the use of JANUVIA during pregnancy is not recommended."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["General: JANUVIA should not be used in patients with type 1 diabetes or for the treatment of diabetic ketoacidosis.", "Pancreatitis: Postmarketing reports of acute pancreatitis, including fatal and non-fatal hemorrhagic or necrotizing pancreatitis (see Adverse Reactions, Postmarketing Experience), have been received in patients receiving sitagliptin. Because these reports are voluntarily reported from a population of uncertain size, it is generally not possible to reliably estimate their frequency or establish a causal relationship to drug exposure. Patients should be informed of the characteristic symptom of acute pancreatitis: persistent, severe abdominal pain. Pancreatitis was observed to resolve after discontinuation of sitagliptin. If pancreatitis is suspected, JANUVIA and other potentially suspect medicinal products should be discontinued.", "Hypoglycemia in Combination with Sulfonylurea or Insulin: In clinical trials of JANUVIA as monotherapy and in combination with agents known not to cause hypoglycemia (i.e., metformin or a PPAR - agonist (thiazolidinediones)), rates of hypoglycemia reported with JANUVIA were similar to rates in patients on placebo. As is true with other antihyperglycemic agents, hypoglycemia has been observed when JANUVIA was used in combination with insulin or a sulfonylurea (see Adverse Reactions). Therefore, to reduce the risk of hypoglycemia associated with a sulfonylurea or insulin, a lower dose of sulfonylurea or insulin may be considered (see Dosage and Administration).", "Hypersensitivity Reactions: There have been postmarketing reports of serious hypersensitivity reactions in patients treated with JANUVIA. These reactions include anaphylaxis, angioedema, and exfoliative skin conditions including Stevens-Johnson syndrome. Because these reports are voluntarily reported from a population of uncertain size, it is generally not possible to reliably estimate their frequency or establish a causal relationship to drug exposure. Onset of these reactions occurred within the first 3 months after initiation of treatment with JANUVIA, with some reports occurring after the first dose. If a hypersensitivity reaction is suspected, discontinue JANUVIA, assess for other potential causes, and institute alternative treatment for diabetes (see Contraindications and Adverse Reactions, Postmarketing Experience)."]}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:14:18.234	januvia-50mg-tablets-for-type-2-diabetes-mellitus-2-blisters-x-14-tablets	43
17	Povidine 10% Povidone-Iodine Antiseptic Dressing for Wounds, Burns, and Skin Conditions (Box of 10 Pads)	P01531	\N	\N	Pharmedic	Vietnam	94118.00	80000.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/ecommerce/20250415090629-0-P01531.jpg?versionId=5x2mZvDqAqiBMblh02qXIq2C2Y2C8PPM	Povidine 10% antiseptic dressing pads indicated for disinfection of wounds, superficial burns, and management of dermatological conditions (Box of 10 pads).	{"indications": ["Indicated for the antiseptic treatment of wounds, superficial burns, and the management of various dermatological conditions."], "sideEffects": ["Prolonged application may induce local irritation or, rarely, hypersensitivity and allergic skin reactions.", "Repeated application over extensive wounds or severe burns may lead to systemic iodine absorption and associated systemic reactions."], "drugInteractions": [{"drug": "Alkalis and proteins", "effect": "Antibacterial efficacy is significantly reduced."}, {"drug": "Soaps", "effect": "May reduce antiseptic efficacy; however, it does not completely abolish it."}, {"drug": "Mercury compounds", "effect": "Concomitant use may form caustic compounds and cause severe local tissue irritation."}, {"drug": "Sodium thiosulfate, sunlight, high temperatures, and other oxidizing antiseptics", "effect": "Causes degradation and loss of pharmacological efficacy."}, {"drug": "Thyroid function tests (e.g., PBI, radioactive iodine uptake)", "effect": "May interfere with diagnostic test results."}], "contraindications": ["Known hypersensitivity to iodine or povidone.", "Regular or frequent use in patients with pre-existing thyroid disorders.", "Pregnant and lactating women.", "Neonates and infants under 2 years of age."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Pharmedic", "origin": "Vietnam", "storage": "Store in a dry place, protected from direct light, at temperatures not exceeding 30°C.", "packaging": "Box of 10 pads", "manufacturer": "Pharmedic Pharmaceutical Medicinal Joint Stock Company"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Apply to the affected wound area once daily or once every 2 days as directed by a healthcare professional.", "administration": "Aseptically open the outer protective packaging.,Apply the medicated dressing directly onto the wound surface and carefully peel away the protective nylon layer.,Cover with a sterile gauze pad or absorbent cotton, then secure with an appropriate bandage.,Povidine dressing contains a water-soluble ointment base that can be easily rinsed off with clean water."}, "generalDescription": "Povidine 10% dressing is a sterile, medicated pad designed to disinfect wounds and superficial burns while managing various skin conditions. It forms an antimicrobial protective barrier to support the physiological wound healing process.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Polyethylene glycol 400, Polyethylene glycol 4000, purified water q.s. to 100g", "activeIngredients": "Povidone-iodine 10g"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "Contraindicated as iodine is excreted in breast milk and may cause thyroid dysfunction in the nursing infant.", "pediatric": "Contraindicated in neonates and children under 2 years of age due to the risk of systemic iodine absorption and thyroid suppression.", "pregnancy": "Contraindicated due to the risk of transplacental iodine absorption affecting fetal thyroid function."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Exercise extreme caution when applying frequently to compromised skin or open wounds in patients with a history of renal impairment or those undergoing concurrent lithium therapy."]}	f	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:15:04.562	povidine-10percent-povidone-iodine-antiseptic-dressing-for-wounds-burns-and-skin-conditions-box-of	211
138	Duphalac (Lactulose) 667g/L Oral Solution for Constipation and Hepatic Encephalopathy (200ml Bottle)	P01710	\N	\N	Abbott	Vietnam	146067.00	130000.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/ecommerce/20250508070523-0-P01710.jpg?versionId=P.YUUY44EPLTifKnFHtvmcnwgH9aa6io	Duphalac oral solution contains lactulose, indicated for the treatment of constipation and hepatic encephalopathy.	{"indications": ["Treatment of constipation", "Softening of stools for medical reasons", "Treatment of hepatic coma and pre-coma (hepatic encephalopathy)"], "sideEffects": ["Very Common: Diarrhea", "Common: Flatulence, abdominal pain, nausea, vomiting", "Uncommon: Electrolyte imbalance due to diarrhea"], "drugInteractions": [{"drug": "Not identified", "effect": "No interaction studies have been performed."}], "effectsOnDriving": "No or negligible influence on the ability to drive and use machines.", "contraindications": ["Hypersensitivity (allergy) to lactulose or any component of the drug.", "Galactosemia.", "Gastrointestinal obstruction, gastrointestinal perforation, or risk of gastrointestinal perforation."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Duphalac", "manufacturer": "Abbott"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Constipation: Adults & Adolescents (Initial: 15-45ml; Maintenance: 15-30ml). Children 7-14 years (Initial: 15ml; Maintenance: 5-10ml). Children 1-6 years (Initial: 5-10ml). Infants under 1 year (Less than 5ml). Hepatic Encephalopathy (Adults): 30-45ml or 2-3 sachets, 3-4 times/day.", "missedDose": "Take as soon as possible when remembered. If it is almost time for the next dose, skip the missed dose and take the next dose according to the regular schedule. Do not double the dose.", "administration": "Can be taken diluted or undiluted. A single dose should be taken at once, without holding it in the mouth for an extended period. It should be taken at the same time each day (e.g., in the morning). Adequate fluid intake (1.5 - 2 liters of water daily) is recommended.", "over