tes the risk of systemic hypotension."}, {"drug": "Fluconazole", "effect": "Reduces the plasma concentration of the active metabolite by approximately 50%."}, {"drug": "Rifampicin", "effect": "Reduces the plasma concentration of the active metabolite by approximately 40%."}, {"drug": "Potassium-sparing diuretics, potassium supplements, salt substitutes containing potassium, heparin", "effect": "Increases the risk of serum potassium elevation (hyperkalemia)."}, {"drug": "Lithium", "effect": "Reduces lithium excretion; rigorous monitoring of serum lithium levels is clinically required."}, {"drug": "Non-Steroidal Anti-Inflammatory Drugs (NSAIDs), including selective COX-2 inhibitors", "effect": "Attenuates the antihypertensive efficacy, impairs renal function, and increases the risk of hyperkalemia."}], "effectsOnDriving": "The medicinal product may occasionally cause dizziness or drowsiness, particularly at the initiation of treatment or when dosage is increased; patients should exercise caution when driving or operating heavy machinery.", "contraindications": ["Hypersensitivity to losartan or any of the inactive excipients contained in the formulation.", "Second and third trimesters of pregnancy.", "Patients with severe hepatic impairment or biliary cirrhosis.", "Concomitant use of losartan-containing products with aliskiren in patients with diabetes mellitus or renal impairment (glomerular filtration rate GFR < 60 mL/min/1.73m - ).", "Patients with primary hyperaldosteronism."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Pymepharco", "origin": "Vietnam", "storage": "Store in a dry place at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Protect from direct light and moisture.", "packaging": "Carton containing 2 blister packs of 15 film-coated tablets each", "manufacturer": "Pymepharco Joint Stock Company"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Dosage is individualized based on the therapeutic indication (hypertension, renal disease, heart failure, stroke risk reduction) and clinical characteristics of the patient population (adults, pediatric patients, elderly, patients with hepatic or renal impairment). The standard initial dosage ranges from 12.5 mg to 50 mg administered once daily.", "administration": "Administer orally, with or without food.", "overdoseManagement": "The predominant manifestations of acute overdose are hypotension and tachycardia; bradycardia may also develop secondary to parasympathetic stimulation. If symptomatic hypotension occurs, appropriate cardiovascular supportive measures must be instituted immediately. Neither losartan nor its active metabolite can be cleared from the circulation via hemodialysis."}, "generalDescription": "Pyzacar 50mg is a pharmaceutical preparation containing Losartan potassium 50mg as the active pharmaceutical ingredient, belonging to the pharmacological class of Angiotensin II Receptor Blockers (ARBs). It is primarily indicated for the management of hypertension and associated cardiovascular and renal conditions.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Microcrystalline cellulose, lactose monohydrate, crospovidone, stearic acid, colloidal anhydrous silica, hypromellose, polyethylene glycol 400 (PEG 400), polyethylene glycol 6000 (PEG 6000), magnesium stearate, titanium dioxide, indigo carmine aluminum lake, D&C Yellow #10 aluminum lake.", "activeIngredients": "Losartan potassium 50mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "An initial starting dose of 25 mg once daily should be considered for elderly patients aged 75 years and older.", "lactation": "It is not known whether losartan is excreted in human breast milk; because of the potential for adverse effects on the nursing infant, a clinical decision must be made whether to discontinue breastfeeding or discontinue the medication, taking into account the importance of the drug to the mother.", "pediatric": "Not recommended for pediatric patients under 6 years of age, pediatric patients with a glomerular filtration rate < 30 mL/min/1.73m - , or pediatric patients with hepatic impairment. Dosage for pediatric patients aged 6 to 18 years must be titrated based on body weight.", "pregnancy": "Contraindicated during the second and third trimesters of pregnancy due to the risk of direct toxicity to the developing fetal and neonatal renal system. Therapy should be discontinued immediately upon confirmation of pregnancy."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Hypersensitivity: Patients with a prior history of angioedema (swelling of the face, lips, pharynx, and/or tongue) require rigorous clinical monitoring.", "Hypotension and Fluid/Electrolyte Imbalance: Symptomatic hypotension, especially after the initial dose, may occur in patients who are intravascularly volume-depleted (e.g., those treated with high-dose diuretics). Such conditions should be corrected prior to initiating therapy.", "Electrolyte Imbalance: Hyperkalemia is frequently observed in patients with renal impairment and/or heart failure; serum electrolyte levels and creatinine clearance must be closely monitored.", "Renal Impairment: Caution is warranted in patients with bilateral renal artery stenosis or renal artery stenosis in a single functioning kidney, as increases in blood urea and serum creatinine have been reported.", "Ischemic Heart Disease and Cerebrovascular Disease: Excessive blood pressure reduction in patients with ischemic cardiovascular or cerebrovascular pathology could precipitate a myocardial infarction or stroke.", "Heart Failure: Caution is advised in patients with severe heart failure or concomitant severe renal impairment.", "Excipients: Contains lactose monohydrate; patients with rare hereditary problems of galactose intolerance, total lactase deficiency, or glucose-galactose malabsorption should not take this medicine.", "Dual Blockade of the Renin-Angiotensin-Aldosterone System (RAAS): Dual blockade utilizing ACE inhibitors, ARBs, or aliskiren is associated with an increased risk of hypotension, hyperkalemia, and changes in renal function compared to monotherapy."], "adverseReactionManagement": "Patients should promptly report any adverse events, unexpected symptoms, or drug intolerance to their treating physician or qualified healthcare professional."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:27:47.855	pyzacar-50mg-film-coated-tablets-losartan-potassium-for-hypertension-and-renal-disease-2-blister	41
