2	Enervon Multivitamin B-Complex and Vitamin C 500mg Film-Coated Tablets for Immune Support and Fatigue Reduction (10 Blisters x 10 Tablets)	P01232	\N	\N	United International Pharma	Vietnam	31438.00	22950.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/ecommerce/20250415090618-0-P01232.jpg?versionId=mF62JFJeUNf6_Nl3dpWlwclyf9AaFldN	Enervon is a high-potency multivitamin supplement containing B-complex vitamins and Vitamin C, formulated to boost immune function, combat fatigue, and support overall metabolic health.	{"sideEffects": ["Ascorbic Acid (Vitamin C): Common: Hyperoxaluria at high doses. Uncommon: Hemolytic anemia, hemolysis, facial flushing, cardiac failure, syncope, dizziness, headache, fatigue, nausea, vomiting, heartburn, diarrhea, and flank pain.", "Thiamine (Vitamin B1): Adverse reactions are extremely rare and generally manifest as hypersensitivity or allergic reactions, predominantly observed following parenteral administration.", "Niacinamide (Vitamin B3): Induces cutaneous vasodilation over the face and upper torso, resulting in flushing, transient nausea, and palpitations. These pharmacological effects present immediately post-administration and typically resolve spontaneously within 30 to 40 minutes.", "Calcium Pantothenate (Vitamin B5): May infrequently provoke mild hypersensitivity reactions, including localized pruritus and transient diarrhea.", "Pyridoxine (Vitamin B6): Daily doses of 200 mg or greater administered chronically (exceeding 2 months) can precipitate severe peripheral neuropathy, characterized by progression from an unsteady gait and distal paresthesia to numbness and clumsiness in the extremities. This neurotoxic effect is generally reversible upon discontinuation of the agent. Rare: Nausea and vomiting.", "Cyanocobalamin (Vitamin B12): Immune-mediated hypersensitivity reactions are rare but can occasionally be severe. Rare: Anaphylaxis, pyrexia, acneiform eruptions, urticaria, pruritus, and erythema."], "drugInteractions": [{"drug": "Ascorbic Acid + Iron", "effect": "Concurrent administration of greater than 200 mg of vitamin C with 30 mg of elemental iron significantly enhances gastrointestinal iron absorption."}, {"drug": "Ascorbic Acid + Aspirin", "effect": "Co-administration of vitamin C and aspirin increases the renal excretion of ascorbic acid while concurrently decreasing the urinary excretion of aspirin."}, {"drug": "Ascorbic Acid + Fluphenazine", "effect": "Concurrent administration results in diminished plasma concentrations of fluphenazine."}, {"drug": "Thiamine, Cyanocobalamin + other B-complex vitamins, Ascorbic Acid, and mineral salts", "effect": "Compatible for combination in standard tablet or sugar-coated tablet dosage forms."}, {"drug": "Riboflavin + Chlorpromazine, Imipramine, Amitriptyline", "effect": "Concurrent use may precipitate functional riboflavin deficiency in susceptible individuals."}, {"drug": "Riboflavin + Ethanol", "effect": "Chronic or acute alcohol consumption may impair the intestinal mucosal absorption of riboflavin."}, {"drug": "Riboflavin + Probenecid", "effect": "Concomitant administration with probenecid leads to reduced gastrointestinal absorption of riboflavin."}, {"drug": "Niacinamide + HMG-CoA Reductase Inhibitors", "effect": "May elevate the risk of developing myopathy and rhabdomyolysis."}, {"drug": "Niacinamide + Antihypertensive Alpha-Adrenergic Blockers", "effect": "Potentiates hypotensive effects, potentially leading to excessive blood pressure reduction."}, {"drug": "Niacinamide + Oral Hypoglycemic Agents or Insulin", "effect": "Antidiabetic medication dosage adjustments may be necessary to maintain glycemic control."}, {"drug": "Niacinamide + Hepatotoxic Agents", "effect": "May exacerbate hepatotoxic adverse reactions."}, {"drug": "Niacinamide + Carbamazepine", "effect": "Elevates plasma carbamazepine concentrations, potentially increasing pharmacological toxicity."}, {"drug": "Calcium Pantothenate + Ophthalmic Anticholinesterase Agents", "effect": "The miosis-inducing pharmacodynamic effects of topical ophthalmic anticholinesterases (e.g., ecothiopate iodide, isoflurophate) may be enhanced."}, {"drug": "Calcium Pantothenate + Succinylcholine", "effect": "Should not be administered within 1 hour following the use of succinylcholine, as it may abnormally prolong the neuromuscular blockade and muscle-relaxant duration of succinylcholine."}, {"drug": "Pyridoxine + Levodopa", "effect": "Pyridoxine accelerates the peripheral decarboxylation of levodopa, thereby decreasing its therapeutic efficacy in the management of Parkinson's disease."}, {"drug": "Pyridoxine (200 mg/day) + Phenytoin and Phenobarbital", "effect": "May induce a 40% to 50% reduction in serum concentrations of phenytoin and phenobarbital in specific patient populations."}, {"drug": "Pyridoxine + Oral Contraceptives", "effect": "May ameliorate depressive symptoms in women using oral contraceptives; conversely, oral contraceptives can increase metabolic requirements for pyridoxine."}], "contraindications": ["Ascorbic Acid (Vitamin C): Contraindicated for high-dose administration in patients with glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase (G6PD) deficiency, a history of nephrolithiasis, hyperoxaluria, oxalate metabolism disorders, or thalassemia.", "Thiamine (Vitamin B1) and Riboflavin (Vitamin B2): Documented hypersensitivity to Vitamin B1 or Vitamin B2.", "Niacinamide (Vitamin B3): Known hypersensitivity to niacin, severe hepatic impairment, active peptic ulcer disease, arterial hemorrhage, and severe hypotension.", "Pyridoxine (Vitamin B6): Documented hypersensitivity to Vitamin B6.", "Cyanocobalamin (Vitamin B12): History of hypersensitivity reactions to cobalamins and presence of malignant neoplasms."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "United International Pharma", "origin": "Vietnam", "storage": "Store in a dry place at controlled room temperatures not exceeding 30°C, protected from excessive moisture and direct light.", "packaging": "Carton containing 10 blisters x 10 film-coated tablets.", "manufacturer": "United International Pharma"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Adults and adolescents aged 16 years and older: Administer orally, one tablet daily, or strictly in accordance with a physician's prescription."}, "generalDescription": "Enervon tablets are a comprehensive multivitamin preparation indicated for the supplementation of essential water-soluble vitamins, specifically Vitamin C and the B-complex group. This therapeutic formulation aids in bolstering immune defense mechanisms, mitigating physical fatigue, and supporting normal physiological and enzymatic functions.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Magnesium Oxide, Colloidal Silicon Dioxide, Magnesium Stearate, Opadry Film Coating System.", "activeIngredients": "Ascorbic Acid 500mg, Thiamine Mononitrate 50mg, Riboflavin 20mg, Niacinamide 50mg, Calcium Pantothenate 20mg, Pyridoxine Hydrochloride 5mg, Cyanocobalamin 5mcg."}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "Routine daily dietary intake of B-complex vitamins and vitamin C during lactation is generally recognized as safe and has not been correlated with adverse clinical effects in nursing infants.", "pregnancy": "Standard recommended dietary allowances of vitamins C and B during pregnancy have not been associated with adverse fetal outcomes. However, chronic excessive daily intake of ascorbic acid during gestation may precipitate neonatal vitamin C deficiency syndrome."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Ascorbic Acid (Vitamin C): Prolonged high-dose intake may induce metabolic tolerance, resulting in signs of vitamin C deficiency upon abrupt dosage reduction. High doses during pregnancy have been associated with rebound scurvy in neonates. Hyperoxaluria and urinary tract acidification may occur, potentially precipitating urate or cystine renal calculi, oxalate stones, or crystallization of concurrent medications within the renal tubules. Patients with glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase (G6PD