ations (e.g., scabies, pediculosis)", "Individuals with a known hypersensitivity to betamethasone, gentamicin, clotrimazole, or any other component of this medication", "External otitis eczema associated with a perforated tympanic membrane", "Skin ulcers (except when associated with Beh - et's disease), second-degree burns or greater", "Perioral dermatitis, acne vulgaris, and rosacea", "Known hypersensitivity to aminoglycoside antibiotics (e.g., streptomycin, kanamycin, gentamicin, neomycin)", "Known hypersensitivity to imidazole-derivative antifungals"], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Dong Kwang Pharm. Co., Ltd. (South Korea)", "origin": "South Korea", "storage": "Store in a dry place at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Protect from direct light and freezing.", "packaging": "Carton containing 1 collapsible aluminum tube of 10g."}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Apply a thin layer of cream to completely cover the affected skin area twice daily, in the morning and evening. Gently massage into the skin. Consistent use is recommended for optimal therapeutic outcomes.", "missedDose": "If a dose is missed, apply it as soon as remembered. However, if it is nearly time for the next scheduled application, skip the missed dose and resume the normal dosing regimen. Do not apply a double dose to make up for a forgotten application.", "administration": "Silkron 10g topical cream is intended for dermatological external use only. Avoid contact with eyes, mucous membranes, and open wounds.", "overdoseManagement": "Acute overdosage symptoms from topical administration are not clearly defined. Prolonged or excessive use may lead to systemic corticosteroid suppression or aminoglycoside accumulation. If systemic toxicity or severe adverse reactions are suspected, discontinue use immediately and seek professional medical evaluation for supportive management."}, "generalDescription": "Silkron topical cream is a broad-spectrum dermatological medication formulated to treat various inflammatory and infectious skin disorders. It combines the anti-inflammatory and vasoconstrictive properties of a corticosteroid, the antibacterial action of an aminoglycoside, and the antifungal efficacy of an azole derivative.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Cetanol, stearyl alcohol, liquid paraffin, polysorbate 60, sorbitan monostearate, propylene glycol, citric acid hydrate, edetate disodium hydrate, methylparaben, propylparaben, purified water", "activeIngredients": "Betamethasone dipropionate 0.64mg, Clotrimazole 10.00mg, Gentamicin sulfate 1.00mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "Exercise caution when administering to nursing mothers. It is unknown whether topical application results in sufficient systemic absorption to excrete measurable quantities into human breast milk.", "pregnancy": "The safety of topical corticosteroids and combination antimicrobials during pregnancy has not been definitively established. Use in pregnant women or women of childbearing potential is not recommended unless the potential clinical benefit outweighs the potential fetal risks, as teratogenic and embryotoxic effects have been observed in animals following topical corticosteroid exposure."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Topical corticosteroids absorbed systemically can produce reversible suppression of the hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal (HPA) axis, manifestations of Cushing's syndrome, hyperglycemia, latent diabetes mellitus, and systemic osteoporosis.", "Avoid long-term continuous use, large treatment surface areas, and the use of occlusive dressings, as these practices significantly increase systemic absorption and the risk of systemic adverse effects characteristic of systemic corticosteroid therapy.", "Concomitant administration with systemic aminoglycoside antibiotics may result in cumulative toxicity. Particular caution and risk-benefit evaluation are required when administering to neonates and pediatric patients due to a higher ratio of skin surface area to body weight."], "adverseReactionManagement": "In the event of hypersensitivity, severe irritation, or systemic adverse reactions, discontinue medication use immediately, contact a qualified physician, or seek evaluation at the nearest medical facility for appropriate clinical management."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 20:30:09.412	silkron-betamethasone-0-64mg-gentamicin-1mg-clotrimazole-10mg-topical-cream-for-dermatological	286
