n of scurvy. Geriatric patients: No special dosage adjustments required.", "missedDose": "This medication is administered in a healthcare facility under medical supervision; missed doses are unlikely to occur.", "administration": "Parenteral administration should be reserved for special cases where oral routes are not feasible or impaired gastrointestinal absorption is suspected. Administration may be via intramuscular, intravenous, or subcutaneous injection, with intramuscular injection being preferred.", "overdoseManagement": "Manifestations: Nephrolithiasis (kidney stones), nausea, gastritis, diarrhea. Management: Forced diuresis via intravenous fluid administration may be beneficial following massive overdoses."}, "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Ascorbic Acid 500mg/5mL"}}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:41:58.474	vitamin-c-kabi-500mg-5ml-intramuscular-intravenous-injection-solution-6-ampoules	\N
