iliary routes. The terminal elimination half-life is 5 to 9 hours in healthy young adults, and prolonged to 11 to 13 hours in the elderly population."}, "manufacturingInfo": {"origin": "India", "storage": "Store in a dry place at controlled room temperature below 30°C, protected from moisture.", "packaging": "Box of 1 blister pack x 14 oral tablets", "manufacturer": "Dr. Reddy's Laboratories Ltd."}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Dosage is strictly individualized based on the specific clinical indication (e.g., stroke prevention or DVT/PE treatment). Strictly follow the prescribed dosing regimen corresponding to each phase of anticoagulant therapy.", "missedDose": "If a dose is missed, the patient should take Rivaroxaban immediately upon remembering on the same day to ensure the intake of the daily total dose. Do not take a double dose to make up for a forgotten tablet.", "administration": "For oral administration. The 15 mg tablet should be taken with food. For patients with dysphagia or those unable to swallow whole tablets, Rivaroxaban tablets may be crushed and mixed with water or apple puree immediately prior to oral administration and delivered via a nasogastric tube."}, "generalDescription": "Rivaxored 15mg contains Rivaroxaban, an oral direct Factor Xa inhibitor that selectively blocks the active site of Factor Xa, thereby interrupting the intrinsic and extrinsic pathway of the blood coagulation cascade and preventing thrombin generation.", "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Rivaroxaban 15 mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "No dosage adjustment is required based solely on advanced age.", "lactation": "Available pharmacokinetic data in humans indicate that Rivaroxaban is excreted into human breast milk. A clinical decision must be made whether to discontinue breastfeeding or to discontinue/abstain from Rivaroxaban therapy, taking into account the benefit of breastfeeding for the child and the benefit of therapy for the woman.", "pediatric": "Safety and effectiveness in pediatric patients aged 0 to 18 years have not been established. Administration in children is not recommended.", "pregnancy": "There are no adequate and well-controlled studies regarding the use of Rivaroxaban in pregnant women. Animal studies have shown reproductive toxicity. Use during pregnancy is not recommended."}}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:42:48.188	rivaxored-15-mg-oral-tablets-for-thromboprophylaxis-and-anticoagulation-dr-reddy-s-box-of-1-blister	243
