and enzymatic degradation in the upper digestive tract.", "elimination": "Excreted primarily via metabolic pathways, with elimination of breakdown products occurring through fecal and renal pathways."}, "contraindications": ["Contraindicated in patients with known hypersensitivity to alpha-chymotrypsin or any excipients in the formulation. Not recommended for patients with decreased or increased vitreous pressure, congenital cataracts, or severe uncontrolled coagulopathies (such as hemophilia)."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "HA TAY", "origin": "Vietnam", "storage": "Store in a dry place, protected from moisture and direct light, at a temperature not exceeding 30°C.", "packaging": "Carton containing 2 blisters x 10 dispersible tablets.", "manufacturer": "Ha Tay Pharmaceutical Joint Stock Company"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Administer 1 to 2 tablets per dose, taken 2 times daily, or as directed by the prescribing physician.", "missedDose": "Take the missed dose as soon as remembered. If it is almost time for the scheduled administration of the next dose, omit the missed dose and resume the standard dosing schedule. Do not administer a double dose to make up for a forgotten dose.", "administration": "Oral administration. Disperse the tablet completely in a sufficient volume of water (approximately 5-10 mL, equivalent to one full teaspoon) prior to ingestion, or swallow the tablet whole with an adequate amount of water."}, "generalDescription": "Chymodk 8.4 mg, containing alpha-chymotrypsin as the active pharmaceutical ingredient, is an enzymatic anti-inflammatory agent utilized to alleviate soft tissue swelling and inflammation caused by localized infections, tissue injuries, or surgical procedures.", "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Alpha-Chymotrypsin 8.4 mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "It is not known whether alpha-chymotrypsin is excreted into human breast milk. Caution should be exercised when administering this product to nursing women; use only when clinically indicated and deemed strictly necessary by a physician.", "pregnancy": "Adequate and well-controlled clinical studies in pregnant women are lacking. This medication should be used during pregnancy only if the potential clinical benefit clearly outweighs the potential fetal risks, and strictly under the direct supervision of a physician."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Chymotrypsin should be administered with extreme caution in patients with reduced cardiac or pulmonary function, severe hepatic impairment, peptic ulcer disease, or bleeding disorders. The use of chymotrypsin during cataract surgery in patients younger than 20 years of age is generally discouraged due to a significantly increased risk of vitreous loss."], "adverseReactionManagement": "Discontinue administration immediately and seek prompt medical attention if signs of hypersensitivity, severe allergic reactions, or paradoxical increases in pain and swelling occur. Report any adverse events or undesirable pharmacological effects encountered during therapy to a qualified healthcare professional."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:24:14.846	chymodk-8-4mg-dispersible-tablets-for-post-traumatic-post-surgical-and-burn-edema-2-blisters-x-10	312
