ciated with increased intracranial pressure (head trauma, cerebral hemorrhage)", "Angle-closure glaucoma", "Concomitant use with phosphodiesterase-5 (PDE-5) inhibitors (e.g., sildenafil, tadalafil, vardenafil) or soluble guanylate cyclase (sGC) stimulators (e.g., riociguat)"], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Egis Pharmaceuticals PLC / Distributed by Viet Ha Pharmaceutical Joint Stock Company", "origin": "Vietnam", "storage": "Store in a dry, cool place at temperatures not exceeding 30°C (86°F). Protect from direct sunlight and freezing. Keep away from naked flames and sources of heat.", "packaging": "Carton containing 1 pressurized canister of 10 g", "manufacturer": "Viet Ha Pharmaceutical Joint Stock Company"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Each actuation delivers 0.4 mg of nitroglycerin. For acute angina attacks: Administer 1 to 2 sprays sublingually onto or under the tongue while the patient is seated. The dose may be repeated if necessary at 5-minute intervals, not to exceed a total of 3 sprays within a 15-minute period. For prophylaxis of angina induced by physical exertion or emotional stress: Administer 1 spray 5 to 10 minutes prior to anticipated exertion.", "administration": "For sublingual administration only as a metered spray. Do not inhale the spray. Prime the pump prior to initial use by releasing several sprays into the air away from the face.", "overdoseManagement": "Overdose may result in severe hypotension, persistent throbbing headache, visual disturbances, vertigo, tachycardia, syncope, methemoglobinemia, and cardiovascular collapse. In the event of an overdose, immediately discontinue administration, place the patient in a recumbent position with the lower extremities elevated, monitor vital signs, and seek emergency medical intervention or contact a poison control center immediately."}, "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Nitroglycerin 8 mg/g (0.4 mg per metered actuation)"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "Use with caution; elderly individuals may be more susceptible to systemic hypotension and orthostatic dizziness.", "lactation": "Use with caution. It is unknown whether nitroglycerin is excreted in human milk; evaluate the risk-benefit ratio prior to administration under close medical supervision.", "pregnancy": "Use with caution. Safety during pregnancy has not been established; administer only if clearly needed and under strict medical supervision."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Use with caution in elderly patients, patients with severe hepatic or renal impairment, hypothyroidism, malnutrition, severe cerebral arteriosclerosis, orthostatic hypotension, mitral valve prolapse, cor pulmonale, and patients with underlying lactase deficiency or glucose-galactose malabsorption syndromes.", "Tolerance to organic nitrates may develop with continuous or prolonged administration. Patients undergoing long-term nitroglycerin therapy who require transition to alternative anti-anginal regimens should have their nitroglycerin therapy tapered gradually to avoid acute withdrawal rebound angina."]}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:25:38.872	nitromint-nitroglycerin-0-4mg-spray-sublingual-spray-for-the-prevention-and-treatment-of-angina	318
