ntration of 14.8° 8.6 ng/mL is achieved approximately 7.25° 1.04 hours following a single intramuscular injection of 40 mg.", "metabolism": "Metabolized primarily in the liver via CYP3A4 into inactive metabolites (20°-hydroxymethylprednisolone and 20°-hydroxymethylprednisolone).", "elimination": "The mean elimination half-life ranges from 1.8 to 5.2 hours. Total body clearance is approximately 5 to 6 mL/min/kg."}, "manufacturingInfo": {"storage": "Store at controlled room temperature not exceeding 30°C."}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Dosage requirements are variable and must be individualized based on the specific disease entity and patient response. Intramuscular: 40°120 mg weekly. Intra-articular: 4°10 mg for small joints, 10°40 mg for medium joints, and 20°80 mg for large joints. Intralesional: 20°60 mg.", "missedDose": "Administer the missed dose as soon as remembered. If it is almost time for the next scheduled dose, skip the missed dose. Do not double doses.", "administration": "Administered via intramuscular, intra-articular, periarticular, soft tissue, tendon sheath, or intralesional injection. Strictly prohibited for intravenous or intrathecal administration. Shake well before use to ensure a uniform suspension. Maintain strict aseptic technique.", "overdoseManagement": "There is no clinical syndrome of acute overdosage with glucocorticoids. Treatment is supportive and symptomatic. Methylprednisolone is dialyzable."}, "generalDescription": "Depo-Medrol 40mg injection contains the active ingredient methylprednisolone acetate, a potent anti-inflammatory glucocorticoid steroid that possesses greater anti-inflammatory potency than prednisolone and causes significantly less sodium and water retention.", "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Methylprednisolone acetate 40 mg/mL"}}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:38:16.766	depo-medrol-40mg-ml-sterile-aqueous-suspension-for-injection-1-ml-vial	\N
