may be impaired as a result of hypoglycemia, hyperglycemia, or visual impairment, posing a hazard when driving or operating machinery.", "contraindications": ["Hypersensitivity to insulin glargine or any of the excipients of this medication."], "manufacturingInfo": {"storage": "Store in the outer carton to protect from light. Do not freeze. Unopened vials should be stored at 2°C to 8°C. Once removed from refrigeration, the vial may be stored at temperatures up to +30°C for a maximum of 4 weeks. Opened vials must be discarded after 28 days.", "packaging": "Box of 1 vial of 10 mL (1000 IU)", "manufacturer": "Sanofi - Aventis Deutschland GmbH"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Administer subcutaneously once daily at the same time every day. Dosage is individualized based on clinical response and metabolic requirements under medical supervision. When switching from once-daily NPH insulin to Lantus, the initial basal insulin dose must be reduced by approximately 20% compared to the total daily NPH dose, followed by individualized dosage titration.", "missedDose": "Administer as soon as remembered. If it is almost time for the next scheduled dose, skip the missed dose and resume the regular dosing schedule. Do not double doses.", "administration": "Lantus is administered subcutaneously. Within a given injection area, rotate the injection sites from one injection to the next. Do not administer intravenously. Inspect the vial prior to use; use only if the solution is clear, colorless, and free of solid particulate matter. Do not dilute or mix with any other insulin preparation or solution.", "overdoseManagement": "Overdose may result in severe, life-threatening hypoglycemia. Mild episodes of hypoglycemia can usually be treated with oral carbohydrates. Severe hypoglycemic episodes with coma, seizure, or neurologic impairment may be treated with intramuscular/subcutaneous glucagon or concentrated intravenous glucose solution."}, "generalDescription": "Lantus 100 IU/mL is manufactured by Sanofi-Aventis Deutschland GmbH, containing insulin glargine as the active pharmaceutical ingredient, utilized for the treatment of diabetes mellitus. Lantus 100 IU/mL is formulated as an injection solution containing 100 IU per mL, supplied in a box of 1 vial of 10 mL (1000 IU).", "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Insulin glargine 100 IU/mL"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "Progressive deterioration of renal function may lead to a gradual decrease in insulin requirements.", "lactation": "Adjustment of dosage and dietary regimen may be necessary.", "pediatric": "Safety and efficacy have not been established in children under 6 years of age.", "pregnancy": "Strict metabolic control is essential. Insulin requirements typically decrease during the first trimester, increase during the second and third trimesters, and decline rapidly postpartum."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Patients must receive adequate instruction on self-management of diabetes mellitus (blood glucose monitoring, proper injection techniques, and management of special circumstances).", "Underlying compliance issues or incorrect injection technique must be ruled out before considering dosage adjustment for uncontrolled blood glucose.", "Clinical experience is limited in children under 6 years of age, patients with hepatic impairment, and patients with moderate to severe renal impairment.", "Insulin requirements may be reduced in patients with renal impairment, elderly patients, and patients with severe hepatic impairment."], "adverseReactionManagement": "Discontinue use, notify the prescribing physician, or seek medical attention at the nearest healthcare facility for prompt management of adverse reactions."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:46:22.148	lantus-100-iu-ml-injection-solution-for-diabetes-mellitus-box-of-1-vial-x-10-ml	85
