thmics)", "effect": "Increased risk of cardiac arrhythmias."}, {"drug": "Corticosteroids", "effect": "Increased risk of tendinitis and tendon rupture."}, {"drug": "Theophylline", "effect": "Requires monitoring of serum concentrations and dosage adjustment."}, {"drug": "Warfarin", "effect": "Enhanced anticoagulant effect, requires monitoring of coagulation parameters (INR)."}, {"drug": "Cyclosporine / Tacrolimus", "effect": "Requires monitoring of plasma concentrations."}, {"drug": "NSAIDs", "effect": "Increased risk of central nervous system stimulation and seizures."}, {"drug": "Hypoglycemic agents", "effect": "Increased risk of glucose homeostasis disorders."}], "effectsOnDriving": "Do not drive or operate machinery while taking this medication due to potential central nervous system adverse effects.", "pharmacodynamics": {"mechanismOfAction": "Bactericidal action resulting from the inhibition of topoisomerase II (DNA gyrase) and topoisomerase IV, which are essential enzymes required for bacterial DNA replication, transcription, and repair.", "pharmacologicalClass": "Fluoroquinolone antibacterial agent, fluoroquinolone derivative (ATC code: J01MA12)."}, "pharmacokinetics": {"absorption": "Widely distributed throughout the body, with poor penetration into cerebrospinal fluid. Plasma protein binding is approximately 30-40%.", "metabolism": "Minimally metabolized, with less than 5% of the dose converted into desmethyl and N-oxide metabolites.", "elimination": "Eliminated almost entirely via the urine (87% as unchanged drug), and approximately 12.8% in the feces. The elimination half-life is 6-8 hours, prolonged in patients with renal impairment. Not effectively removed by hemodialysis or peritoneal dialysis."}, "contraindications": ["Hypersensitivity to levofloxacin or other quinolones.", "Epilepsy.", "Glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase (G6PD) deficiency.", "History of tendon disorders associated with fluoroquinolone administration.", "Pediatric patients under 18 year