eratures not exceeding 30°C.", "packaging": "Box of 10 blisters x 10 enteric-coated tablets", "manufacturer": "Pharmedic Pharmaceutical Medical Materials Joint Stock Company"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Initial dose: 1 tablet, 3 times daily. Maintenance dose: 1 tablet, twice daily. Dysmenorrhea: 1 tablet, twice daily. Dosage recommendations are for reference purposes only.", "missedDose": "If a dose is missed, take it as soon as possible. However, if it is almost time for the next dose, skip the missed dose and resume the regular dosing schedule. Do not double the dose.", "administration": "Swallow the tablets whole with water without chewing, preferably before meals.", "overdoseManagement": "Acute diclofenac toxicity: Manifests as more severe adverse effects. Management: Transfer the patient immediately to a medical facility for prompt medical intervention."}, "generalDescription": "Diclofen is a nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID) used for pain relief, reduction of inflammation, and fever management. The medication is commonly prescribed for the treatment of conditions such as arthritis, back pain, toothache, and other musculoskeletal pain.", "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Diclofenac sodium 50mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "Diclofenac is excreted into breast milk in very small amounts. There are no clinical data regarding effects on breastfed infants. Nursing mothers may use the medication if clearly indicated.", "pregnancy": "Use only when strictly necessary and when alternative anti-inflammatory therapies are unsuitable, utilizing the lowest effective dose. Avoid use during the third trimester of pregnancy. Women planning to conceive should avoid use due to potential inhibition of blastocyst implantation."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Patients with a history of peptic ulcer disease, gastrointestinal bleeding, or perforation.", "Patients with renal impairment, hepatic impairment, or systemic lupus erythematosus.", "Patients with hypertension or heart disease associated with fluid retention or edema.", "Patients with a history of liver disease require regular monitoring of hepatic function during long-term treatment.", "Patients with active bacterial infections.", "Patients with a history of coagulation disorders or bleeding tendencies."], "adverseReactionManagement": "If adverse effects occur, discontinue use immediately, notify a physician, or visit the nearest medical facility for prompt management."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:45:52.563	diclofen-50mg-enteric-coated-tablets-for-pain-relief-and-musculoskeletal-inflammation-10-blisters-x	211
