 once daily.", "administration": "Administer via the oral route."}, "generalDescription": "Lorastad Stella 10mg is a second-generation H1-receptor antagonist used for the symptomatic relief of allergic conditions such as sneezing, nasal pruritus, rhinorrhea, ocular pruritus, lacrimation, and urticaria. It is significantly less sedating than first-generation antihistamines.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Lactose monohydrate, maize starch, talc, povidone K30, magnesium stearate, quinoline yellow lake.", "activeIngredients": "Loratadine 10mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "Because loratadine is excreted in breast milk and poses potential risks to neonates and premature infants, a decision should be made whether to discontinue nursing or discontinue the medication.", "pregnancy": "Should only be used during pregnancy if the potential therapeutic benefit outweighs the potential risk to the fetus."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Hepatic impairment.", "Risk of dry mouth, particularly in elderly patients, which increases the risk of dental caries; adequate oral hygiene is recommended."]}	f	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:50:12.698	lorastad-stella-10mg-tablets-for-allergic-rhinitis-urticaria-and-pruritus-10-blisters-x-10-tablets	39
