 "Concomitant use of angiotensin receptor blockers (ARBs) - including Diovan - or angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitors (ACEIs) with aliskiren in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus (see section Drug Interactions, Dual Blockade of the Renin-Angiotensin System [RAS]).", "Severe hepatic impairment, severe cirrhosis, biliary cirrhosis."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Novartis", "origin": "Switzerland", "storage": "Do not store above 30°C. Store in the original package.", "packaging": "Box of 2 blisters x 14 film-coated tablets", "manufacturer": "Novartis Pharmaceutica, S.A"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Adults:\\nHypertension: The recommended starting dose of Diovan is 80mg or 160mg film-coated tablets once daily. The daily dose may be increased up to 320mg or additional diuretics may be added. Diovan can be administered with other antihypertensive agents.\\nHeart Failure: The recommended starting dose of Diovan is 40mg film-coated tablets twice daily. Titrate upwards to 80mg and 160mg twice daily, as tolerated by the patient. Consideration should be given to reducing the dose of concomitant diuretics.\\nPost-Myocardial Infarction: Therapy may be initiated as early as 12 hours after a myocardial infarction. Following an initial dose of 20mg twice daily, valsartan therapy should be titrated to 40mg, 80mg, and 160mg film-coated tablets twice daily over the subsequent weeks. The maximum target dose is 160mg twice daily.\\nGeneral Guidance for All Indications: No initial dosage adjustment is required for patients with renal impairment or hepatic impairment of non-biliary and non-cholestatic origin.\\nPediatric Population: The safety and efficacy of Diovan in children and adolescents below 18 years of age have not been established.\\nRenal Impairment: No dosage adjustment is required for patients with a creatinine clearance >10 mL/min.\\nHepatic Impairment: The dose should not exceed 80mg in patients with mild to moderate hepatic impairment without cholestasis.", "administration": "Film-coated tablets: Diovan should be taken independently of meals and with water."}, "generalDescription": "Diovan 160mg tablets are indicated for the treatment of hypertension and heart failure, containing Valsartan as the active pharmaceutical ingredient. Each carton contains 2 blisters, with 14 tablets per blister. Diovan works by selectively blocking angiotensin II receptors, inducing vasodilation, reducing blood pressure, and supporting cardiac function, thereby alleviating the symptoms of hypertension and heart failure.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Microcrystalline cellulose, crospovidone, colloidal anhydrous silica, magnesium stearate, hypromellose, titanium dioxide (E171), macrogol 8000, red iron oxide (E172), yellow iron oxide (E172), black iron oxide (E172; present in 160mg strength only)", "activeIngredients": "Valsartan"}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Read the package leaflet carefully before use. Consult your physician for further information if needed.", "This medicinal product must be dispensed only under a medical prescription.", "Hyperkalemia: Concomitant use with potassium supplements, potassium-sparing diuretics, salt substitutes containing potassium, or other agents that may increase potassium levels (e.g., heparin) is not recommended. Appropriate monitoring of serum potassium levels should be undertaken.", "Sodium- and/or Volume-Depleted Patients: Symptomatic hypotension may occur after initiation of therapy with Diovan in patients who are severely sodium- and/or volume-depleted. Volume and/or sodium depletion should be corrected prior to administering Diovan. If hypotension occurs, the patient should be placed in the supine position and, if necessary, given an intravenous infusion of normal saline.", "Renal Artery Stenosis: Monitoring of blood urea nitrogen and serum creatinine is recommended as a safety measure.", "Renal Impairment: No dosage adjustment is required in patients with renal impairment. However, due to the lack of safety data in severe cases (creatinine clearance <10 mL/min), caution is advised. The combination of ARBs (including Diovan) or ACEIs with aliskiren should be avoided in patients with severe renal impairment (GFR <30 mL/min).", "Hepatic Impairment: No dosage adjustment is required in patients with hepatic impairment. Particular caution should be exercised when administering valsartan to patients with biliary obstruction.", "Heart Failure / Post-Myocardial Infarction: Administration of Diovan in patients with heart failure or post-myocardial infarction commonly results in some reduction in blood pressure, but discontinuation of therapy due to continuing symptomatic hypotension is generally not necessary provided dosage instructions are followed. Caution should be observed when initiating therapy in these patient populations. Triple combination therapy with an ACE inhibitor, a beta-blocker, and valsartan should be used with caution.", "Angioedema: Diovan must be discontinued immediately if angioedema develops, and the drug should not be re-administered.", "Dual Blockade of the Renin-Angiotensin System (RAS): Caution is required when co-administering ARBs (including Diovan) with other agents affecting the RAS, such as ACEIs or aliskiren.", "Effects on Ability to Drive and Use Machines: As with other antihypertensive medications, caution should be exercised when driving or operating machinery.", "Pregnancy and Lactation:\\nWomen of Childbearing Potential: As with any drug that acts directly on the renin-angiotensin-aldosterone system (RAAS), Diovan should not be used in women planning to become pregnant.\\nPregnancy: The use of drugs acting directly on the RAAS is contraindicated during pregnancy. If pregnancy is detected during therapy, Diovan must be discontinued as soon as possible.\\nBreastfeeding: It is unknown whether valsartan is excreted in human milk. Because valsartan is excreted in the milk of lactating rats, Diovan is not recommended for nursing mothers.\\nFertility: There is no information on the effects of valsartan on human fertility."]}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:15:27.248	diovan-160mg-film-coated-tablets-for-hypertension-and-heart-failure-box-of-2-blisters-x-14-tablets	120
