tration": "For topical application. For occlusive dressings: Cleanse and disinfect the skin, apply a small amount of cream and massage gently, then apply another layer of cream without massaging, and cover tightly with a plastic bandage.", "overdoseManagement": "Overdose may lead to severe adverse effects associated with corticosteroids and antibiotics. In the event of an overdose, discontinue medication use and contact a physician immediately for prompt medical management."}, "generalDescription": "Flucort N is a topical dermatological agent utilized for the management of inflammatory and allergic skin conditions associated with infection. The medication contains two active ingredients: Fluocinolone acetonide BP 0.025% and Neomycin Sulphate BP 0.5%, equivalent to 0.35% Neomycin base. Fluocinolone acetonide is a potent corticosteroid possessing anti-inflammatory and antipruritic properties, while Neomycin is an antibiotic that combats bacteria responsible for skin infections. Flucort N is specifically formulated for the management of severe dermatoses refractory to other corticosteroids. This product is particularly suitable for treating inflammatory skin conditions located in intertriginous areas or hair-bearing regions.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "White soft paraffin, liquid paraffin, cetomacrogol 1000, cetostearyl alcohol, propylene glycol, methylparaben, propylparaben, anhydrous sodium phosphate, sodium dihydrogen phosphate, purified water.", "activeIngredients": "Fluocinolone acetonide BP 0.025%, Neomycin Sulphate BP 0.5% (equivalent to 0.35% Neomycin base)"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "Adequate and well-controlled studies in nursing mothers are lacking; consult a physician prior to use.", "pregnancy": "Adequate and well-controlled studies in pregnant women are lacking; consult a physician prior to use."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["If Flucort-N is used in the presence of an infection, appropriate antibacterial therapy must be administered.", "Prolonged and continuous topical application of steroid medications may induce skin atrophy.", "Do not apply steroid medications to the facial area for extended periods.", "Long-term topical administration of steroids may result in systemic absorption sufficient to cause symptoms of adrenal suppression."]}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:17:54.531	flucort-n-fluocinolone-acetonide-0-025percent-w-w-and-neomycin-0-5percent-w-w-topical-ointment-for	258
