tly decreasing their gastrointestinal absorption."}], "effectsOnDriving": "This medicinal product has no or negligible influence on the ability to drive and operate machinery.", "pharmacodynamics": {"mechanismOfAction": "Calcium is a major macromineral essential for the maintenance of nervous, muscular, and skeletal systems, as well as vascular contraction, vasodilation, muscle contraction, and intracellular signaling. Vitamin D3 (cholecalciferol) enhances active intestinal absorption of calcium and phosphorus in the small intestine and promotes bone mineralization.", "pharmacologicalClass": "Mineral and Vitamin Supplement / Calcium and Vitamin D combination."}, "pharmacokinetics": {"absorption": "Calcium is absorbed primarily in the duodenum and proximal jejunum via active transport and passive diffusion mechanisms. Cholecalciferol (Vitamin D3) is well absorbed from the gastrointestinal tract, predominantly in the small intestine, in the presence of bile salts.", "metabolism": "Approximately 99% of total body calcium is stored in the bones and teeth, with the remaining 1% distributed in extracellular and intracellular fluids. Vitamin D3 undergoes hepatic hydroxylation to 25-hydroxycholecalciferol, followed by renal hydroxylation to the biologically active metabolite 1,25-dihydroxycholecalciferol (calcitriol).", "elimination": "Calcium is eliminated primarily through feces, with fractional excretion via urine, sweat, and breast milk. Vitamin D3 and its metabolites are excreted mainly via the biliary system into the feces, with minimal renal excretion."}, "contraindications": ["Known hypersensitivity to calcium carbonate, cholecalciferol, or any excipients in the formulation.", "Conditions associated with hypercalcemia and severe hypercalciuria.", "Nephrolithiasis, urolithiasis, or history of renal calcium calculi.", "Severe renal impairment or end-stage renal disease.", "Immobilization-induced osteoporosis leading to hypercalciuria and/or hypercalcemia.", "Concurrent pharmacological vitamin D therapy."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Hasan-Demarpharm", "origin": "Vietnam", "storage": "Store in a dry place, protected from moisture and light, at a temperature below 30°C.", "packaging": "Box of 3 blister packs x 10 tablets per blister", "manufacturer": "Hasan - Demarpharm Co., Ltd. (Vietnam)"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Adults and pediatric patients: 1 to 2 tablets daily. Pregnant and lactating women: Total daily intake should not exceed 400 IU of Vitamin D (approximately 3 tablets daily) unless specifically directed by a physician.", "administration": "Administer orally, preferably taken after meals or as prescribed by a qualified healthcare professional.", "overdoseManagement": "Clinical manifestations of acute or chronic hypervitaminosis D and hypercalcemia include anorexia, nausea, vomiting, constipation, polyuria, polydipsia, muscle weakness, lethargy, and cardiac arrhythmias. Management: Discontinue administration immediately. Institute rehydration with intravenous normal saline, administer loop diuretics if appropriate, monitor serum electrolytes and electrocardiogram (ECG), and consider corticosteroids or calcitonin in severe refractory hypercalcemia."}, "generalDescription": "Caldihasan is formulated as oral tablets containing calcium and vitamin D3, designed for the prophylaxis and treatment of deficiencies associated with insufficient dietary intake or increased physiological requirements of calcium and vitamin D.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Lactose monohydrate, Microcrystalline cellulose (Avicel M101), Sodium starch glycolate, Sodium saccharin, Povidone (Kollidon K30), Magnesium stearate.", "activeIngredients": "Calcium carbonate 1250mg (equivalent to 500mg of elemental calcium), Cholecalciferol (Vitamin D3) 3.125mcg (equivalent to 125 International Units)."}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "Cholecalciferol and its metabolites are excreted into breast milk. Maternal doses should not exceed recommended daily allowances unless specifically advised by a physician.", "pregnancy": "Recommended dietary allowances (RDA) for Vitamin D (400 IU/day) should not be exceeded. Use during pregnancy only when clearly indicated and when dietary calcium intake is insufficient."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Prolonged use or excessive dosage of calcium salts may result in hypercalcemia and secondary renal impairment.", "Exercise caution and evaluate medical history in patients with cardiac disease, atherosclerosis, renal impairment, nephrolithiasis, electrolyte imbalances, or achlorhydria.", "Regular monitoring of serum calcium levels and urinary calcium excretion is recommended during long-term therapy.", "Avoid concurrent administration of other vitamin D or calcium supplements without medical supervision to prevent toxicity."]}	f	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:28:08.27	caldihasan-tablets-calcium-carbonate-1250mg-cholecalciferol-125-iu-for-prevention-and-treatment-of	217
