k. If an infant develops diarrhea, breastfeeding should be discontinued.", "pediatric": "Not for use in children under 2 years of age. Children over 6 years should use weight-based dosing.", "pregnancy": "Use with caution and only if the benefits outweigh the risks. Mesalazine crosses the placental barrier. Pregnancy complications should be monitored."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Caution in patients with sulfasalazine allergy (risk of salicylate allergy), elderly patients.", "Discontinue the drug immediately if acute intolerance reactions occur (e.g., abdominal cramps, fever, severe headache, rash).", "Liver function (ALT, AST) and renal function (creatinine) should be monitored before and during treatment.", "Patients with lung diseases (especially bronchial asthma) should be carefully monitored.", "Regular blood tests are required to monitor for hematologic disorders.", "Caution is advised with concomitant use of nephrotoxic drugs or myelosuppressive agents."], "adverseReactionManagement": "If adverse effects occur, discontinue use and inform your doctor or go to the nearest medical facility for timely management."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:28:34.97	pentasa-500mg-controlled-release-tablets-mesalazine-for-ulcerative-colitis-and-crohn-s-disease-10	262
