: "Recommended treatment duration: 4 weeks for the scalp and 8 weeks for non-scalp areas. The maximum daily dose should not exceed 15 g, and the total treated body surface area should not exceed 30%. For scalp application, apply 1 g to 4 g per day (4 g is equivalent to one teaspoon).", "administration": "Apply the gel to the affected skin areas once daily."}, "generalDescription": "Xamiol Gel is a topical medication indicated for the treatment of plaque psoriasis, including scalp and non-scalp plaque psoriasis. The active pharmaceutical ingredients are calcipotriol and betamethasone.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Liquid paraffin, butylhydroxytoluene (E321), polyoxypropylene-15 stearyl ether (PPG-15 stearyl ether), all-rac-alpha-tocopherol, hydrogenated castor oil.", "activeIngredients": "Calcipotriol 50 mcg (as monohydrate), Betamethasone 0.5 mg (as dipropionate)"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "Use with caution during lactation.", "pediatric": "Pediatric patients under 18 years of age: Safety and efficacy have not been established.", "pregnancy": "Use with caution during pregnancy."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Do not use concurrently with other topical corticosteroids on the scalp.", "Avoid application to large areas of damaged skin, mucous membranes, or skin folds.", "Avoid excessive exposure to natural or artificial sunlight during treatment.", "Use with caution in pregnant and breastfeeding women.", "Monitor closely for signs of generalized pustular psoriasis and systemic corticosteroid adverse effects during long-term therapy."]}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:46:18.92	xamiol-50mcg-g-0-5mg-g-gel-for-plaque-psoriasis-15g-tube	244
1739	Panangin 140mg/158mg Tablets for Heart Failure, Post-Myocardial Infarction, and Cardiac Arrhythmia (Box of 50 Tablets)	P02651	\N	\N	Gedeon Richter Plc.	Hungary	171951.00	141000.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/ecommerce/20250520035418-0-P02651.png?versionId=0p8.wYDN4.O_zpNx3snowozlMtwFbTqh	Panangin 140mg/158mg is an oral mineral supplement containing magnesium and potassium aspartate, indicated for the treatment and prevention of magnesium and potassium deficiencies, and adjunctively in cardiovascular conditions such as heart failure, post-myocardial infarction, and cardiac arrhythmias.	{"indications": ["Indicated for the treatment and prevention of magnesium and potassium deficiencies in the body. Frequently prescribed for patients at risk of or suffering from cardiovascular disorders such as cardiac arrhythmias, myocardial infarction, and heart failure. This product helps improve cardiovascular function and maintains electrolyte balance."], "sideEffects": ["Higher doses may cause an increased frequency of bowel movements."], "drugInteractions": [{"drug": "Oral tetracyclines, iron salts, and sodium fluoride", "effect": "Inhibits the gastrointestinal absorption of Panangin. The administration interval between Panangin and these medications should be at least 3 hours."}, {"drug": "Potassium-sparing diuretics, angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitors (ACEIs), beta-blockers, cyclosporine, heparin, and non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs)", "effect": "May lead to hyperkalemia."}], "effectsOnDriving": "Panangin has no influence on the ability to drive and use machines.", "contraindications": ["Hypersensitivity to any of the active substances or excipients of the medication.", "Acute or chronic renal failure.", "Addison's disease (adrenocortical insufficiency).", "Third-degree atrioventricular block.", "Cardiogenic shock (blood pressure < 90 mmHg)."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Gedeon Richter", "origin": "Hungary", "storage": "Store at temperatures between 15°C and 30°C. Keep the medication out of the sight and reach of children.", "packaging": "Box of 50 tablets.", "manufacturer": "Gedeon Richter Plc."}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Unless otherwise prescribed by the physician, the usual dosage is 1-2 tablets 3 times daily. The dosage may be increased up to 3 tablets 3 times daily. Gastric acid can reduce the effectiveness of Panangin, so the tablets should be swallowed whole, unchewed, and taken after meals. If you have taken more medication than directed, stop the medication and consult a physician.", "missedDose": "Do not take a double dose to make up for a forgotten dose. Take the next dose at the usual scheduled time.", "administration": "For oral administration. Gastric acid can reduce the efficacy of Panangin; therefore, the tablets should be swallowed whole without chewing, preferably after meals.", "overdoseManagement": "Symptoms of overdose have not been reported even when administered at high doses. In case of overdose, serum potassium and magnesium concentrations may increase, potentially causing symptoms (diarrhea, generalized fatigue, paresthesia, bradycardia, paralysis, cardiac arrhythmias, nausea, vomiting, lethargy, hypotension, hyporeflexia). In the event of overdose, symptomatic treatment is recommended (intravenous (IV) calcium chloride solution at 100 mg/minute, hemodialysis if necessary)."}, "generalDescription": "Panangin Tablets is a medicinal mineral supplement containing magnesium and potassium, used for the treatment and prevention of magnesium and potassium deficiencies in the body. Panangin is commonly prescribed for individuals at risk of or experiencing cardiovascular problems such as arrhythmias, myocardial infarction, and heart failure. This product helps improve cardiovascular function and maintain electrolyte balance in the body.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Colloidal anhydrous silica, povidone, magnesium stearate, talc, maize starch, potato starch, macrogol 6000, titanium dioxide (E171), Eudragit E 100, talc.", "activeIngredients": "Each tablet contains 140 mg anhydrous magnesium aspartate (as 175 mg magnesium aspartate tetrahydrate) equivalent to 11.8 mg Mg2+ and 158 mg anhydrous potassium aspartate (as 166.3 mg potassium aspartate hemihydrate) equivalent to 36.2 mg K+."}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "[object Object]", "lactation": "There is insufficient information on the excretion of Panangin in human breast milk.", "pediatric": "[object Object]", "pregnancy": "There are no or limited amount of data from the use of Panangin in pregnant women."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["In conditions with a predisposition to hyperkalemia, the administration of this medication requires strict medical supervision."], "adverseReactionManagement": "Inform your physician or healthcare provider of any adverse reactions experienced while using the medication."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:51:12.677	panangin-140mg-158mg-tablets-for-heart-failure-post-myocardial-infarction-and-cardiac-arrhythmia	272
1744	Amlodipine 5mg Capsules for Hypertension and Angina Pectoris (3 Blisters x 10 Capsules)	P02276	\N	\N	Vietnam	Vietnam	22250.00	17800.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/ecommerce/20250728082901-0-P02276.png?versionId=40ESa1gR77cHICwy1UB6dd7lDXkJlkwc	Amlodipine 5mg capsules indicated for the management of hypertension and myocardial ischemia (angina pectoris), supplied in a package of 3 blisters x 10 capsules.	{"sideEffects": ["Dizziness", "Headache", "Fatigue", "Nausea", "Peripheral edema (swelling of ankles or feet)"], "drugInteractions": [{"drug": "Simvastatin", "effect": "Coadministration of multiple doses of 10 mg amlodipine with 80 mg simvastatin resulted in a 77% increase in exposure to simvastatin compared to simvastatin alone. Limit the dose of simvastatin to 20 mg daily in patients taking amlodipine."}, {"drug": "Grapefruit Juice", "effect": "Coadministration of 240 mL of grapefruit juice with a single oral dose of 10 mg amlodipine in 20 healthy volunteers had no significant effect on the pharmacokinetics of amlodipine. However, administration with grapefruit or grapefruit juice is not recommended as bioavailability may be increased in some patients, resulting in augmented blood pressure-lowering effects."}, {"drug": "CYP3A4 Inhibitors (e.g., diltiazem, erythromycin, ketoconazole, itraconazole, ritonavir)", "effect": "Coadministration of diltiazem with amlodipine in elderly hypertensive patients increased systemic exposure to amlodipine by 57%. Strong CYP3A4 inhibitors (such as ketoconazole, itraconazole, ritonavir) may increase plasma concentrations of amlodipine to a greater extent. Exercise caution when coadministering."}, {"drug": "Clarithromycin", "effect": "Increased risk of hypotension when clarithromycin is administered concomitantly with amlodipine. Close monitoring of patients is recommended."}, {"drug": "CYP3A4 Inducers (e.g., rifampicin, St. John's wort / Hypericum perforatum)", "effect": "Coadministration with CYP3A4 inducers may decrease plasma concentrations of amlodipine. Exercise caution and monitor clinical efficacy."}, {"drug": "Cimetidine", "effect": "Coadministration of amlodipine with cimetidine did not alter the pharmacokinetics of amlodipine."}, {"drug": "Aluminum/Magnesium Antacids", "effect": "Coadministration of aluminum and magnesium hydroxide antacids with a single dose of amlodipine had no significant effect on its pharmacokinetics."}, {"drug": "Sildenafil", "effect": "A single 100 mg dose of sildenafil in subjects with essential hypertension did not affect the pharmacokinetic parameters of amlodipine. Both agents independently exert their respective blood pressure-lowering effects."}, {"drug": "Atorvastatin", "effect": "Coadministration of multiple doses of 10 mg amlodipine with 80 mg atorvastatin resulted in no significant change in the steady-state pharmacokinetic parameters of atorvastatin."}, {"drug": "Digoxin", "effect": "Coadministration of amlodipine with digoxin did not change serum digoxin levels or digoxin renal clearance in healthy volunteers."}, {"drug": "Ethanol (Alcohol)", "effect": "Single or multiple 10 mg doses of amlodipine did not significantly affect the pharmacokinetics of ethanol."}, {"drug": "Warfarin", "effect": "Coadministration of amlodipine with warfarin did not change warfarin prothrombin response time."}, {"drug": "Cyclosporine", "effect": "Various studies in renal transplant patients indicate that coadministration of amlodipine with cyclosporine can affect trough concentrations of cyclosporine, ranging from no change to an average increase of 40%. Consider monitoring cyclosporine levels."}, {"drug": "Tacrolimus", "effect": "There is a risk of increased blood tacrolimus concentrations when coadministered with amlodipine. Monitor blood tacrolimus levels and adjust dosage accordingly."}, {"drug": "mTOR Inhibitors (Sirolimus, Temsirolimus, Everolimus)", "effect": "mTOR inhibitors are CYP3A substrates. Amlodipine is a weak CYP3A inhibitor and may increase exposure to mTOR inhibitors when coadministered."}], "effectsOnDriving": "Amlodipine may have a minor or moderate influence on the ability to drive and use machines. If patients taking amlodipine experience dizziness, headache, fatigue, or nausea, their ability to react may be impaired. Caution is recommended, especially at the start of treatment.", "pharmacokinetics": {"absorption": "After oral administration of therapeutic doses, absorption is well-documented with peak plasma concentrations reached between 6 and 12 hours post-dose.", "elimination": "Terminal plasma elimination half-life is about 35 to 50 hours and is consistent with once-daily dosing."}, "contraindications": ["Hypersensitivity to dihydropyridine derivatives, amlodipine, or any excipients of the medication.", "Severe hypotension.", "Shock, including cardiogenic shock.", "Obstruction of the left ventricular outflow tract (e.g., high-grade aortic stenosis).", "Hemodynamically unstable heart failure following acute myocardial infarction."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Domessco (Vietnam)", "origin": "Vietnam", "storage": "Store at temperatures between 15 - 30°C, protect from light.", "packaging": "Box of 3 blisters x 10 Capsules", "manufacturer": "Vietnam"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Starting dose: Typically 5 mg once daily. Maintenance dose: Can be increased up to 10 mg daily based on patient response and physician instruction.", "missedDose": "If a dose is missed, take it as soon as remembered. If it is almost time for the next dose, skip the missed dose and resume the normal dosing schedule. Do not double doses.", "administration": "Administer orally with a glass of water, at the same time each day.", "overdoseManagement": "Overdose may lead to excessive peripheral vasodilation and possibly reflex tachycardia. Severe and potentially prolonged systemic hypotension up to and including shock with fatal outcome has been reported. Active cardiovascular support should be instituted."}, "generalDescription": "Amlodipine 5mg is a long-acting calcium channel blocker (dihydropyridine class) that inhibits the transmembrane influx of calcium ions into vascular smooth muscle and cardiac muscle, resulting in peripheral arterial vasodilation and reduction in blood pressure.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Microcrystalline cellulose, anhydrous dibasic calcium phosphate, sodium starch glycolate, magnesium stearate", "activeIngredients": "Amlodipine besylate equivalent to 5 mg Amlodipine."}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "Use with caution; initial dose selection should be cautious, usually starting at the low end of the dosing range.", "lactation": "Data indicate that amlodipine passes into human breast milk. Estimated daily dose received by the infant is within safe limits, but caution is advised during lactation.", "pediatric": "Safety and efficacy in pediatric patients have not been established.", "pregnancy": "Safety of amlodipine in human pregnancy has not been established. Use during pregnancy only if the potential benefit outweighs the potential risk to the mother and fetus."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Heart Failure Patients: In a long-term, placebo-controlled study (PRAISE-2) of amlodipine in patients with NYHA class III-IV heart failure of non-ischemic etiology, amlodipine was associated with increased reports of pulmonary edema, though without significant difference in the incidence of worsening heart failure compared to placebo.", "Impaired Hepatic Function: Exposure and half-life of amlodipine are prolonged in patients with impaired liver function; dosage recommendations have not been established. Use with caution.", "Contains wheat starch; patients with wheat allergy (other than celiac disease) should not take this medication."], "adverseReactionManagement": "Manage mild adverse effects such as peripheral edema or dizziness by adjusting dosage or symptomatic care under medical supervision."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:51:29.771	amlodipine-5mg-capsules-for-hypertension-and-angina-pectoris-3-blisters-x-10-capsules	273
1749	Sentipec 50mg Sulpiride Capsules for Anxiety in Adults and Severe Behavioral Disorders in Children (5 Blisters x 10 Capsules)	P10868	\N	\N	\N	Vietnam	51316.00	39000.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/ecommerce/20250806051521-0-P10868.png?versionId=SH9sAw4zjtzgeTxYzAofIUnIR5zWDykh	Sentipec 50mg Capsules indicated for the short-term treatment of anxiety in adults unresponsive to standard therapies and severe behavioral disorders in children (5 blisters x 10 Capsules).	{"indications": ["Sentipec 50 is indicated for the following conditions:", "<p>Short-term treatment of anxiety symptoms in adults when standard treatments have failed. Treatment of severe behavioral disorders (such as agitation, self-mutilation, and stereotypic behaviors) in children over 14 years of age.</p>"], "pharmacodynamics": {"mechanismOfAction": "High doses of sulpiride control acute positive symptoms of schizophrenia, whereas low doses have an activating and alerting effect on withdrawn, apathetic schizophrenic patients.\\nSulpiride does not cause catalepsy, does not affect dopamine-sensitive adenylate cyclase, does not affect noradrenaline and 5-HT turnover, has virtually no anticholinergic activity, and does not affect muscarinic or GABA receptors.", "pharmacologicalClass": "Sulpiride belongs to the benzamide class, exerting antipsychotic effects by selectively blocking dopamine D2 receptors in the brain. Sulpiride is considered an intermediate medication between typical antipsychotics and antidepressants."}, "pharmacokinetics": {"absorption": "Sulpiride is slowly absorbed through the gastrointestinal tract; its bioavailability is low and subject to individual variability. Peak plasma concentrations are reached 3 to 6 hours after a single oral dose.", "metabolism": "95% of the sulpiride dose is excreted unmetabolized.", "elimination": "The drug is eliminated via urine and feces, primarily in unchanged form (approximately 95%). The elimination half-life is approximately 8 to 9 hours."}, "manufacturingInfo": {"storage": "Store in a dry place, below 30°C, protected from light."}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "<em>Adults:</em>\\nAnxiety symptoms in adults: 50 - 150 mg/day, used for a maximum of 4 weeks.\\n<em>Children:</em>\\nSevere behavioral disorders in children.\\n<em>Children &gt; 14 years old:</em>\\nOral administration of 3-5 mg/kg/day.\\n<em>Children &lt; 14 years old:</em>\\nNot indicated.\\n<em>Elderly:</em>\\nDosage should be reduced similarly to adult dosing, but starting with a low initial dose and gradually increasing: Initial dose of 50-100 mg twice daily, then titrated up to the effective dose.\\n<em>Renal impairment:</em>\\nReduce the dose or increase the dosing interval depending on creatinine clearance.\\n<em>Creatinine clearance:</em>\\n30 - 60 ml/min: Administer 2/3 of the normal dose.\\n10 - 30 ml/min: Administer 1/2 of the normal dose.\\n&lt; 10 ml/min: Administer 1/3 of the normal dose.\\nAlternatively, increase the dosing interval to 1.5, 2, and 3 times compared to normal subjects.\\nSulpiride should be avoided in moderate and severe renal impairment.\\nNote: The above dosages are for reference only. The specific dosage depends on the patient's physical condition and the progression of the disease. To obtain an appropriate dosage, please consult a physician or healthcare professional.", "missedDose": "If you miss a dose, take it as soon as you remember. However, if it is almost time for your next dose, skip the missed dose and resume your regular dosing schedule. Do not double the dose.", "administration": "For oral administration.", "overdoseManagement": "Overdose: Commonly reported with doses of 1 to 16 grams, with no fatalities reported even at the 16-gram dose.\\nClinical symptoms vary depending on the dose. Doses of 1 - 3 grams can cause lethargy, agitation, and rarely extrapyramidal symptoms. Doses of 3 - 7 grams may cause agitation, confusion, and more pronounced extrapyramidal symptoms. With doses exceeding 7 grams, coma and hypotension may occur in addition to the aforementioned symptoms.\\nIn general, symptoms usually resolve within a few hours. Coma occurring from high doses may last up to 4 days.\\nManagement: There is no specific antidote for sulpiride. Therefore, if the medication was recently ingested, perform gastric lavage, administer activated charcoal (emetics are ineffective), and alkalinize the urine to enhance drug excretion. If necessary, antiparkinsonian agents can be administered, along with supportive and symptomatic treatment measures."}, "generalDescription": "Sentipec 50 is indicated for the following conditions: Short-term treatment of anxiety symptoms in adults when standard treatments have failed. Treatment of severe behavioral disorders (such as agitation, self-mutilation, and stereotypic behaviors) in children over 14 years of age.", "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Sulpiride 50mg"}}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:51:46.919	sentipec-50mg-sulpiride-capsules-for-anxiety-in-adults-and-severe-behavioral-disorders-in-children	\N
