ife is prolonged."}, "contraindications": ["Pediatric patients under 18 years of age."], "manufacturingInfo": {"storage": "Store below 30°C in a dry place, protected from light and moisture."}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Recommended dosage for adults with normal renal function (creatinine clearance > 50 mL/min): Community-acquired pneumonia (500 mg once or twice daily for 7°14 days); Complicated urinary tract infections (250 mg once daily for 7°10 days); Chronic bacterial prostatitis (500 mg once daily for 28 days); Skin and soft tissue infections (250 mg once daily or 500 mg once or twice daily for 7°14 days); Uncomplicated urinary tract infections (250 mg once daily for 3 days); Acute sinusitis (500 mg once daily for 10°14 days); Acute bacterial exacerbation of chronic bronchitis (250 to 500 mg once daily for 7°10 days).", "missedDose": "Take the missed dose as soon as remembered. If it is almost time for the next scheduled dose, skip the missed dose and resume the regular dosing schedule. Do not double the dose to make up for a forgotten dose.", "administration": "For oral administration. Tablets should be swallowed whole without crushing, with an adequate amount of water. The tablet may be divided along the break score line for dose titration. Administration may occur with or without food. Take at least 2 hours before or after iron preparations, antacids, and sucralfate.", "overdoseManagement": "Symptoms: Confusion, tinnitus, altered consciousness, seizures, QT interval prolongation, nausea. Management: Symptomatic treatment, electrocardiogram (ECG) monitoring, and administration of antacids to protect the gastric mucosa. There is no specific antidote. Hemodialysis is not effective in removing the drug from the body."}, "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Levofloxacin 250mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "No dosage adjustment is necessary based on age alone; however, renal function should be carefully monitored.", "pediatric": "Contraindicated in pediatric patients under 18 years of age."}}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:40:08.913	nirdicin-250mg-levofloxacin-film-coated-tablets-for-bacterial-infections-box-of-10-tablets	\N
