inister via intramuscular or intravenous route. For intramuscular injection, administer deeply into the muscle. For intravenous injection, administer slowly while the patient is in a supine position.", "overdoseManagement": "Symptoms: Ataxia, dizziness, convulsions, respiratory depression, sinus tachycardia, prolonged Q-T interval. Management: Treatment of seizures with diazepam, administration of physostigmine for severe anticholinergic symptoms, fluid resuscitation or vasopressors for hypotension, and respiratory support."}, "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Diphenhydramine 10mg/ml"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "25 mg per dose, 2 to 3 times daily, titrated upward if necessary."}}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:41:35.418	dimedrol-hd-10mg-1ml-solution-for-injection-for-allergic-conditions-nausea-and-dystonic-reactions	\N
