eralDescription": "Crestor 10mg contains rosuvastatin calcium, a selective and competitive HMG-CoA reductase inhibitor used as an adjunct to diet for the treatment of primary hypercholesterolemia and mixed dyslipidemia, as well as for the prevention of cardiovascular disease.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Lactose monohydrate, microcrystalline cellulose, calcium phosphate, crospovidone, magnesium stearate, hypromellose, glycerol triacetate, titanium dioxide (E171), red iron oxide (E172).", "activeIngredients": "Each film-coated tablet contains rosuvastatin calcium equivalent to 10mg of rosuvastatin base."}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "A starting dose of 5mg once daily is recommended in patients over 70 years of age.", "lactation": "Contraindicated during lactation. It is unknown whether rosuvastatin is excreted in human milk.", "pediatric": "Safety and efficacy in pediatric patients below 8 years of age have not been established.", "pregnancy": "Contraindicated during pregnancy. Cholesterol and other products of cholesterol biosynthesis are essential components for fetal development."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Renal effects: Proteinuria, mostly tubular in origin, has been observed in patients treated with higher doses (particularly 40mg).", "Skeletal muscle effects: Cases of myalgia, myopathy, and rarely rhabdomyolysis have been reported in patients treated with rosuvastatin, especially at doses of 20mg and 40mg.", "Liver enzyme abnormalities: Periodic liver function testing is recommended; use with caution in patients who consume substantial quantities of alcohol or have a history of chronic liver disease.", "Ethnicity: Higher plasma concentrations of rosuvastatin have been demonstrated in Asian subjects, warranting a lower starting dose.", "Lactose intolerance: Patients with rare hereditary problems of galactose intolerance, total lactase deficiency, or glucose-galactose malabsorption should not take this medicine.", "Interstitial lung dis