owing steady-state dosing."}, "manufacturingInfo": {"origin": "India", "storage": "Store at a temperature below 30°C. Protect from light and moisture.", "packaging": "Carton containing 10 blister packs of 10 tablets each (100 tablets total).", "manufacturer": "TORRENT PHARMACEUTICALS LTD."}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Adults: Initial dosage of 12.5 mg to 25 mg once or twice on the first day, followed by gradual titration with increments of 25 mg to 50 mg per day, as tolerated, to achieve a target dose of 300 mg/day within 14 days. Subsequent dosage adjustments may be made in increments of 50 mg to 100 mg once or twice weekly. The usual therapeutic range is 200 mg to 450 mg/day. The maximum daily dose is 900 mg.", "administration": "Administered orally. May be taken with or without food.", "overdoseManagement": "Symptoms: Manifestations of acute overdosage include drowsiness, lethargy, areflexia, coma, confusion, hallucinations, agitation, delirium, convulsive seizures, hypersalivation, mydriasis, blurred vision, thermoregulatory instability, tachycardia, cardiac arrhythmias, hypotension, respiratory depression, and aspiration pneumonia. Management: Establish and maintain a patent airway and ensure adequate oxygenation. Administer activated charcoal, which may be as or more effective than gastric lavage, if given within 1 to 2 hours of ingestion. Employ general supportive measures with continuous electrocardiographic (ECG) and vital signs monitoring. Avoid the use of epinephrine or derivatives for hypotension due to the potential for reverse alpha-adrenergic blockade."}, "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Clozapine 25 mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"pediatric": "Safety and efficacy in pediatric patients under 18 years of age have not been established; use in children is not recommended."}}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:21:59.456	clozapyl-clozapine-25mg-tablets-for-schizophrenia-10-blister-packs-x-10-tablets	301
