s the hepatic metabolism and clearance of methylprednisolone, potentially requiring dosage adjustment."}, {"drug": "Phenytoin, phenobarbital, rifampin, and potassium-depleting diuretics", "effect": "Inducers of hepatic enzymes may reduce the clinical efficacy of methylprednisolone; potassium-depleting agents increase the risk of severe hypokalemia."}, {"drug": "Insulin or oral antidiabetic agents", "effect": "Methylprednisolone induces hyperglycemia, necessitating dosage titration and increased monitoring of antidiabetic therapy."}], "contraindications": ["Systemic fungal infections, unless specific anti-infective therapy is concurrently administered.", "Known hypersensitivity to methylprednisolone or any component of the formulation.", "Active or untreated latent tuberculosis, and viral or fungal skin lesions.", "Administration of live or live-attenuated virus vaccines in patients receiving immunosuppressive corticosteroid doses."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "SPM", "origin": "Vietnam", "storage": "Store in a dry, tightly closed container, protected from direct light, at temperatures not exceeding 30°C.", "packaging": "Blister of 10 tablets, box of 3 blisters, box of 10 blisters, box of 30 blisters; High-density polyethylene (HDPE) bottle of 500 tablets, bottle of 1000 tablets.", "manufacturer": "SPM Pharmaceutical Joint Stock Company (Vietnam)"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Dosage must be individualized based on the specific disease entity, severity, and patient response. Initial therapeutic dosage range: 4mg to 48mg of methylprednisolone daily, administered for 3 to 5 days. Subsequent maintenance dosage should be titrated down to the lowest effective level (typically 4mg to 32mg daily). Alternate-day therapy (administering a double daily dose every other morning) may be employed for long-term maintenance to minimize hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis suppression. (Specific clinical indications such as bronchial asthma, rheumatoid arthritis, ulcerative c