alene is excreted in human milk. Exercise caution when administering to nursing mothers.", "pediatric": "The safety and efficacy of Adapalene in children under 12 years of age have not been established.", "pregnancy": "Do not use adapalene during pregnancy unless the potential benefit outweighs the potential risk to the fetus."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Klenzit MS medication is for topical external use only.", "Certain skin signs and symptoms such as erythema, dry skin, scaling, burning, or pruritus may occur during treatment.", "Avoid contact with the eyes, lips, corners of the nose, and mucous membranes.", "Avoid exposure to strong sunlight, including sunlamps. Appropriate sun protection products are recommended when going outdoors.", "Avoid concurrent use with topical preparations that may cause skin dryness or irritation, such as medicated soaps, cleansers, harsh drying soaps and cosmetics, high-concentration alcohol preparations, astringents, fragrances, or alkalis, as local irritation may occur.", "Do not apply medication to cuts, abrasions, eczematous skin, or sunburned areas.", "Avoid skin exposure to ultraviolet rays while using the medication."], "adverseReactionManagement": "If adverse reactions occur, discontinue use and notify a physician or visit the nearest medical facility for timely management."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:51:22.392	klenzit-topical-gel-adapalen-0-1percent-clindamycin-15g-tube-for-acne-vulgaris	22
