ion of therapeutic efficacy."}, {"drug": "Coumarin derivatives", "effect": "Reduction of anticoagulant efficacy."}, {"drug": "Carbenoxolone", "effect": "Attenuation of pharmacological efficacy."}, {"drug": "Neomycin", "effect": "Impaired gastrointestinal absorption of spironolactone."}, {"drug": "Triptorelin, buserelin, gonadorelin", "effect": "Potentiation of pharmacological effects."}], "contraindications": ["Pregnancy", "Lactation"], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Verospiron", "storage": "Store below 30°C (86°F).", "packaging": "Box of 1 blister pack x 20 tablets. Physical description: Round, flat, nearly white tablets possessing a characteristic sulfur-like odor.", "manufacturer": "Gedeon Richter"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Primary hyperaldosteronism: 100 - 400 mg daily prior to surgery; Edema: Adults 100 mg daily administered in 2 divided doses (may range from 25 to 200 mg daily), Pediatric patients 3.0 mg/kg daily; Hypertension: 50 - 100 mg daily; Hypokalemia: 25 - 100 mg daily.", "overdoseManagement": "Symptoms: Somnolence, mental confusion, and electrolyte laboratory abnormalities. Management: Discontinue drug administration, institute supportive and symptomatic care, maintain fluid-electrolyte and acid-base balance, and perform hemodialysis if clinically indicated."}, "generalDescription": "Verospiron 25mg is manufactured by Gedeon Richter Plc., containing spironolactone 25 mg as the primary active pharmaceutical ingredient.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Colloidal silicon dioxide, magnesium stearate, talc, starch, lactose", "activeIngredients": "Spironolactone 25mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "Regular surveillance of serum electrolytes and renal function parameters is required.", "lactation": "Contraindicated during lactation.", "pregnancy": "Contraindicated during pregnancy."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Renal impairment and hyperkalemia: Close monitoring of serum electrolytes and renal function is mandatory.", "Hepatic dy