a suggesting that the drug impairs the ability to drive or operate machinery.", "contraindications": ["Known hypersensitivity to chymotrypsin or any excipients contained in the formulation.", "Contraindicated in patients with congenital or acquired alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency. Clinical note: Patients with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD), particularly those with pulmonary emphysema, and patients with nephrotic syndrome are at an elevated risk of alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Sanofi", "origin": "Vietnam", "storage": "Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C (86°F), protect from excessive moisture and direct light.", "packaging": "Box of 2 blister packs x 15 tablets.", "manufacturer": "Sanofi Synthelabo Pharmaceutical Joint Stock Company (Vietnam)"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Oral administration: 2 tablets per dose, administered 3 to 4 times daily. It is recommended to ingest with an adequate volume of water (at least 8 oz or 240 mL) to optimize enzymatic activity. Sublingual administration: 4 to 6 tablets daily, divided into multiple doses. Allow the tablets to dissolve slowly beneath the tongue.", "administration": "Administer orally or via sublingual route."}, "generalDescription": "Alpha Choay 4200 IU is an anti-inflammatory and anti-edematous proteolytic enzyme medication. It is primarily indicated for the reduction of soft tissue swelling, edema, and inflammation associated with trauma, surgical interventions, or secondary causes.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Menthol essential oil, magnesium stearate, wheat starch, sucrose", "activeIngredients": "Chymotrypsin or alphachymotrypsin 21°katals (equivalent to 25 C.Hb units per tablet)"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "Chymotrypsin is contraindicated during lactation and breastfeeding.", "pregnancy": "Chymotrypsin is contraindicated during pregnancy."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Chymotrypsin exhibits a favorable safety profile and is generally well-tolerated with minimal significant adverse effects.", "Patient populations who should avoid enzyme therapy include: individuals with hereditary coagulation disorders (such as hemophilia), active bleeding disorders, patients receiving anticoagulant therapy, patients scheduled for surgical procedures, individuals with known protein hypersensitivity, pregnant or nursing women, and patients with active peptic ulcer disease."]}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:25:55.256	alpha-choay-alphachymotrypsin-4200-iu-tablets-for-post-traumatic-post-surgical-and-burn-edema-box	85
