lock, overt cardiac failure or cardiogenic shock.", "Severe allergic rhinitis and bronchial hyperresponsiveness, hypersensitivity to other beta-blockers.", "Severe renal impairment.", "Hyperchloremic acidosis."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Alcon", "origin": "Belgium", "storage": "Store at a temperature below 30°C (86°F).", "packaging": "Box of 1 bottle of 5ml", "manufacturer": "Alcon"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Instill 1 drop into the conjunctival sac of the affected eye, twice daily.", "missedDose": "Continue with the next dose as directed. Do not instill more than one drop at a time, twice daily.", "administration": "For ophthalmic use only. Shake the bottle well before use. Avoid allowing the dropper tip to touch the eye or any other surface. After instillation, compress the nasolacrimal duct or close the eyes to reduce systemic absorption. If using multiple eye drops, administer at least 5 minutes apart.", "overdoseManagement": "Symptoms of beta-blocker overdose: bradycardia, hypotension, heart failure, bronchospasm. Symptoms due to brinzolamide: electrolyte imbalance, metabolic acidosis, neurological effects. Management: Supportive treatment, rinse eyes with warm water, symptomatic treatment."}, "generalDescription": "Azarga eye drops manufactured by Alcon contain the main active ingredients Brinzolamide and timolol, used to reduce intraocular pressure in patients with ocular hypertension or open-angle glaucoma. Azarga eye drops are formulated as a sterile, homogeneous white to off-white suspension.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Benzalkonium chloride, Disodium edetate, sodium chloride, tyloxapol, mannitol, carbomer 974P, sodium hydroxide and/or hydrochloric acid, purified water.", "activeIngredients": "Brinzolamide 10 mg/ml and Timolol maleate 6.8 mg/ml (equivalent to Timolol 5 mg/ml)."}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "No difference in safety and efficacy compared to other adults.", "lactation": "Beta-blockers are excreted into b