1188	Betadine (Povidone-Iodine 10%) Topical Ointment for Skin Disinfection and Treatment of Infected Lesions (Tube of 40g)	P11026	\N	\N	Mundipharma	Vietnam	83125.00	66500.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/ecommerce/20250729065646-0-P11026.png?versionId=MWZxKdlbiNxh0gShRt2ToAbLbLsm3CSg	Betadine (Povidone-Iodine 10%) is a topical antiseptic ointment indicated for skin disinfection, antisepsis of compromised skin, and the treatment of infected skin lesions, superficial wounds, and burns.	{"indications": ["Indicated for use as an antiseptic for repeated application, for a limited duration, on compromised skin such as decubitus ulcers (pressure injuries), chronic venous leg ulcers, superficial wounds, burns, and infected or superinfected dermatoses."], "pharmacodynamics": {"mechanismOfAction": "Free iodine acts as a potent microbicide, while the iodine bound within the povidone complex serves as a sustained-release reservoir. Upon contact with the skin and mucous membranes, iodine is progressively dissociated from the complex. Free iodine rapidly oxidizes and reacts with the -SH (sulfhydryl) and -OH (hydroxyl) groups of amino acids in microbial enzymes and structural proteins, leading to their inactivation and destruction.,During this oxidation process, active iodine is consumed and loses its characteristic brown color. Consequently, the persistence of the brown color serves as an indicator ofertal antimicrobial efficacy of the preparation. Reapplication may be warranted when the brown coloration fades."}, "pharmacokinetics": {"absorption": "Topical application to intact skin results in minimal systemic absorption of iodine. Absorption may increase when applied to extensive denuded skin, large surface wounds, or severe burns.", "elimination": "Systemically absorbed iodine is eliminated predominantly via renal excretion, with a renal clearance ranging from 15 to 60 mL/min depending on serum iodine concentration and creatinine clearance. Povidone (polyvinylpyrrolidone) fractions with a molecular weight of 35,000 to 50,000 are excreted renally, while higher molecular weight fractions may potentially accumulate in the reticuloendothelial system."}, "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Betadine", "storage": "Store below 30°C (86°F). Protect from excessive heat and direct sunlight.", "packaging": "Collapsible aluminum or plastic tube containing 40g of topical ointment.", "manufacturer": "Mundipharma"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Apply 1 to 2 times daily for a maximum duration of 14 days. The treated area may be covered with a dressing or bandage if clinically indicated. If clinical symptoms do not improve or if signs of infection persist after 2 to 5 days of regular use, consult a healthcare professional.", "missedDose": "For topical agents, if a dose is missed, apply the ointment as soon as remembered, then resume the regular application schedule.", "administration": "Topical administration. Apply Betadine 10% ointment evenly to the affected skin area after thoroughly cleaning and drying the lesion.", "overdoseManagement": "[object Object]"}, "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Povidone-Iodine 10% w/w"}}	f	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:26:08.596	betadine-povidone-iodine-10percent-topical-ointment-for-skin-disinfection-and-treatment-of-infected	319
