, potentially causing mild or symptomatic hypotension."}], "effectsOnDriving": "Clinical studies on the effects of tadalafil on the ability to drive and operate machinery have not been conducted. Although the incidence of dizziness reported with placebo and tadalafil in clinical trials was comparable, patients should evaluate their individual response to the medication prior to driving or operating machinery.", "contraindications": ["Co-administration with organic nitrates or nitric oxide donors, whether continuously or intermittently.", "Known hypersensitivity to tadalafil or any of the excipients contained in the formulation."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Stella", "origin": "In accordance with manufacturer specifications", "storage": "Store at temperatures below 30°C in a dry place, protected from light. Keep out of reach of children.", "packaging": "Carton containing 1 blister pack x 2 tablets"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Tadalafil Stella 10mg is taken orally once daily, regardless of meals. The standard initial dose is 10mg taken at least 30 minutes prior to anticipated sexual activity. The dose may be increased to 20mg or decreased to 5mg based on individual efficacy and tolerability. The pharmacological effect of tadalafil may persist for up to 36 hours post-dose. The maximum recommended dosing frequency is once daily; continuous daily dosing is not recommended due to the lack of long-term safety data. No dosage adjustment is necessary for elderly patients. For patients with mild to moderate hepatic impairment, the maximum dose should not exceed 10mg once daily; tadalafil is contraindicated in severe hepatic impairment. For patients with moderate renal impairment (creatinine clearance 31°50 mL/min), a starting dose of 5mg not more than once daily is recommended, with a maximum dose not exceeding 10mg once every 48 hours. In severe renal impairment (creatinine clearance < 30 mL/min), including patients undergoing hemodialysis, the maximum dose is 5mg once daily. For patients stabilized on alpha-blocker therapy, the recommended starting dose is 5mg. For patients receiving potent CYP3A4 inhibitors, the maximum recommended dose is 10mg once every 72 hours. Note: Dosing regimens provided are for reference only. Individualized dosing depends on clinical status and pathology. Consult a qualified physician or healthcare provider.", "missedDose": "Administer the missed dose as soon as remembered. Refer to the dosage guidelines for further instructions.", "administration": "Tadalafil Stella 10mg is administered via the oral route.", "overdoseManagement": "Single doses up to 500mg administered to healthy subjects and multiple daily doses up to 100mg administered to patients resulted in adverse reactions similar to those observed at lower therapeutic doses. In the event of overdose, standard supportive medical measures should be implemented as clinically indicated. Hemodialysis contributes negligibly to the elimination of tadalafil."}, "generalDescription": "Tadalafil Stella is a phosphodiesterase type 5 (PDE5) inhibitor containing tadalafil as the active pharmaceutical ingredient. It is primarily indicated for the treatment of erectile dysfunction in men by enhancing blood flow to the corpus cavernosum during sexual stimulation, thereby facilitating and improving erectile function.", "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Tadalafil 10mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "No dosage adjustments are required for elderly patients.", "lactation": "Tadalafil is not indicated for use in female patients.", "pediatric": "The safety and efficacy of tadalafil in pediatric patients under 18 years of age have not been established; administration in children and infants is strictly contraindicated.", "pregnancy": "Tadalafil is not indicated for use in female patients."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Cardiovascular system: Sexual activity carries inherent cardiovascular risks. Therefore, a patient's cardiovascular status should be thoroughly evaluated prior to initiating tadalafil therapy.", "Serious cardiovascular adverse events associated with tadalafil include myocardial infarction, sudden cardiac death, stroke, chest pain, palpitations, and tachycardia. Tadalafil must not be used in men with cardiac conditions for whom sexual intercourse is inadvisable.", "Particular caution should be exercised regarding the potential for systemic vasodilation and hypotension in patients with left ventricular outflow obstruction (e.g., aortic stenosis, idiopathic hypertrophic subaortic stenosis) or severely impaired autonomic blood pressure regulation.", "Ophthalmology: Tadalafil should not be administered to patients with hereditary degenerative retinal disorders, including retinitis pigmentosa.", "Genitourinary system: Administer with caution in patients with anatomical penile deformation (such as angulation, cavernosal fibrosis, or Peyronie's disease) or conditions predisposing to priapism (such as sickle cell anemia, multiple myeloma, or leukemia).", "Tadalafil should not be co-administered with other therapies for erectile dysfunction, as the safety and efficacy of such combination regimens have not been established in clinical trials."], "adverseReactionManagement": "If any adverse drug reactions manifest, discontinue treatment immediately and consult a physician or seek medical attention at the nearest healthcare facility for prompt management."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:14:35.362	tadalafil-10mg-stella-tablets-for-erectile-dysfunction-1-blister-x-2-tablets	39
