45	Allopurinol 300mg Tablets for Chronic Gout and Urolithiasis (Bottle of 100 Tablets)	P02757	\N	\N	Domesco	Vietnam	139881.00	117500.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/ecommerce/P02757_1.jpg	Allopurinol 300mg Domesco tablets indicated for chronic gout and kidney stones (Bottle of 100 tablets).	{"indications": ["This medication is primarily indicated for the treatment of chronic gout and urolithiasis (kidney stones). Gout occurs when the body accumulates excessive uric acid in the blood, leading to the formation of urate crystals in the joints, causing pain and inflammation. Allopurinol acts by reducing uric acid production in the body, helping to prevent acute gout flares and kidney stone formation. This drug is also used to treat other medical conditions associated with elevated uric acid deposition, such as in patients undergoing cancer treatment via chemotherapy or radiation therapy."], "sideEffects": ["Nausea, diarrhea, skin rash accompanied by low-grade fever.", "Elevated alkaline phosphatase, increased SGOT/SGPT.", "Acute gout exacerbations with vesicular eruptions."], "drugInteractions": [{"drug": "Amoxicillin/Ampicillin", "effect": "Increased incidence of skin rashes."}, {"drug": "Chlorpropamide", "effect": "Risk of secondary hypoglycemia in patients with renal impairment."}, {"drug": "6-Mercaptopurine and Azathioprine", "effect": "Prolongation of pharmacological activity."}, {"drug": "Vidarabine", "effect": "Increased half-life."}, {"drug": "Salicylates and Uricosuric agents", "effect": "Accelerated excretion of Allopurinol."}, {"drug": "Chlorpropamide", "effect": "Increased risk of prolonged hypoglycemic activity."}, {"drug": "Coumarin anticoagulants", "effect": "Potentiation of anticoagulant activity."}, {"drug": "Phenytoin", "effect": "Inhibition of hepatic oxidation."}, {"drug": "Theophylline", "effect": "Inhibition of metabolism."}, {"drug": "Ampicillin/Amoxicillin", "effect": "Increased frequency of cutaneous rashes."}, {"drug": "Cyclophosphamide, Doxorubicin, Bleomycin, Procarbazine, Mechlorethamine", "effect": "Exacerbation of bone marrow suppression."}, {"drug": "Ciclosporin", "effect": "Elevated plasma concentrations."}], "effectsOnDriving": "This medication may cause somnolence, loss of balance, dizziness, and ataxia. Patients should avoid driving or operating machinery while taking this drug.", "contraindications": ["Pregnancy and lactation.", "Known hypersensitivity to Allopurinol.", "Concomitant administration with xanturic agents.", "During an acute gout attack."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Domesco.", "origin": "Vietnam", "storage": "Store below 30°C, protect from direct light.", "packaging": "Bottle of 100 tablets.", "manufacturer": "Domesco"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Gout, hyperuricemia: Adults: 100 mg daily, may be gradually increased to 200°400 mg daily, divided into 2°4 doses. Severe cases may require 600°800 mg daily.\\nNeoplastic conditions: 600°800 mg daily, in courses of 2°3 days.\\nPsoriasis: 100°400 mg daily, divided into 3°4 doses.\\nPediatric patients aged 6°15 years: 100 mg per dose, 3 times daily.\\nPediatric patients under 6 years: 50 mg per dose, 3 times daily, or 8 mg/kg/day, divided into 3 doses.\\nRenal impairment: 100 mg daily; dose should be increased only if therapeutic response is inadequate. Doses lower than 100 mg daily or 100 mg administered at intervals greater than 1 day for patients with severe renal failure. For hemodialysis patients, the recommended dose is 300°400 mg immediately following dialysis.", "administration": "Administer orally after meals.", "overdoseManagement": "In the event of an overdose, discontinue medication use and contact a physician immediately. Management measures may include symptomatic treatment and supportive care for vital organ functions."}, "generalDescription": "Allopurinol 300mg is a medication primarily used to manage chronic gout and nephrolithiasis. Gout is characterized by hyperuricemia resulting in the precipitation of urate crystals within joint spaces, precipitating acute inflammatory arthritis. Allopurinol functions as a xanthine oxidase inhibitor, decreasing endogenous uric acid biosynthesis to mitigate recurrent gout attacks and uric acid nephropathy. It is also indicated for hyperuricemia secondary to oncologic conditions, including chemotherapy or radiation therapy.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Lactose, Starch 1500, Povidone, Sunset Yellow lake, Croscarmellose sodium, Aerosil, q.s. one tablet.", "activeIngredients": "Allopurinol 300mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "Pregnant and lactating women should not use Allopurinol unless strictly necessary and explicitly directed by a physician.", "pregnancy": "Pregnant and lactating women should not use Allopurinol unless strictly necessary and explicitly directed by a physician."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Discontinue use and notify a physician immediately if signs of skin rash, dysuria, hematuria, ocular irritation, or swelling of the lips or mouth occur."]}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:15:53.073	allopurinol-300mg-tablets-for-chronic-gout-and-urolithiasis-bottle-of-100-tablets	61
