 to plasma proteins approximately 95%.", "elimination": "Simvastatin is eliminated primarily via the biliary route into feces as metabolites. Approximately 10% to 15% is recovered in the urine, primarily in inactive forms. The plasma elimination half-life of the beta-hydroxyacid metabolite is 1.9 hours."}, "manufacturingInfo": {"storage": "Store in a dry place, protect from light, and store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C."}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "The usual dosage range is 5 to 80 mg administered orally once daily in the evening. The 80 mg dosage is restricted to patients with severe hypercholesterolemia and high risk for cardiovascular complications who have not achieved their treatment goals on lower doses.", "missedDose": "If a dose is missed, take it as soon as possible. However, if it is almost time for the next scheduled dose, skip the missed dose and resume the regular dosing schedule. Do not double the dose to make up for a forgotten dose.", "administration": "Administered orally, usually as a single dose in the evening.", "overdoseManagement": "Symptoms: A few cases of overdosage have been reported; the maximum dose ingested was 3.6 g. All patients recovered without sequelae. Management: There is no specific antidote; symptomatic and supportive measures should be instituted."}, "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Simvastatin 10 mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "No dosage adjustment is necessary for elderly patients.", "pediatric": "For children and adolescents (10°17 years of age) with heterozygous familial hypercholesterolemia, the recommended usual starting dose is 10 mg once daily in the evening, with a maximum recommended dose of 40 mg daily."}}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:40:21.989	simvastatin-stella-10mg-tablets-for-hyperlipidemia-and-cardiovascular-risk-reduction-box-of-100	\N
