tion (hemoglobin, myoglobin).", "pharmacologicalClass": "Iron (III) preparations, oral solutions."}, "pharmacokinetics": {"absorption": "Iron is absorbed primarily in the duodenum and upper jejunum. Iron absorption increases when body iron stores are low or when iron demand is elevated.", "elimination": "Iron is excreted mainly through cells of the skin, gastrointestinal mucosa, nails, and hair, with only trace amounts eliminated via bile and sweat."}, "contraindications": ["Hypersensitivity to any component of the medication.", "Peptic ulcer disease, regional enteritis, or ulcerative colitis.", "Do not use for treatment exceeding 6 months except in patients with continuous bleeding, menorrhagia, or recurrent pregnancies.", "Hemolytic anemia (unless iron deficiency is also present)."], "manufacturingInfo": {"origin": "Vietnam", "storage": "Store in a cool, dry place away from light, at temperatures below 30°C.", "packaging": "Box of 1 bottle x 30ml", "manufacturer": "OPV Pharmaceutical Joint Stock Company"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Specific dosage depends on the patient's physical condition and disease progression. Detailed dosages for treating anemia, non-anemic iron deficiency, and prophylaxis are regulated according to age and weight (refer to the package insert for details).", "missedDose": "Skip the missed dose and take the next dose according to the normal schedule. Do not double the dose.", "administration": "Zibifer oral solution is administered via the oral route. Take during or immediately after meals. Can be administered as a single daily dose or divided into multiple doses throughout the day.", "overdoseManagement": "Symptoms: Epigastric pain, nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, hematemesis, drowsiness, pallor, cyanosis, convulsions, shock, coma, metabolic acidosis, hepatic necrosis, renal failure. Management: Gastric lavage with warm water or 1-5% sodium bicarbonate solution, and administration of deferoxamine to chelate iron."}, "detailedIngredients":