sis should be reassessed and alternative therapy initiated. For patients with tinea versicolor, clinical symptoms and hypopigmented or hyperpigmented patches generally resolve after 2 weeks of treatment. Elderly and children over 10 years of age: Dosage is the same as for adults. Children under 10 years of age: Safety and efficacy in pediatric patients under 10 years have not been established.", "missedDose": "Apply the missed dose as soon as remembered. However, if it is almost time for the next scheduled dose, skip the missed dose and resume the normal dosing schedule. Do not double the dose to make up for a forgotten application.", "administration": "For external topical use only. Do not apply to the mucous membranes or eyes. Do not swallow. Avoid prolonged use. Wash hands before and after application. Clean and dry the affected skin area thoroughly, then apply a thin layer of cream to the target area and surrounding skin.", "overdoseManagement": "No data regarding overdose with topical application are available; do not exceed the prescribed dosage. Closely monitor the patient for any adverse signs and provide appropriate supportive care if necessary. In case of suspected overdose or accidental ingestion, immediately take the patient to the nearest medical facility or poison control center."}, "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Ciclopirox 7.7 mg"}}	f	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:41:52.066	ciclopirox-0-77percent-vcp-topical-cream-for-superficial-fungal-infections-1-tube-x-15g	\N
