Close clinical supervision is recommended due to an increased risk of severe adverse complications.", "lactation": "Corticosteroids are excreted in breast milk and may suppress growth or interfere with endogenous corticosteroid production. A decision should be made whether to discontinue nursing or discontinue the drug.", "pediatric": "Dosage should be adjusted based on the severity of the disease and patient response. Contraindicated in premature infants and neonates.", "pregnancy": "Use only if the potential benefit outweighs the potential risk to the fetus. Infants born to mothers who have received substantial doses of corticosteroids during pregnancy should be carefully observed for signs of hypoadrenalism."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Severe neurological adverse events have been reported with epidural administration (including spinal cord infarction, paraplegia, and cortical blindness).", "Injection of hydrocortisone may cause localized skin and subcutaneous fat atrophy.", "Use with caution in patients with congestive heart failure, hypertension, or renal impairment due to the risk of sodium and water retention.", "Close clinical monitoring for symptoms of adrenocortical insufficiency is required during withdrawal.", "Corticosteroids may exacerbate systemic fungal infections.", "Use with caution in patients with active peptic ulcer disease, diverticulitis, or cirrhosis.", "Do not administer to premature infants and neonates due to the presence of benzyl alcohol in the solvent."], "adverseReactionManagement": "Cushingoid symptoms and osteoporosis can be minimized by careful selection of steroid preparations, alternate-day or intermittent dosing schedules, and supportive therapy (calcium and vitamin D supplementation). Opportunistic bacterial infections must be monitored regularly and treated with appropriate antibiotics if necessary."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:42:05.093	hydrocortisone-bidiphar-100mg-powder-for-injection-1-vial-1-ampoule-of-2ml-solvent	209
