tions": {"dosage": "Hypertension: Adults 5mg once daily. Chronic heart failure: Initiate titration starting from 1.25mg daily, doubling up to a maximum recommended dose of 10mg once daily as tolerated based on individual clinical response.", "missedDose": "Take the missed dose as soon as remembered. If it is nearly time for the subsequent dose, omit the missed dose and resume the regular dosing schedule. Do not double doses to compensate for a forgotten dose.", "administration": "For oral administration. Tablets may be taken with meals.", "overdoseManagement": "Clinical manifestations: severe bradycardia, profound hypotension, bronchospasm, and acute heart failure. Management: Institution of intensive care monitoring, performance of gastric lavage, administration of activated charcoal, atropine, catecholamines, glucagon, or temporary cardiac pacing if clinically indicated."}, "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Nebivolol 5mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "Patients over 65 years: initiate therapy at a starting dose of 2.5mg daily. Patients over 75 years: administer with caution and under close clinical monitoring.", "lactation": "Data regarding excretion in human breast milk are lacking. Nursing mothers should discontinue either breastfeeding or the administration of this drug.", "pediatric": "Safety and efficacy have not been established; therefore, use in pediatric patients and adolescents under 18 years of age is not recommended.", "pregnancy": "Adequate and well-controlled clinical data regarding use during pregnancy are not available. Nebivolol should not be used during pregnancy unless strictly necessary."}}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:42:15.623	nebilet-5mg-nebivolol-tablets-for-hypertension-and-chronic-heart-failure-box-of-2-blister-packs-x	\N
