orption and subsequent degradation into smaller peptides and amino acids. The mean terminal half-life of lixisenatide is approximately 3 hours, and the apparent clearance (CL/F) is approximately 35 L/h."}, "manufacturingInfo": {"origin": "Germany", "storage": "Store in a refrigerator (2°C - 8°C). Do not freeze.,After first use, store the pen at a temperature not exceeding 25°C for a maximum of 28 days.,Protect from excessive heat and direct light. Always keep the pen cap on when the pen is not in use.,Do not store the pen with a needle attached.", "manufacturer": "Sanofi-Aventis Deutschland GmbH"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Dosing must be individualized based on clinical response. Two prefilled pen strengths are available: Pen (10-40) delivers 10-40 units of insulin glargine in combination with 5-20 mcg of lixisenatide; Pen (30-60) delivers 30-60 units of insulin glargine in combination with 10-20 mcg of lixisenatide.", "administration": "Administer by subcutaneous injection in the abdomen, deltoid, or thigh.,Rotate injection sites within the chosen injection area from one injection to the next to reduce the risk of lipodystrophy.,Always use a new needle for each injection to prevent needle clogging.,Do not draw insulin out of the cartridge of the prefilled pen into a syringe to avoid dosing errors.", "overdoseManagement": "Overdose may result in hypoglycemia and gastrointestinal adverse reactions. Mild episodes of hypoglycemia can usually be treated with oral carbohydrates. Severe hypoglycemia may require the administration of glucagon or intravenous glucose. Gastrointestinal reactions require appropriate supportive treatment."}, "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Insulin glargine 100 units/mL; Lixisenatide 50 mcg/mL"}}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:43:29.09	soliqua-solostar-100-iu-ml-50-mcg-ml-insulin-glargine-lixisenatide-solution-for-injection-prefilled	85
