min D metabolites are excreted mainly through bile and feces, with trace amounts in urine."}, "manufacturingInfo": {"origin": "South Korea", "storage": "Keep out of reach of children. Protect from direct sunlight, store in a cool, dry place. Do not store the medication in other containers.", "packaging": "Box of 10 blisters x 10 Tablets", "manufacturer": "GENUONE SCIENCES INC"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "2 Tablets once daily.", "overdoseManagement": "Overdose may lead to hypercalcemia with symptoms including anorexia, excessive thirst, nausea, vomiting, abdominal pain, muscle weakness, mental status changes, polydipsia, polyuria, and cardiac arrhythmias. Management: Rehydration with fluids, discontinuation of calcium supplements, thiazide diuretics, or vitamin D. Corticosteroids may decrease calcium absorption. Bisphosphonates may be utilized for life-threatening hypercalcemia."}, "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Lactose monohydrate, low-substituted hydroxypropyl cellulose, colloidal silicon dioxide, anhydrous citric acid, magnesium stearate, talc.", "activeIngredients": "Calcium Citrate 750 mg (Equivalent to Elemental Calcium 158 mg), Cholecalciferol 4 mg (Equivalent to Vitamin D3 400 IU)"}}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:45:04.975	dicarbo-genuone-calcium-citrate-750mg-and-cholecalciferol-4mg-tablets-for-calcium-supplementation	138
