 gouty arthritis: Usual dose is 0.6 mg/day, 3 - 4 times per week. Prophylaxis for patients undergoing surgery for gout: 0.6 mg/dose, 3 times daily for 3 days before and 3 days after surgery.,Familial Mediterranean fever: Long-term prophylaxis: 1 - 2 mg/day divided into multiple small doses. Children: 0.5 mg/day for children < 5 years; 1 mg/day for children 5 - 10 years; 1.5 mg/day for children > 10 years.,Treatment of primary biliary cholangitis: 0.5 mg twice daily, repeated for many days.,Treatment of liver cirrhosis: Take orally 5 days per week, 1 mg daily.", "administration": "Dochicin is used as directed by a physician, typically taken orally with water."}, "generalDescription": "Dochicin is a medication used for the treatment and prevention of pain associated with gout and other inflammatory conditions.", "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Colchicine 1mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "Colchicine is excreted in breast milk. Mothers can avoid high drug concentrations in milk by taking the medication in the evening before bedtime and breastfeeding 8 hours later.", "pregnancy": "Avoid using Dochicin in pregnant women."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["When used for the treatment of acute gout attacks: Exercise caution in patients with renal or hepatic impairment.", "Exercise caution in patients with cardiac, hepatic, renal, or gastrointestinal diseases.", "Elderly and debilitated patients are susceptible to toxicity due to drug accumulation."], "adverseReactionManagement": "If adverse effects occur, discontinue use and notify a physician or go to the nearest medical facility for timely management."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:47:20.819	dochicin-1mg-tablets-for-acute-gout-and-arthritis-2-blisters-x-10-tablets	61
1643	Strepsils Orange & Vitamin C Lozenges for Sore Throat Relief (50 Sachets x 2 Lozenges)	P00455	\N	\N	Reckitt	Thailand	6286.00	4400.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/ecommerce/20241107084414-0-P00455.png?versionId=18y9z8jh2b_OWanEeogYyLCwW2RFjQ.b	Strepsils Orange & Vitamin C Lozenges formulated for the symptomatic relief of sore throat and minor mouth irritation (Box of 50 sachets x 2 Lozenges).	{"sideEffects": ["Adverse drug reactions (ADRs) may occur during treatment with this medication.", "Rare: Gastrointestinal disturbances such as diarrhea and gastric discomfort, glossodynia (painful tongue), etc., though they do not follow a specific pattern."], "effectsOnDriving": "Does not affect the ability to drive and operate machinery.", "contraindications": ["Hypersensitivity to any of the active ingredients or excipients contained in this medication."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Reckitt", "origin": "Thailand", "storage": "Store at room temperature (not exceeding 30°C).", "packaging": "Box of 50 sachets x 2 Lozenges.", "manufacturer": "Reckitt"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Allow one lozenge to dissolve slowly in the mouth every 2 to 3 hours. Do not exceed the recommended dosage. Consult a physician if symptoms persist.", "missedDose": "If a dose is missed, take it as soon as possible. However, if it is nearly time for the next scheduled dose, skip the missed dose and resume the regular dosing schedule. Do not double doses.", "administration": "Medicated cough lozenge for oral dissolution in the oral cavity.", "overdoseManagement": "No human overdose cases have been formally reported. Based on animal studies, the oral lethal dose (LD50) in mice corresponds to approximately over 80 lozenges/kg of body weight."}, "generalDescription": "Strepsils Orange & Vitamin C is a medicated lozenge indicated for the relief of coughs and sore throats. Formulated as orange-flavored lozenges enriched with vitamin C, it is used to alleviate pharyngeal symptoms such as sore throat and hoarseness. Strepsils Orange & Vitamin C typically contains active antiseptic agents that soothe pain and support the healing of minor mucosal lesions in the throat.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Propylene glycol, blood orange flavor, natural menthol, tartaric acid, refined sugar, liquid glucose, Sunset Yellow FCF (Edicol), Ponceau 4R (Edicol).", "activeIngredients": "2,4-Dichlorobenzyl Alcohol (Dybenal) 1.2 mg, Amylmetacresol 0.6 mg, Vitamin C 100 mg (containing: Ascorbic Acid 33.52 mg, Sodium Ascorbate 75.0 mg)."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Read the package leaflet carefully before use. For further information, consult your physician or pharmacist.", "Exercise caution and adjust dosage in patients with hepatic or renal impairment to prevent potential toxicity and adverse effects.", "Keep out of reach of young children as lozenges may present a choking hazard."], "adverseReactionManagement": "In the event of adverse reactions, discontinue use immediately, inform your physician, or seek medical attention at the nearest healthcare facility for prompt management."}	f	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:47:24.524	strepsils-orange-and-vitamin-c-lozenges-for-sore-throat-relief-50-sachets-x-2-lozenges	370
1703	Tanatril 5mg Tablets for Essential Hypertension (10 Blisters x 10 Tablets)	P00615	\N	\N	\N	[object Object]	676056.00	480000.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/ecommerce/20250728074547-0-P00615.png?versionId=UIWb9AdHz0ngmDjSDLRcX2eWOCUWjhJr	Tanatril 5mg tablets indicated for the treatment of essential hypertension in adults, formulated with imidapril hydrochloride.	{"indications": ["Indicated for the treatment of essential hypertension in adults."], "sideEffects": ["Renal: Increased blood urea nitrogen (BUN) and serum creatinine.", "Nervous system: Headache, confusion, dizziness.", "Cardiovascular: Hypotension.", "Respiratory: Cough, throat discomfort.", "Hepatic: Increased AST (SGOT) and ALT (SGPT).", "Hypersensitivity: Rash, pruritus.", "Other: Hyperkalemia.", "Hematological: Decreased red blood cell count, hemoglobin, hematocrit, and platelet count. Increased eosinophil count.", "Renal: Proteinuria.", "Nervous system: Orthostatic dizziness, insomnia.", "Cardiovascular: Palpitations.", "Gastrointestinal: Nausea, vomiting, gastric discomfort, abdominal pain, anorexia, diarrhea.", "Hepatic: Increased alkaline phosphatase and LDH, jaundice.", "Other: Tinnitus, dysgeusia, thirst, increased creatine phosphokinase (CPK), chest tightness, fatigue, edema, flushing, taste alterations, asthenia."], "drugInteractions": [{"drug": "Dextran cellulose sulfate for LDL-cholesterol adsorption (LDL adsorption column: Liposorber)", "effect": "Negatively charged dextran cellulose stimulates kinin production in the blood, and imidapril HCl interacts with bradykinin metabolism. Co-administration increases bradykinin accumulation, leading to anaphylactic shock."}, {"drug": "Patients undergoing hemodialysis with acrylonitrile methallylsulfonate sodium membranes", "effect": "AN69 polyelectrolyte stimulates kinin production in the blood; imidapril HCl interacts with bradykinin metabolites, causing bradykinin accumulation and resulting in anaphylactic shock."}, {"drug": "Potassium-sparing diuretics (spironolactone, triamterene, etc.), potassium supplements", "effect": "Elevated serum potassium levels."}, {"drug": "Aliskiren fumarate", "effect": "Risk of renal impairment, hyperkalemia, and hypotension."}, {"drug": "Antihypertensive diuretics (trichlormethiazide, hydrochlorothiazide, etc.)", "effect": "Pronounced hypotension following the initiation of imidapril."}, {"drug": "Lithium-containing preparations (lithium carbonate)", "effect": "Risk of lithium toxicity (somnolence, tremor, confusion, etc.)."}, {"drug": "Non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (e.g., indomethacin)", "effect": "Reduced antihypertensive efficacy of imidapril."}, {"drug": "Kallidinogenase-containing preparations", "effect": "Excessive blood pressure reduction."}, {"drug": "Antihypertensive agents (nitrates, etc.)", "effect": "Potentiated hypotensive effect."}, {"drug": "Non-potassium-sparing diuretics", "effect": "Risk of sudden and severe hypotension and/or acute renal failure upon initiating ACE inhibitor therapy."}, {"drug": "Gold preparations", "effect": "Nitritoid reactions (flushing, nausea, vomiting, hypotension)."}, {"drug": "Antidiabetic medications (insulin, sulfonamides)", "effect": "Enhanced hypoglycemic effect."}, {"drug": "Tricyclic antidepressants, antipsychotics", "effect": "Enhanced hypotensive effect and increased risk of orthostatic hypotension."}, {"drug": "Rifampicin", "effect": "Decreased serum concentrations of imidapril and its active metabolite, potentially reducing the antihypertensive effect."}, {"drug": "Sympathomimetics", "effect": "Reduced antihypertensive efficacy."}], "effectsOnDriving": "Due to the hypotensive effect of the medication which may cause dizziness or lightheadedness, patients should exercise caution when engaging in activities requiring alertness, such as driving, working at heights, or operating machinery.", "contraindications": ["Patients with a history of hypersensitivity to any component of the medication.", "Patients with a history of angioedema (angioedema associated with ACE inhibitors, hereditary angioedema, acquired angioedema, idiopathic angioedema, etc., which may present with dyspnea).", "Patients undergoing extracorporeal treatment using dextran sulfate fixed with cellulose, tryptophan fixed with polyvinyl alcohol, or polyethylene terephthalate (risk of shock).", "Patients undergoing hemodialysis with acrylonitrile methallylsulfonate sodium (AN69) membranes due to the risk of anaphylactoid reactions.", "Women who are pregnant or of childbearing potential.", "Patients with diabetes mellitus receiving treatment with aliskiren fumarate (except in patients whose blood pressure remains uncontrolled despite alternative antihypertensive therapy). Increased risk of non-fatal stroke, hyperkalemia, and renal impairment has been reported.", "Renal impairment with or without hemodialysis (creatinine clearance < 10 mL/min)."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Tanatril", "origin": "[object Object]", "storage": "Store in a dry place below 30°C. Protect from light. Protect from moisture after opening the box.", "packaging": "[object Object]", "manufacturer": "[object Object]"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Adults: Initial dose is 5 mg once daily. If optimal blood pressure is not achieved after 3 weeks of treatment, the daily dose may be increased to 10 mg, which is the optimal daily dose. However, a small number of patients may require a maximum recommended daily dose of 20 mg, or combination therapy with a diuretic. The benefits of combining imidapril with other antihypertensive modalities have not been fully evaluated in all patients.\\nElderly patients (65 years and older): The initial dose is 2.5 mg once daily. Dosage should be adjusted based on blood pressure response. The maximum recommended dose is 10 mg once daily.\\nRenal impairment: Imidapril and its active pharmacological metabolite imidaprilat are primarily eliminated via the kidneys. Renal function should be assessed prior to initiating imidapril therapy in patients with suspected renal impairment. Creatinine clearance should be determined prior to treatment using the Cockcroft & Gault formula (Nephron 1976, 16: 31-41).\\nHepatic impairment: Recommended initial dose is 2.5 mg once daily. Exercise caution when prescribing this medication to this patient group.\\nPatients at increased risk of first-dose hypotension: First-dose hypotension may occur in high-risk patients. Prior to initiating treatment, correct salt and/or fluid depletion if possible, and discontinue diuretic therapy 2 to 3 days before starting ACE inhibitor treatment. If correction is not feasible, an initial dose of 2.5 mg is recommended. In patients with severe congestive heart failure, hypotension has been reported following ACE inhibitor therapy. In these patients, the recommended dose is 2.5 mg once daily under strict medical supervision. Patients at high risk of acute, severe hypotension after the first dose should be medically monitored, preferably in a hospital setting, for up to 68 hours following the initial dose and whenever the dose of imidapril or a concomitant diuretic is increased. The starting dose should be 2.5 mg. This also applies to patients with angina pectoris or cerebrovascular disease, who are at increased risk of myocardial infarction or cerebrovascular accidents due to excessive blood pressure reduction.\\nPediatric patients: Safety and efficacy of Tanatril have not been established due to insufficient research data.", "missedDose": "[object Object]", "administration": "The medication should be taken at the same time each day approximately 15 minutes before a meal, as clinical efficacy has been established under these conditions.", "overdoseManagement": "[object Object]"}, "generalDescription": "Tanatril 5mg tablets are an antihypertensive medication containing the active ingredient imidapril hydrochloride. The medication is used for the treatment of essential hypertension in adults.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Lactose, Macrogol 6000, Magnesium stearate", "activeIngredients": "Imidapril hydrochloride 5mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "Special caution must be exercised when administering the medication to this population, initiating at a lower dose (e.g., 2.5 mg) and monitoring the patient carefully. Tanatril is primarily eliminated via the kidneys, and elderly patients often have impaired renal function, leading to higher drug concentrations and increased susceptibility to adverse reactions. Additionally, excessive hypotension is dangerous for elderly patients (cerebral infarction, etc.).", "lactation": "Do not use Tanatril during lactation. If treatment is necessary, breast-feeding must be discontinued.", "pediatric": "The safety and efficacy of Tanatril have not been established due to insufficient research data.", "pregnancy": "Tanatril is contraindicated during pregnancy or suspected pregnancy due to the risk of oligohydramnios, fetal death, hypotension, renal failure, hyperkalemia, and neonatal skull hypoplasia during the second or third trimesters. Limb contractures and craniofacial deformations in newborns may occur secondary to oligohydramnios."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["General precautions (Tanatril must be used with caution in the following patients):", "Renal impairment: Changes in renal function can be anticipated in susceptible individuals due to the inhibition of the renin-angiotensin-aldosterone system. Therefore, imidapril and other ACE inhibitors should be used with caution in patients with renal impairment. Dosage reduction is required for patients with a creatinine clearance between 30 and 80 mL/min.", "Imidapril should not be used in patients with a creatinine clearance below 30 mL/min due to limited clinical experience.", "Monitor renal function closely throughout treatment. Renal impairment has been reported in association with ACE inhibitors, primarily in patients with severe heart failure or underlying renal disease, including renal artery stenosis. Some patients without prior renal disease may experience transient increases in blood urea nitrogen and serum creatinine when ACE inhibitors are co-administered with diuretics. Dosage reduction of the ACE inhibitor and/or diuretic may be required, and renal function should be monitored during the first week of treatment.", "Unilateral or bilateral renal artery stenosis.", "Cerebrovascular disorders (severe hypotension may cause reduced arterial blood flow to the brain, worsening the patient's condition).", "Elderly patients.", "Hyperkalemia.", "Important precautions:", "Patient populations including those with severe hypertension, patients undergoing hemodialysis, patients taking diuretics (especially newly initiated diuretic therapy), or patients on a strict salt-restricted diet may experience a transient, profound hypotensive drop following the initial dose of Tanatril; treatment should be initiated at a lower dose with gradual titration while closely monitoring the patient.", "Discontinue the medication 24 hours prior to surgery.", "In patients with unilateral or bilateral renal artery stenosis, renal function may rapidly deteriorate due to decreased renal blood flow and reduced glomerular filtration pressure. Tanatril should not be used in these patients unless treatment is strictly necessary.", "In patients with hyperkalemia, symptoms may worsen. Tanatril should not be used in these patients unless treatment is strictly necessary. Since hyperkalemia is often secondary to renal impairment and/or uncontrolled diabetes mellitus, serum potassium levels should be monitored carefully.", "Patients may experience renal impairment, hyperkalemia, and hypotension when combining the medication with aliskiren fumarate. Do not co-administer Tanatril and aliskiren fumarate in patients with renal impairment with an estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) < 60 mL/min/1.73 m - , unless necessary.", "In patients with type 1 diabetes mellitus-associated diabetic nephropathy, further deterioration of renal function or hyperkalemia may occur during the initial treatment period (approximately 1 month). Serum creatinine and potassium levels should be monitored throughout the initiation phase. If rapid renal function decline or severe hyperkalemia occurs, reduce the dose or discontinue the medication.", "Aortic stenosis or mitral stenosis/hypertrophic cardiomyopathy: Similar to other ACE inhibitors, exercise caution when prescribing imidapril to patients with left ventricular outflow obstruction.", "Neutropenia/agranulocytosis, thrombocytopenia, and anemia are rarely observed in patients treated with ACE inhibitors, including imidapril. In patients with normal renal function and no other risk factors, neutropenia is extremely rare. Use imidapril with extreme caution in patients with collagen vascular disease, immunosuppressive therapy, treatment with allopurinol or procainamide, or those with multiple risk factors, particularly pre-existing renal impairment. In rare isolated cases, some patients with severe infections fail to respond to potent antibiotics.", "If imidapril is administered to such patients, white blood cell counts and differentials should be monitored prior to treatment, every 2 weeks during the first 3 months of imidapril therapy, and periodically thereafter. Throughout treatment, patients should be instructed to report any signs of infection (e.g., pharyngitis, fever) to facilitate detection of leukopenia.", "Discontinue imidapril and concomitant medications if neutropenia is detected or suspected (neutrophil count below 1000/mm - ). In most patients, neutrophil counts return to normal upon discontinuation of imidapril.", "Hypertension secondary to renovascular disease: Increased risk of severe hypotension and renal failure in patients with bilateral or unilateral renal artery stenosis treated with ACE inhibitors. Loss of renal function may occur with only minor changes in serum creatinine. In these patients, treatment must be initiated under close medical supervision at low doses, with strict monitoring of renal function.", "Kidney transplantation: There is no clinical experience with the administration of imidapril in recent kidney transplant recipients.", "Anaphylactoid reactions during desensitization: Life-threatening anaphylactoid reactions rarely occur in patients receiving insect venom desensitization therapy while taking another ACE inhibitor. In these patients, such reactions can be avoided by temporarily withholding the ACE inhibitor. Exercise caution when administering ACE inhibitors to patients undergoing anesthesia.", "Hepatic impairment: Rarely, ACE inhibitors have been associated with a syndrome that starts with cholestatic jaundice and progresses to fulminant hepatic necrosis and (sometimes) death. The mechanism of this syndrome is not fully understood. Patients receiving ACE inhibitors who develop jaundice or marked elevations of hepatic enzymes should discontinue the ACE inhibitor and receive appropriate medical follow-up.", "Diabetic patients: Blood glucose levels should be closely monitored in pre-existing diabetic patients treated with oral hypoglycemic agents or insulin during the first month of ACE inhibitor therapy.", "Lactose: Tanatril contains lactose. Patients with rare hereditary problems of galactose intolerance, total lactase deficiency, or glucose-galactose malabsorption should not take this medication.", "Dual blockade of the renin-angiotensin-aldosterone system (RAAS): There is evidence that co-administration of ACE inhibitors, angiotensin II receptor blockers, or aliskiren increases the risk of hypotension, hyperkalemia, and renal impairment (including renal failure). Dual blockade of the RAAS through the combination of ACE inhibitors, angiotensin II receptor blockers, or aliskiren is not recommended. If dual blockade therapy is considered absolutely necessary, it must be subject to close supervision and frequent monitoring of renal function, electrolytes, and blood pressure. ACE inhibitors and angiotensin II receptor blockers should not be co-administered in patients with diabetic nephropathy.", "Elderly patients: Special caution must be exercised when administering the medication to this population; initiate therapy at a lower dose (e.g., 2.5 mg) and monitor the patient carefully. Tanatril is primarily eliminated via the kidneys, and elderly patients frequently exhibit decreased renal function, leading to elevated drug retention and an increased susceptibility to adverse reactions. Furthermore, excessive blood pressure reduction poses severe risks to elderly patients (e.g., cerebral infarction).", "Pediatric use: The safety of the medication in children has not been established.", "Caution: Tanatril tablets are packaged in press-through blister (PTP) packs. Patients must be instructed to remove the medication from the packaging before ingestion (cases have been reported where patients accidentally swallowed the entire PTP pack, and the sharp edges of the foil lacerated the esophageal mucosa, leading to serious complications such as mediastinitis)."]}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:49:38.223	tanatril-5mg-tablets-for-essential-hypertension-10-blisters-x-10-tablets	\N
1636	Klacid 125mg/5ml Clarithromycin Granules for Oral Suspension for Respiratory Tract Infections (Bottle of 60ml)	P01690	\N	\N	Abbott	United States	169333.00	127000.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/ecommerce/20250520035308-0-P01690.png?versionId=Io58VcdXXNVL6nU6xeEFV1OutlSNin9K	Klacid 125mg/5ml granules for oral suspension for the treatment of bacterial respiratory tract infections (60ml bottle).	{"indications": ["Upper respiratory tract bacterial infections", "Lower respiratory tract bacterial infections", "Acute otitis media", "Skin and skin structure bacterial infections", "Localized or disseminated Mycobacterium infections caused by M. avium or M. intracellulare", "Localized infections caused by M. chelonae, M. fortuitum, or M. kansasii"], "sideEffects": ["Common: Insomnia, dysgeusia, headache, ageusia, vasodilation, diarrhea, vomiting, dyspepsia, nausea, abdominal pain, abnormal liver function tests, rash, hyperhidrosis.", "Uncommon: Cellulitis, Candida superinfection, gastroenteritis, vaginal infection, leukopenia, anaphylactic reaction, anorexia, anxiety, dizziness, tremor, hearing impaired, tinnitus, cardiac arrest, atrial fibrillation, QT prolongation, asthma, esophagitis, gastroesophageal reflux, hepatitis, increased liver enzymes, urticaria, muscle spasm, blood creatinine increased."], "drugInteractions": [{"drug": "Drugs metabolized by CYP3A4 (alprazolam, carbamazepine, cyclosporine, statins, etc.)", "effect": "Increased plasma concentrations of these drugs."}, {"drug": "CYP3A4 inducers (rifampicin, phenytoin, phenobarbital, St. John's Wort)", "effect": "Increased metabolism of clarithromycin, resulting in decreased drug concentrations."}, {"drug": "Hypoglycemic agents, insulin", "effect": "May cause hypoglycemia."}, {"drug": "Warfarin", "effect": "Risk of severe hemorrhage and increased International Normalized Ratio (INR)."}], "effectsOnDriving": "May cause dizziness, vertigo, confusion, and disorientation.", "contraindications": ["Hypersensitivity to macrolide antibiotics or any excipients.", "Concomitant administration with astemizole, cisapride, pimozide, or terfenadine.", "Concomitant administration with ergotamine or dihydroergotamine.", "Concomitant administration with HMG-CoA reductase inhibitors (statins) extensively metabolized by CYP3A4 (lovastatin or simvastatin).", "History of QT prolongation on electrocardiogram (ECG) or ventricular cardiac arrhythmia.", "Concomitant use with colchicine in patients with hepatic or renal impairment who are taking P-glycoprotein or CYP3A4 inhibitors."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Abbott", "origin": "United States", "storage": "Store at room temperature (15°30°C). The reconstituted suspension is stable for 14 days; do not refrigerate.", "packaging": "60ml bottle"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Pediatric patients 6 months to 12 years of age: 7.5 mg/kg twice daily (maximum 500 mg per dose). Mycobacterium infections: 15°30 mg/kg/day divided into 2 doses. Patients with renal impairment (creatinine clearance < 30 mL/min): reduce dosage by half.", "missedDose": "Take the missed dose as soon as remembered. If it is almost time for the next dose, skip the missed dose and resume the normal dosing schedule. Do not double the dose.", "administration": "Prepare the oral suspension by adding water to the granules in the bottle and shaking vigorously prior to administration. Can be taken with or without food, and may be administered with milk.", "overdoseManagement": "Symptoms: Nausea, vomiting, abdominal pain, diarrhea. Management: Symptomatic and supportive treatment; hemodialysis is not effective."}, "generalDescription": "Klacid 125mg/5ml, manufactured by PT. Abbott Indonesia, is a macrolide antibiotic with Clarithromycin as its primary active ingredient.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Sucrose, xanthan gum, silicon dioxide, potassium sorbate, citric acid, maltodextrin, titanium dioxide, fruit flavoring agents.", "activeIngredients": "Clarithromycin 125mg (per 5ml)"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "Special caution is required when co-administered with colchicine due to the risk of toxicity.", "lactation": "Safety has not been established; the drug is excreted in breast milk.", "pediatric": "Dosage is based on body weight (6 months to 12 years of age).", "pregnancy": "Should not be used unless the potential benefit outweighs the potential risk."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Use with caution in patients with severe renal impairment or hepatic impairment.", "Risk of superinfection with non-susceptible bacteria or fungi during prolonged use.", "Risk of Clostridium difficile-associated diarrhea (pseudomembranous colitis).", "May exacerbate myasthenia gravis.", "Exercise caution when administered concomitantly with CYP3A4 inducers, hypoglycemic agents, warfarin, or triazolobenzodiazepines.", "Risk of QT interval prolongation.", "Discontinue medication immediately if severe hypersensitivity reactions occur, such as Stevens-Johnson syndrome or anaphylactic shock."], "adverseReactionManagement": "Discontinue use and notify a physician or proceed to the nearest medical facility for prompt medical management."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:46:59.245	klacid-125mg-5ml-clarithromycin-granules-for-oral-suspension-for-respiratory-tract-infections	3
1645	Hapacol 650mg Extra Tablets for Pain Relief and Fever Reduction (10 Blisters x 10 Tablets)	P00506	\N	\N	DHG Pharma	Vietnam	6471.00	5500.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/ecommerce/20250415090624-0-P00506.jpg?versionId=.fj7Yb3q5zzxr1jva8YZ590qguRl_Omc	Hapacol 650mg Extra tablets formulated with Paracetamol and Caffeine for effective pain relief and fever reduction (Box of 10 blisters x 10 tablets).	{"indications": ["Indicated for pain relief in conditions such as headaches, migraine, sore throat, dysmenorrhea, toothache, and musculoskeletal pain, as well as for fever reduction."], "sideEffects": ["Paracetamol: Allergic reactions, skin rashes, vomiting, nausea, pancytopenia, leukopenia, anemia, and hepatic impairment with prolonged high-dose use.", "Caffeine: Hypertension, daytime drowsiness, nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, insomnia, headache, tremors, nervousness, and anxiety."], "drugInteractions": [{"drug": "Coumarin and indandione derivatives", "effect": "Long-term, high-dose administration of paracetamol slightly increases the anticoagulant effect."}, {"drug": "Phenothiazines and antipyretic therapy", "effect": "May lead to severe hypothermia."}, {"drug": "Anticonvulsants (phenytoin, barbiturates, carbamazepine) and isoniazid", "effect": "Increases the hepatotoxicity of paracetamol."}, {"drug": "Alcohol", "effect": "Chronic and excessive consumption increases paracetamol-induced hepatotoxicity."}, {"drug": "Caffeine-containing beverages (tea, coffee)", "effect": "Concurrent use should be avoided."}, {"drug": "Antibiotics (ciprofloxacin, enoxacin, lomefloxacin, norfloxacin, ofloxacin)", "effect": "Prolong the elimination half-life of caffeine."}, {"drug": "Phenytoin, fluvoxamine, terbinafine, cimetidine, methoxsalen, oral contraceptives, phenylpropanolamine, ephedrine, theophylline", "effect": "Do not co-administer with caffeine."}], "effectsOnDriving": "This medication does not affect the ability to drive and operate machinery.", "contraindications": ["Hypersensitivity to any of the ingredients in this medication.", "Patients with glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase (G6PD) deficiency."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "HAU GIANG PHARMACEUTICAL JOINT STOCK COMPANY", "origin": "Vietnam", "storage": "Store in a dry place, protected from light, at temperatures below 30°C.", "packaging": "Box of 10 blisters x 10 tablets."}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Adults and adolescents aged 12 years and older: Take 1 tablet 3 to 4 times daily. The dosing interval between doses should be 4 to 6 hours. Do not exceed 6 tablets per day. In patients with severe renal impairment (creatinine clearance < 10 mL/min), the interval between doses must be at least 8 hours.", "missedDose": "Take the dose as soon as remembered. If it is almost time for the next dose, skip the missed dose and resume the normal dosing schedule. Do not double the dose.", "administration": "Hapacol 650 Extra is administered via the oral route.", "overdoseManagement": "Paracetamol overdose: Hepatic necrosis is the most serious acute toxic effect. Management: Gastric lavage within 4 hours, administration of sulfhydryl compounds (N-acetylcysteine) or methionine, activated charcoal, and saline laxatives. Caffeine overdose: Insomnia, restlessness, agitation, and delirium."}, "generalDescription": "Hapacol 650 Extra is manufactured by Hau Giang Pharmaceutical Joint Stock Company. Containing Paracetamol and Caffeine as active ingredients, it is a medication used to relieve pain including headaches, migraines, sore throats, dysmenorrhea, toothaches, and muscle aches, and to reduce fever.", "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Paracetamol 650mg, Caffeine 65mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "Use this medication only when strictly necessary.", "pregnancy": "Use this medication only when strictly necessary."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Patients with phenylketonuria and those who must restrict phenylalanine intake should avoid using paracetamol concomitantly with medications or foods containing aspartame.", "Hypersensitive individuals (e.g., those with asthma) should avoid paracetamol combined with medications or foods containing sulfites.", "Use with caution in patients with preexisting anemia, or hepatic and renal impairment.", "Avoid or limit alcohol consumption as it increases hepatotoxicity.", "Exercise caution in patients with hypertension when using high doses of caffeine.", "Warning regarding severe cutaneous adverse reactions (SCAR) such as Stevens-Johnson syndrome (SJS), toxic epidermal necrolysis (TEN), Lyell syndrome, and acute generalized exanthematous pustulosis (AGEP)."], "adverseReactionManagement": "Notify your physician immediately of any adverse reactions experienced while using this medication."}	f	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:47:31.896	hapacol-650mg-extra-tablets-for-pain-relief-and-fever-reduction-10-blisters-x-10-tablets	62
