e: 0.5 mg/kg/day for 4 weeks. Maintenance dose: 0.1 to 1 mg/kg/day adjusted according to individual patient response and tolerance. A maximum dose of 1 mg/kg/day should only be prescribed for a limited duration. The standard duration of treatment is 16 weeks.", "administration": "For lower doses, administer once daily. For higher dosages, divide the total daily dose into multiple administrations, to be taken with meals."}, "generalDescription": "Aju Akinol is a specialized dermatological medication indicated for severe forms of acne that fail to respond to standard treatments. The primary active pharmaceutical ingredient is isotretinoin, which acts on sebaceous glands to suppress sebum production, reduce sebocyte proliferation, and inhibit inflammatory processes within the pilosebaceous unit.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Soybean oil, palm oil, white beeswax, lecithin, gelatin, concentrated glycerin, D-sorbitol 70%, ethyl vanillin, titanium dioxide, FD&C Red No. 3, FD&C Red No. 40, FD&C Blue No. 1, and purified water.", "activeIngredients": "Isotretinoin 10mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "Contraindicated. Due to its lipophilic nature, isotretinoin is likely excreted in breast milk and may pose significant risks to the nursing infant.", "pregnancy": "Contraindicated. Isotretinoin is a potent human teratogen associated with a high frequency of severe and life-threatening congenital malformations."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Contraindicated in women who are pregnant or planning to become pregnant due to high teratogenic risk.", "Regular monitoring of serum lipid profiles (specifically triglycerides) and hepatic function is required during therapy."]}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:47:38.363	akinol-10mg-soft-capsules-for-severe-nodulocystic-acne-3-blisters-x-10-capsules	371
