hould be inserted deep into the vagina in the evening before bedtime, preferably in a supine position with legs slightly flexed. In case of vaginal dryness, the tablet may be moistened with a drop of water prior to insertion.", "overdoseManagement": "Administering more than one tablet daily may increase the incidence of adverse reactions. In the event of overdose, perform vaginal irrigation to remove any remaining medication."}, "generalDescription": "Fluomizin 10 mg (1 x 6 tablets) manufactured by Rottendorf Pharma GmbH, containing dequalinium chloride as the active pharmaceutical ingredient, is indicated for the treatment of fungal and bacterial vaginal infections (such as bacterial vaginosis and candidiasis), trichomoniasis, and for achieving vaginal antisepsis prior to gynecological interventions and delivery. The vaginal tablets are white to off-white, oval-shaped, and biconvex.", "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Dequalinium chloride 10mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "Can be used during the lactation period.", "pregnancy": "Can be used during pregnancy. However, caution should be exercised during the first trimester."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Read the package leaflet carefully before use. Do not use vaginal douches or rinses while undergoing treatment. Patients should use sanitary pads and change underwear daily, washing them at a temperature of at least 80°C."], "adverseReactionManagement": "Notify your physician of any adverse reactions experienced. If discomfort persists or vaginal epithelial damage occurs, the patient should discontinue treatment and seek medical attention."}	f	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:47:44.737	fluomizin-10mg-vaginal-tablets-for-vaginal-candidiasis-and-bacterial-vaginosis-1-blister-x-6-tablets	372
