taken immediately before bedtime. Dosage must be individualized. Adults: initial dose 10mg, may be increased to 20mg after 1-2 weeks. Renal impairment (GFR < 50 ml/min): initial dose 5mg, may be increased to 10mg. Pediatric patients aged 2-5 years: 5mg (recommended for Eastern countries). Pediatric patients aged 6-12 years: initial dose 10mg, may be increased to 20mg (doses >10mg are not recommended for children in Eastern countries).", "missedDose": "Administer as soon as remembered. If close to the next scheduled dose, skip the missed dose and resume the normal dosing schedule. Do not double doses.", "administration": "Administered orally, taken immediately before bedtime.", "overdoseManagement": "Symptoms: Headache, anxiety, tremor, nausea, muscle cramps, palpitations, tachycardia, cardiac arrhythmias, hypotension, hyperglycemia, lactic acidosis, hypokalemia. Management: Usually supportive. Severe cases: Gastric lavage, activated charcoal, evaluation of acid-base balance, blood glucose, and electrolytes. Cardiovascular monitoring. Antidote is a cardioselective beta-blocker (use with caution in patients with bronchospasm)."}, "generalDescription": "Bambec 10mg tablets are a bronchodilator medication used for the treatment of respiratory tract conditions such as bronchial asthma and chronic bronchitis. The active pharmaceutical ingredient is bambuterol hydrochloride at a strength of 10mg. It acts as a selective beta-2 adrenergic receptor agonist, causing relaxation of bronchial smooth muscle, inhibiting edema responses, and preventing the release of endogenous bronchoconstricting mediators.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Lactose monohydrate, maize starch, povidone, microcrystalline cellulose, magnesium stearate.", "activeIngredients": "Bambuterol hydrochloride 10mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "Administer standard adult dosing.", "lactation": "It is unknown whether the medication is excreted into breast milk. Terbutaline passes into breast milk but does not appear to affect nursing infants at therapeutic doses. The decision to discontinue breastfeeding or discontinue the medication should be based on clinical benefit.", "pediatric": "Not recommended for use in pediatric patients due to limited clinical data. Specific dosage guidelines for children aged 2-12 years vary by geographic region.", "pregnancy": "Use with caution during the first trimester of pregnancy. Exercise caution in late pregnancy due to tocolytic effects. Transient hypoglycemia has been reported in premature infants whose mothers were treated with beta-2 agonists."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Patients with renal impairment (GFR < 50 ml/min): dose reduction by half is required.", "Patients with cirrhosis or severe hepatic impairment: individual dosage adjustment is necessary.", "Patients with thyrotoxicosis.", "Patients with severe cardiovascular disease (ischemic heart disease, arrhythmias, or severe heart failure): advise patients to report chest pain or worsening symptoms.", "Patients with diabetes mellitus: closer blood glucose monitoring is required due to the hyperglycemic effect of the medication.", "Patients at risk of hypokalemia (especially during acute severe asthma exacerbations): serum potassium levels should be monitored.", "If symptoms persist or an increase in dosage is required: the therapeutic regimen must be re-evaluated."], "adverseReactionManagement": "Most adverse reactions are characteristic of sympathomimetic amines and typically subside within 1 to 2 weeks of treatment."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:48:04.141	bambec-10mg-tablets-for-asthma-and-chronic-bronchitis-3-blisters-x-10-tablets	\N
