ring in the elderly or in the presence of other recognized risk factors.", "Hypomagnesemia: Severe hypomagnesemia has been reported in patients treated with proton pump inhibitors for at least 3 months, and in most cases for approximately 1 year.", "Gastrointestinal effects: Symptomatic response to pantoprazole does not preclude the presence of gastric malignancy. The possibility of malignant gastric ulceration should be ruled out prior to initiating therapy.", "Hepatic effects: Mild and transient increases in serum ALT (SGPT) have been reported.", "Cyanocobalamin malabsorption: Hypochlorhydria or achlorhydria resulting from long-term daily treatment (exceeding 3 years) with acid-suppressing medications may reduce absorption of cyanocobalamin.", "Pediatric population: The safety and efficacy of the medication in children under 18 years of age have not been established."]}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:49:08.59	pantostad-40mg-delayed-release-capsules-for-gastroesophageal-reflux-disease-4-blisters-x-7-tablets	183
