eeding women.", "Children under 18 years of age (due to insufficient safety and efficacy data in this population)."], "manufacturingInfo": {"storage": "Store in a dry place at temperatures not exceeding 30°C."}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "The usual dosage of Mydocalm 50 mg film-coated tablets is 1 to 3 tablets taken three times daily.", "missedDose": "If a dose is missed, take it as soon as possible. However, if it is almost time for your next dose, skip the missed dose and resume your regular dosing schedule. Do not double the dose to make up for a forgotten tablet.", "administration": "For oral administration. Take the medication during or after a meal with a glass of water.", "overdoseManagement": "Mydocalm has no specific antidote. In the event of an overdose, symptomatic and supportive treatment is recommended. In case of an emergency, immediately call local emergency services or visit the nearest medical facility."}, "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Core tablets: Citric acid monohydrate, colloidal anhydrous silica, stearic acid, talc, microcrystalline cellulose, corn starch, lactose monohydrate (48.500 mg). Coating: Colloidal anhydrous silica, titanium dioxide (E 171), macrogol 6000, hypromellose, lactose monohydrate (0.392 mg).", "activeIngredients": "Tolperisone Hydrochloride 50mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "Tolperisone is contraindicated during breastfeeding.", "pediatric": "The use of this medication is not recommended in children under 18 years of age.", "pregnancy": "Due to the lack of adequate human clinical data, tolperisone should not be used during pregnancy (especially in the first trimester) unless the potential benefit to the mother outweighs the potential risk to the fetus."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Hypersensitivity reactions: The risk of hypersensitivity reactions is generally higher in women, patients with a history of allergies, or those with a history of hypersensitivity to other medications.", "Caution should be exercised when administering tolperisone to patients hypersensitive to lidocaine due to the potential for cross-reactivity.", "Patients with lactose intolerance should note that each Mydocalm 50 mg tablet contains 48.892 mg of lactose monohydrate. This product also contains the excipient titanium dioxide (E171)."], "adverseReactionManagement": "If adverse reactions occur, discontinue use and inform your doctor or visit the nearest medical facility for timely management."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:49:22	mydocalm-50mg-tablets-for-post-stroke-muscle-spasticity-in-adults-3-blisters-x-10-tablets	\N
1679	Axcel Hydrocortisone 1% Topical Cream for Dermatitis, Eczema, Allergies, and Pruritus (15g Tube)	P00697	\N	\N	\N	Vietnam	46667.00	35000.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/ecommerce/20250508070522-0-P00697.jpg?versionId=VtcXAfESq864U8b5OqZCug6KVwtDxj6c	Axcel Hydrocortisone 1% topical cream formulated for the treatment of inflammatory dermatoses, eczema, allergic skin reactions, and pruritus.	{"effectsOnDriving": "No evidence indicates that the medication affects the ability to drive or operate machinery.", "contraindications": ["Cutaneous tuberculosis, fungal skin infections, varicella, recent vaccination sites, and Herpes simplex infections.", "Hypersensitivity to any component of the medication.", "Hydrocortisone should not be applied to the ear if the tympanic membrane is perforated."], "manufacturingInfo": {"storage": "Store below 30°C, protect from light.", "packaging": "15g tube"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Apply a thin layer of the medication to the affected skin area 2 to 3 times daily after gently cleansing the area. Once clinical improvement is observed, application frequency may be reduced to 1 to 2 times daily. Treatment duration should not exceed 2 weeks. Discontinue use once the condition has cleared. If no clinical response is observed within 2 weeks, discontinue treatment and re-evaluate the diagnosis.", "missedDose": "If a dose is missed, apply it as soon as remembered. However, if it is almost time for the next scheduled dose, skip the missed dose and resume the normal dosing schedule. Do not double the dose to make up for a forgotten application.", "administration": "For external topical use only.", "overdoseManagement": "Acute toxicity or fatalities resulting from overdose are extremely rare. In cases of overdose, there is no specific antidote; management should be supportive and symptomatic. In case of emergency, immediately contact local emergency services or proceed to the nearest medical facility."}, "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Dehydag wax 'O', cremophor A6, cremophor A25, liquid paraffin, chlorocresol, propylene glycol, sodium dihydrogen phosphate, purified water", "activeIngredients": "Hydrocortisone 0.15g (per 15g cream)"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "The safety of topical hydrocortisone during lactation has not been established. Therefore, application over large surface areas or for extended periods should be avoided.", "pregnancy": "The safety of topical hydrocortisone during pregnancy has not been established. Therefore, application over large surface areas or for extended periods should be avoided."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Hydrocortisone may mask or exacerbate early signs of bacterial infection. If a bacterial infection is suspected, appropriate adjunctive therapy (such as antibiotics) should be considered; if the infection does not respond promptly, use of the medication should be suspended until the infection is controlled. Systemic adverse effects may occur when applied to extensive surface areas. Occlusive dressings should be avoided. Although hydrocortisone is generally effective for symptomatic treatment of dermatoses, underlying causes should be identified and treated whenever possible. Avoid prolonged use in infants, pregnant women, and nursing mothers."]}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:49:25.251	axcel-hydrocortisone-1percent-topical-cream-for-dermatitis-eczema-allergies-and-pruritus-15g-tube	\N
