ne", "effect": "Particular caution is required when administered concomitantly."}, {"drug": "Alcohol", "effect": "Concomitant use is not recommended."}], "effectsOnDriving": "In some patients, the medication may decrease alertness. Therefore, attention should be drawn to the risk of drowsiness associated with the use of this medicinal product, particularly when driving and operating machinery.", "contraindications": ["Hypersensitivity to tianeptine or to any of the excipients of Stablon.", "Children under 15 years of age.", "Pregnancy or breastfeeding.", "Combination with non-selective monoamine oxidase inhibitors (MAOIs) (see section Drug Interactions)."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Servier", "origin": "France", "storage": "Keep this medication out of the reach and sight of children. Store below 30°C.", "packaging": "Box containing 30 tablets (2 blisters x 15 tablets)", "manufacturer": "Les Laboratoires Servier Industrie"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "The recommended dosage is 3 tablets daily, taken immediately before breakfast, lunch, and dinner, swallowed with water.,In patients over 70 years of age and those with renal impairment, the dosage must not exceed 2 tablets daily.,Do not stop taking this medication without consulting your physician.,Follow the duration of treatment prescribed by your physician strictly.,Under no circumstances should the treatment be prolonged without medical authorization.,Always strictly adhere to the prescription issued by your physician.", "missedDose": "Consult your physician before continuing treatment.", "administration": "Oral administration."}, "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "D-mannitol, maize starch, talc, magnesium stearate. Film coating: ethylcellulose, glyceryl oleate, SEPIFILM SE 700 white (povidone, carmellose sodium, colloidal anhydrous silica, talc, sucrose, polysorbate 80, titanium dioxide, sodium bicarbonate), white beeswax.", "activeIngredients": "Tianeptine sodium 12.5mg."}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "Inform your physician if you are breastfeeding. As a rule, always consult your physician or pharmacist before taking any medication during breastfeeding.", "pregnancy": "Inform your physician if you are pregnant. As a rule, always consult your physician or pharmacist before taking any medication during pregnancy."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Prolonged use at high doses may lead to drug dependence.", "Do not exceed the recommended dose.", "Suicidal ideation and worsening of your depression or anxiety disorder: If you are depressed and/or have anxiety disorders, you can sometimes have thoughts of harming or killing yourself. These may be increased when first starting antidepressants, since these medicines all take time to work, usually about two weeks, but sometimes longer. You may be more likely to think like this: If you have previously had thoughts about killing or harming yourself. If you are a young adult. Clinical trials have shown an increased risk of suicidal behavior in young adults aged under 25 years with psychiatric conditions who were treated with antidepressants. If you have thoughts of harming or killing yourself at any time, contact your doctor or go to a hospital straight away. You may find it helpful to tell a relative or close friend that you are depressed or have an anxiety disorder, and ask them to read this leaflet. You might ask them to tell you if they think your depression or anxiety is getting worse, or if they are worried about changes in your behavior.", "Stablon should not be administered to children and adolescents (under 18 years of age).", "This medicinal product contains sucrose; therefore, it is contraindicated in patients with fructose intolerance, glucose-galactose malabsorption syndrome, or sucrase-isomaltase deficiency (rare metabolic disorders).", "Do not discontinue treatment abruptly; the dosage must be tapered gradually over a period of 7 to 14 days.", "If general anesthesia is required, inform the anesthesiologist that you are taking this medication, and discontinue the treatment 24 or 48 hours prior to surgery.", "Inform your physician in the event of renal impairment."]}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:50:56.005	stablon-12-5mg-tablets-for-major-depressive-episodes-2-blisters-x-15-tablets	17
1735	Klenzit-C (Adapalene 0.1% & Clindamycin 1% w/w) Topical Gel for Acne Vulgaris (15g Tube)	P02736	\N	\N	Glenmark Pharmaceuticals Ltd.	India	137349.00	114000.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/ecommerce/20250728082912-0-P02736.png?versionId=gn8XehlVJki6jC5qnlH.ZODhIq4WNEsb	Topical combination therapy containing Adapalene and Clindamycin phosphate indicated for the topical treatment of mild to moderate acne vulgaris characterized by comedones, papules, and pustules.	{"indications": ["Klenzit-C is indicated for the topical treatment of acne vulgaris in patients with mild to moderate severity, particularly where comedones, papules, and pustules predominate."], "sideEffects": ["Erythema, scaling, dry skin, pruritus, and burning sensation occurring in 10% to 40% of patients.", "Pruritus and burning immediately following application are frequently observed.", "Skin irritation, skin pain/stinging, erythema, severe sunburn, and acne flare-ups reported in approximately 1% or less of patients.", "These adverse reactions are most common during the first month of treatment and progressively decrease in frequency and severity thereafter.", "All adverse effects associated with the use of Adapalene and Clindamycin in clinical trials were reversible upon discontinuation of treatment."], "drugInteractions": [{"drug": "Other topical products with high potential for irritation (such as medicated soaps, harsh cleansers, soaps and cosmetics with strong drying effects, products with high alcohol concentrations, astringents, spices, or alkalis)", "effect": "May increase the risk of cumulative local irritation."}, {"drug": "Preparations containing sulfur, resorcinol, or salicylic acid", "effect": "Particular caution is required when used concurrently; allow the effects of such agents to subside before initiating Klenzit-C therapy."}, {"drug": "Neuromuscular blocking agents", "effect": "Clindamycin has been shown to have neuromuscular blocking properties that may enhance the action of other neuromuscular blocking agents."}], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Glenmark", "origin": "India", "storage": "Store below 30°C. Do not freeze. Keep out of reach of children.", "packaging": "Box of 1 tube (15g).", "manufacturer": "Glenmark Pharmaceuticals Ltd."}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Apply once daily at bedtime.", "missedDose": "[object Object]", "administration": "Apply a thin film of gel to clean, dry affected areas once daily at bedtime. Avoid simultaneous application of other potentially irritating topical medications. During the initial weeks of therapy, an apparent exacerbation of acne may occur; this is due to the action of the medication on previously unseen microcomedones and should not be considered a reason to discontinue treatment. Therapeutic results are typically observed after 8 to 12 weeks of consistent use.", "overdoseManagement": "KLENZIT-C Gel is intended for external topical use only. Excessive application will not yield faster or better results and may lead to marked redness, peeling, or cutaneous discomfort. The acute oral toxicity of Adapalene in mice and rats is greater than 10 mg/kg. Chronic oral ingestion of Adapalene may lead to systemic side effects similar to those observed with excessive oral vitamin A intake. Topical application of Clindamycin may result in systemic absorption sufficient to produce systemic adverse effects."}, "generalDescription": "Klenzit-C is a topical dermatological gel formulated for the treatment of acne vulgaris, combining two active pharmaceutical ingredients: Adapalene (a retinoid) and Clindamycin Phosphate (a lincosamide antibiotic).", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Disodium edetate, Carbomer 940, Propylene glycol, Methylparaben, Phenoxyethanol, Poloxamer 407, Sodium hydroxide, Purified water q.s.", "activeIngredients": "Each gram of gel contains: Adapalene USP 1 mg, Clindamycin Phosphate USP equivalent to Clindamycin 10 mg."}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "Clinical studies of Adapalene did not include sufficient numbers of subjects aged 65 and over to determine whether they respond differently from younger patients. Other reported clinical experience has not identified differences in responses between elderly and younger patients. Furthermore, acne vulgaris is predominantly a condition of adolescence and young adulthood, rendering treatment in geriatric populations generally unnecessary.", "lactation": "[object Object]", "pediatric": "Safety and effectiveness of the Adapalene and Clindamycin combination in pediatric patients below the age of 12 years have not been established; therefore, use in this age group is not recommended.", "pregnancy": "[object Object]"}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Because Adapalene may cause local irritation, concomitant use of other potentially irritating topical products (such as medicated soaps, harsh cleansers, cosmetics with strong drying effects, high-alcohol preparations, astringents, or alkalis) should be approached with caution. Special care must be taken when using preparations containing sulfur, resorcinol, or salicylic acid concurrently with Klenzit-C gel; allow previous treatments to clear before starting therapy. Clindamycin exhibits neuromuscular blocking properties and should be used with caution in patients receiving concurrent neuromuscular blocking agents, as it may potentiate their action."]}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:50:59.328	klenzit-c-adapalene-0-1percent-and-clindamycin-1percent-w-w-topical-gel-for-acne-vulgaris-15g-tube	258
1740	Rosuvastatin STELLA 10mg Film-Coated Tablets for Hypercholesterolemia (3 Blisters x 10 Tablets)	P02588	\N	\N	Stella Pharm	Vietnam	107059.00	91000.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/ecommerce/20250728082752-0-P02588.png?versionId=e5QHXG1dQVtzzkBIlk6TU8ZP6grkq1v7	Rosuvastatin STELLA 10mg film-coated tablets indicated for the treatment of hypercholesterolemia, packaged in 3 blisters of 10 tablets.	{"sideEffects": ["Endocrine disorders: Diabetes mellitus, hypertension, increased HbA1c.", "Nervous system disorders: Headache, dizziness.", "Gastrointestinal disorders: Constipation, nausea, abdominal pain.", "Musculoskeletal and connective tissue disorders: Myalgia.", "General disorders: Asthenia, cognitive impairment (such as memory loss, confusion, etc.).", "Skin and subcutaneous tissue disorders: Pruritus, rash, and urticaria.", "Immune system disorders: Hypersensitivity reactions including angioedema.", "Gastrointestinal disorders: Pancreatitis.", "Musculoskeletal and connective tissue disorders: Myopathy (including myositis), rhabdomyolysis."], "drugInteractions": [{"drug": "Ciclosporin", "effect": "When ciclosporin is co-administered with rosuvastatin, rosuvastatin AUC values are on average 7 times higher than those seen in healthy volunteers, while plasma concentrations of ciclosporin are unaffected."}, {"drug": "Vitamin K antagonists (such as warfarin or other coumarin anticoagulants)", "effect": "The initiation of treatment or dose escalation of rosuvastatin in patients concomitantly treated with vitamin K antagonists may result in an increase in International Normalized Ratio (INR). Discontinuation or reduction of rosuvastatin may result in a decrease in INR."}, {"drug": "Ezetimibe", "effect": "Concomitant use of rosuvastatin and ezetimibe does not result in a change in AUC or Cmax of either drug. However, a pharmacodynamic interaction, in terms of adverse effects, cannot be ruled out."}, {"drug": "Gemfibrozil and other lipid-lowering medications", "effect": "Concomitant use of rosuvastatin and gemfibrozil results in a 2-fold increase in rosuvastatin Cmax and AUC. The 40 mg dose is contraindicated when combined with fibrates."}, {"drug": "HIV protease inhibitors (atazanavir, atazanavir/ritonavir, and lopinavir/ritonavir)", "effect": "Co-administration with rosuvastatin results in a approximately 3-fold increase in rosuvastatin exposure."}, {"drug": "Antacids", "effect": "Simultaneous dosing of an antacid with rosuvastatin results in a 20% decrease in rosuvastatin AUC and a 30% decrease in Cmax."}, {"drug": "Oral contraceptives / Hormone Replacement Therapy (HRT)", "effect": "Concomitant use of rosuvastatin and an oral contraceptive resulted in an increase in ethinyl estradiol AUC of 26% and norgestrel AUC of 34%."}, {"drug": "Cytochrome P450 enzymes", "effect": "Results from in vitro and in vivo studies show that rosuvastatin is neither an inhibitor nor an inducer of cytochrome P450 enzymes. Furthermore, rosuvastatin is a poor substrate for these isoenzymes. Therefore, pharmacokinetic interactions resulting from enzyme induction or inhibition are unlikely."}], "effectsOnDriving": "Studies to determine the effect of rosuvastatin on the ability to drive and use machines have not been performed. However, based on its pharmacodynamic properties, rosuvastatin is unlikely to affect this ability. When driving vehicles or operating machinery, it should be noted that dizziness may occur during treatment.", "contraindications": ["Patients with hypersensitivity to any component of the medication.", "Patients with active liver disease including unexplained persistent elevations of serum transaminases and any serum transaminase elevation exceeding 3 times the upper limit of normal (ULN).", "Patients with severe renal impairment (creatinine clearance < 30 mL/min).", "Patients with myopathy.", "Pregnant and lactating women, and women of childbearing potential not employing appropriate contraceptive measures."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Stellapharm", "origin": "Vietnam", "storage": "Store in a tight container in a dry place. Temperature not exceeding 30°C.", "packaging": "10 tablets per blister. Box of 3 blisters.", "manufacturer": "Stellapharm (Vietnam)"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "The usual starting dose is 5 to 10 mg once daily, depending on plasma cholesterol levels, cardiovascular risk factors, and risk factors for adverse reactions. If necessary, the dose may be adjusted at 4-week intervals to the usual maximum dose of 20 mg once daily. The 40 mg dose may be administered under specialist supervision in patients with severe hypercholesterolemia. Elderly patients, Asian patients, and patients with predisposing factors for myopathy should initiate therapy at 5 mg. Patients taking ciclosporin should be limited to 5 mg once daily, and those taking gemfibrozil or ritonavir-boosted lopinavir should be limited to 10 mg once daily. Patients with severe hypercholesterolemia, such as homozygous familial hypercholesterolemia, may start with 20 mg once daily. Patients with renal impairment (creatinine clearance between 30 and 60 mL/min) should start at 5 mg once daily with a maximum dose of 20 mg once daily. When combined with atazanavir, atazanavir/ritonavir, or lopinavir/ritonavir, rosuvastatin dosage is limited to a maximum of 10 mg once daily. Note: The dosages above are for reference only. Specific dosing depends on the patient's condition and disease progression. Consult a physician or healthcare professional for appropriate dosing.", "missedDose": "Take the missed dose as soon as remembered. However, if it is almost time for the next dose, skip the missed dose and resume the normal dosing schedule. Do not double the dose to make up for a forgotten dose.", "administration": "Rosuvastatin STELLA 10mg is taken orally, as a single dose at any time of the day, with or without food. Patients should be placed on a standard cholesterol-lowering diet before receiving rosuvastatin and should continue this diet during treatment. Dosage may be adjusted carefully based on individual patient needs and therapeutic response by titrating the dose at intervals of no less than 4 weeks. Adverse drug reactions must be closely monitored, particularly adverse musculoskeletal effects.", "overdoseManagement": "There is no specific treatment in the event of an overdose. In the event of overdose, symptomatic treatment and supportive measures should be employed as required. Liver function and creatine kinase levels should be monitored. Hemodialysis is unlikely to be of benefit."}, "generalDescription": "Rosuvastatin STELLA 10mg, manufactured by Stellapharm Joint Venture Co., Ltd. - Branch 1, contains rosuvastatin 10 mg as its active ingredient. It is a lipid-modifying agent, specifically an HMG-CoA reductase inhibitor. The tablets are round, light red, film-coated, scored on one side and plain on the other.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Lactose monohydrate, microcrystalline cellulose, magnesium stearate, crospovidone, anhydrous dibasic calcium phosphate, hypromellose, polyethylene glycol 6000, talc, titanium dioxide, iron oxide red.", "activeIngredients": "Rosuvastatin 10mg (Equivalent to rosuvastatin calcium 10.4mg)"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "Elderly patients (> 70 years) have predisposing factors for rhabdomyolysis and require caution.", "lactation": "Contraindicated. Rosuvastatin is excreted in the milk of rats. Data on excretion in human milk are not available.", "pediatric": "[object Object]", "pregnancy": "Contraindicated. Since cholesterol and other products of cholesterol biosynthesis are essential for the development of the fetus, the potential risk from inhibition of HMG-CoA reductase outweighs the advantage of treatment during pregnancy."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Creatine kinase (CK) should be monitored in the following situations: Renal impairment, hypothyroidism, personal or family history of hereditary muscular disorders, previous history of muscular toxicity with another statin or fibrate, history of liver disease and/or substantial alcohol consumption, elderly patients (> 70 years) with predisposing factors for rhabdomyolysis, situations where an increase in plasma concentration may occur, and in special patient populations. If CK levels are significantly elevated (> 5 x ULN) at baseline, statin treatment should not be initiated.", "During statin treatment: Patients should report promptly any unexplained muscle pain, tenderness, or weakness. If these symptoms occur, CK levels should be evaluated for appropriate medical intervention.", "Musculoskeletal effects: Rhabdomyolysis has been reported more frequently in patients receiving rosuvastatin at a 40 mg dose compared to lower doses. Discontinue rosuvastatin if marked elevation of serum CK levels occurs or if myopathy is diagnosed or suspected. Caution should be exercised in patients over 65 years of age, patients with uncontrolled hypothyroidism, and patients with renal impairment. Patients must promptly report any signs or symptoms of muscle pain, fatigue, fever, dark urine, nausea, or vomiting during treatment.", "Hepatic effects: Liver enzymes tests should be performed prior to initiating statin therapy and as clinically indicated thereafter.", "Renal effects: Dose reduction should be considered in patients taking the 40 mg dose who exhibit unexplained persistent proteinuria during routine urinalysis.", "Concomitant use of lipid-lowering statins with medications for HIV and hepatitis C virus (HCV) treatment may increase the risk of muscle injury, most seriously rhabdomyolysis, leading to secondary renal failure and potential fatalities.", "Rosuvastatin STELLA 10mg contains lactose. Patients with rare hereditary problems of galactose intolerance, total lactase deficiency, or glucose-galactose malabsorption should not take this medication."], "adverseReactionManagement": "If experiencing any adverse drug reactions, discontinue use and notify a physician or visit the nearest medical facility for timely management."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:51:16.052	rosuvastatin-stella-10mg-film-coated-tablets-for-hypercholesterolemia-3-blisters-x-10-tablets	39
