m light, at a temperature not exceeding 30°C", "packaging": "Box of 1 blister x 4 Tablets", "manufacturer": "Davipharm (Vietnam)"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Adults and children over 5 years of age: Administer a single dose of 0.15 mg/kg. Higher doses increase adverse reactions without improving therapeutic efficacy. Annual retreatment with the above dosage is required to ensure control of Onchocerca volvulus microfilariae. If patients have heavy ocular microfilarial loads, more frequent retreatment (e.g., every 6 months) may be necessary.\\nRecommended dosage guidelines for ivermectin in the treatment of Onchocerca infection (single oral dose based on body weight): 15 - 25 kg: 3 mg; 26 - 44 kg: 6 mg; 45 - 64 kg: 9 mg; 65 - 84 kg: 12 mg; > 85 kg: 0.15 mg/kg.", "missedDose": "[object Object]", "administration": "Administer ivermectin orally with water early in the morning on an empty stomach, or at another time, but avoid food intake within 2 hours before and after administration.", "overdoseManagement": "[object Object]"}, "generalDescription": "Pizar 6mg is an anthelmintic medication containing ivermectin as the active ingredient. In addition to treating onchocerciasis, the medication is highly effective in the treatment of intestinal strongyloidiasis caused by Strongyloides stercoralis.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Cellactose 80, magnesium stearate, croscarmellose sodium.", "activeIngredients": "Ivermectin 6mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "[object Object]", "lactation": "Ivermectin is excreted in breast milk in low concentrations (less than 2% of the administered dose). Safety in newborns has not been established; therefore, the medication should only be administered to nursing mothers when the potential benefits outweigh the risks to the infant.", "pediatric": "Safety and effectiveness in children under 5 years of age have not been established.", "pregnancy": "Ivermectin may be used after the first trimester of pregnancy."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Clinical experience in children under 5 years of age is limited; therefore, use in this age group is not recommended.", "Because ivermectin potentiates GABA, it is theorized to affect the central nervous system in patients with compromised blood-brain barriers (such as in meningitis or Trypanosoma infection).", "When treating onchodermatitis with ivermectin, hyperreactive-type reactions may occur, potentially leading to more severe adverse effects, particularly edema and exacerbation of the condition.", "Keep out of reach of children."], "adverseReactionManagement": "Report any adverse reactions experienced during the use of the medication to your healthcare provider."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:51:26.56	pizar-6mg-tablets-for-helminthiasis-and-onchocerciasis-1-blister-x-4-tablets	112
