acetaminophen."}, {"drug": "Probenecid", "effect": "May reduce the elimination of acetaminophen and increase its plasma half-life."}, {"drug": "CYP1A2 Substrates (such as Clozapine) or Inducers/Inhibitors of this Isoenzyme", "effect": "Caffeine has the potential for pharmacokinetic interactions."}], "effectsOnDriving": "Since dizziness may occur, caution should be exercised during activities such as driving, operating machinery, working at heights, and other hazardous tasks.", "pharmacodynamics": {"mechanismOfAction": "Paracetamol acts on the hypothalamic heat-regulating center to cause antipyresis, vasodilation, and increased peripheral blood flow; it inhibits prostaglandin synthesis in the central nervous system. Caffeine acts as a central nervous system stimulant, constricting cerebral blood vessels and enhancing the analgesic potency of paracetamol."}, "pharmacokinetics": {"absorption": "Paracetamol is rapidly and almost completely absorbed from the gastrointestinal tract. Peak plasma concentrations occur 30 to 60 minutes after oral administration. Caffeine is also rapidly and completely absorbed.", "metabolism": "Paracetamol is metabolized primarily in the liver via cytochrome P450 enzyme pathways, forming minor hepatotoxic intermediate metabolites conjugated by hepatic glutathione. Caffeine is metabolized extensively in the liver by oxidation, demethylation, and acetylation.", "elimination": "Paracetamol is excreted primarily in the urine mainly as glucuronide and sulfate conjugates. Caffeine is eliminated principally via urinary excretion of its metabolites, with a plasma half-life of approximately 3 to 7 hours."}, "contraindications": ["Patients with hypersensitivity to any component of the medication.", "Patients with severe hepatic impairment.", "Patients with glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase (G6PD) deficiency.", "Children under 12 years of age."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Tydol Plus", "origin": "Vietnam", "storage": "Store at temperatures below 30°C, in a dry place, protected from light.", "packaging": "Box of 10 blisters x 10 tablets", "manufacturer": "Domestic Pharmaceutical Manufacturer"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Adults and children over 12 years: Oral dose of 1 to 2 tablets every 6 hours as symptoms persist. Do not exceed 8 tablets per 24 hours, or as directed by a physician. Note: The dosage provided is for reference only. The specific dosage depends on the patient's physical condition and disease severity. Consult a physician or healthcare professional for an appropriate dosage regimen.", "missedDose": "If a dose is missed, take it as soon as remembered. However, if it is nearly time for the next dose, skip the missed dose and resume the normal dosing schedule. Do not double the dose.", "administration": "Tydol Plus tablets are administered orally.", "overdoseManagement": "Acetaminophen: Symptoms include nausea, vomiting, and abdominal pain occurring within 2 to 3 hours after toxic ingestion. Methemoglobinemia leading to cyanosis of the skin, mucous membranes, and nail beds is a characteristic sign of acute p-aminophenol derivative toxicity. Central nervous system stimulation, agitation, and delirium may occur initially, followed by CNS depression, stupor, hypothermia, tachypnea, tachycardia, hypotension, and circulatory failure. Management: Early diagnosis is critical. Gastric lavage should be performed ideally within 4 hours of ingestion. The primary specific antidote is N-acetylcysteine, administered orally or intravenously, most effective if given within 10 hours of ingestion. Methionine may be used as an alternative. Activated charcoal and/or saline cathartics may also reduce absorption. Caffeine: Symptoms include gastrointestinal pain, mild delirium, insomnia, diuresis, dehydration, and fever. Severe symptoms include cardiac arrhythmias and tonic-clonic seizures. Management: Symptomatic and supportive care, gastric emptying, administration of activated charcoal, and anticonvulsants such as diazepam if necessary."}, "generalDescription": "Tydol Plus is an Over-The-Counter (OTC) medication commonly used for mild pain relief and fever reduction. This medication combines two primary active ingredients: Paracetamol, which provides effective analgesic and antipyretic effects, and Caffeine, which acts as an adjuvant to enhance the analgesic efficacy of paracetamol and increases alertness.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Pregelatinized starch, lactose monohydrate, colloidal anhydrous silica, sodium starch glycolate, maize starch, povidone K30, talc, magnesium stearate, Opadry II white, Ponceau 4R lake.", "activeIngredients": "Paracetamol 500mg, Caffeine 65mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "Use with caution; dose adjustment may be necessary based on renal and hepatic function.", "lactation": "Caffeine is excreted in breast milk and may cause stimulant effects in nursing infants; therefore, this medication should not be used by nursing mothers.", "pediatric": "Contraindicated in children under 12 years of age.", "pregnancy": "Acetaminophen-caffeine combination is not recommended during pregnancy due to potential risks of low birth weight and spontaneous abortion associated with caffeine."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Physicians should warn patients about signs of serious, potentially fatal skin reactions including Stevens-Johnson syndrome, Toxic Epidermal Necrolysis (TEN), Lyell's syndrome, and Acute Generalized Exanthematous Pustulosis (AGEP).", "Patients must discontinue acetaminophen and seek immediate medical attention upon the first appearance of skin rash or any other sign of hypersensitivity. Patients with a history of hypersensitivity reactions should not use products containing acetaminophen.", "Blood dyscrasias including thrombocytopenia, leukopenia, and pancytopenia have been reported with p-aminophenol derivatives, especially during prolonged use of large doses.", "Exercise caution when administering acetaminophen to patients with preexisting anemia, hepatic impairment, renal impairment, alcoholism, chronic malnutrition, or dehydration.", "Avoid excessive alcohol consumption during treatment due to increased hepatotoxicity risks.", "Avoid excessive caffeine consumption (coffee, tea) while taking this medication.", "This medication contains lactose; patients with rare hereditary problems of galactose intolerance, Lapp lactase deficiency, or glucose-galactose malabsorption should not take this medicine.", "This medication contains Ponceau 4R lake, which may cause allergic reactions."], "adverseReactionManagement": "If adverse effects occur, discontinue use immediately, notify your doctor, or go to the nearest medical facility for prompt management."}	f	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:51:43.705	tydol-plus-500mg-65mg-tablets-for-mild-pain-relief-and-fever-reduction-10-blisters-x-10-tablets	382
