ol, Propafenone, Quinidine, and Selective Serotonin Reuptake Inhibitors [SSRIs])", "effect": "Risk of increasing serum concentrations of dextromethorphan, leading to enhanced adverse effects."}, {"drug": "Alcohol", "effect": "Avoid concurrent use due to the risk of increased central nervous system depression and psychomotor impairment."}], "effectsOnDriving": "Avoid administering this medication to patients who drive vehicles or operate machinery, as the product may cause drowsiness, somnolence, and dizziness.", "contraindications": ["Hypersensitivity to any of the active ingredients or excipients in this medication.", "Pregnant and lactating women.", "Children under 4 years of age.", "Patients currently receiving Monoamine Oxidase Inhibitors (MAOIs) or within 14 weeks of stopping such treatment."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Imexpharm", "origin": "Vietnam", "storage": "Store below 30°C, protect from moisture and light.", "packaging": "Box of 10 blisters x 10 Soft Capsules", "manufacturer": "Imexpharm Corporation (Vietnam)"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Adults and children aged 6 years and older: Take 1 capsule 2 times daily. Children aged 4 to under 6 years: Take 1 capsule daily. Children under 4 years of age: The dosage form and strength of this medication are not suitable for children under 4 years old. Note: The above dosages are for reference only. The specific dosage depends on the patient's constitution and the severity of the condition. Consult a physician or healthcare professional for an appropriate dosage regimen.", "missedDose": "If you miss a dose of Cidetuss, take it as soon as possible. However, if it is almost time for your next dose, skip the missed dose and resume your regular dosing schedule. Do not double the dose to make up for a forgotten dose.", "administration": "Cidetuss cough capsules are administered orally, before or after meals.", "overdoseManagement": "In the event of a Cidetuss overdose, the potential contribution of each component (guaifenesin, cetirizine, or dextromethorphan) must be evaluated for appropriate management.\\nGuaifenesin: Symptoms: Ingestion of doses higher than therapeutic levels may cause nausea and vomiting. Management: Gastric lavage if detected early, along with symptomatic treatment.\\nCetirizine: Symptoms: The most frequent symptom of cetirizine overdose is somnolence in adults; agitation may occur in children. In severe overdose, induce emesis and perform gastric lavage, alongside supportive measures. There is currently no specific antidote.\\nDextromethorphan: Symptoms: Nausea, vomiting, somnolence, blurred vision, nystagmus, urinary retention, stupor, hallucinations, ataxia, respiratory depression, and convulsions. Management: Supportive care, intravenous administration of naloxone (2 mg), and repeated doses if necessary, up to a total dose of 10 mg."}, "generalDescription": "Cidetuss 100mg is a pharmaceutical preparation utilized for the management and treatment of respiratory conditions, specifically designed to suppress dry or irritative coughs, loosen phlegm and bronchial secretions, and relieve allergic symptoms such as sneezing and rhinorrhea.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Lecithin, Beeswax, Soybean Oil, Gelatin, Glycerin, Vanillin, Titanium Dioxide, L-Lysine HCl, Citric Acid, FD&C Yellow No. 5, FD&C Yellow No. 6, Patent Blue V.", "activeIngredients": "Each soft capsule contains: Guaifenesin 100mg, Cetirizine Dihydrochloride 5mg, Dextromethorphan Hydrobromide 15mg."}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "Due to insufficient clinical data regarding the excretion of this medication in breast milk, administration during lactation should be avoided to ensure infant safety. If use is essential, consult a physician to weigh potential benefits against risks.", "pregnancy": "Due to insufficient clinical safety data regarding the use of this medication in pregnant women, administration during pregnancy should be avoided to ensure fetal safety. If use is essential, consult a physician to carefully weigh potential benefits against risks."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Exercise caution when administering the medication to patients with excessive sputum production, prolonged or chronic coughs associated with smoking, asthma, pneumothorax, chronic bronchitis, pulmonary emphysema, or respiratory impairment.", "Dosage adjustment is required in patients with hepatic impairment, moderate-to-severe renal impairment, or patients undergoing hemodialysis.", "Avoid use in patients with porphyria, as guaifenesin has been shown to induce porphyrin metabolism in animal models.", "Use with caution in patients at risk for or experiencing respiratory depression.", "Avoid concomitant use with alcohol and other central nervous system depressants.", "Abuse of guaifenesin-containing products may lead to nephrolithiasis.", "Abuse and dependence on dextromethorphan may occur (though rare), particularly with high-dose use.", "Patients must maintain adequate hydration during treatment. Do not self-administer for more than 7 days without consulting a physician."]}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:51:50.324	cidetuss-100mg-capsules-for-cough-cold-and-allergic-rhinitis-10-blisters-x-10-soft-capsules	83
