pairment (Child-Pugh score - 10).", "missedDose": "If a dose is missed, take it as soon as possible. However, if it is almost time for the next dose, skip the missed dose and resume the regular dosing schedule. Do not double the dose to make up for a forgotten one.", "administration": "Magrax-F is administered orally.", "overdoseManagement": "No clinical reports of etoricoxib overdose are available. In the event of an overdose, standard supportive measures should be employed, such as removing unabsorbed medication from the gastrointestinal tract, clinical monitoring, and supportive therapy as indicated. Etoricoxib is not dialyzable via hemodialysis."}, "generalDescription": "Magrax-F is manufactured by Dat Vi Phu Pharmaceutical Joint Stock Company with Etoricoxib as the active ingredient, serving as a medication used for the treatment of acute gout attacks.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Microcrystalline cellulose, lactose monohydrate, povidone, sodium starch glycolate, sodium lauryl sulfate, magnesium stearate, hydroxypropyl methylcellulose, talc, titanium dioxide, polyethylene glycol 6000, green mint dye, sunset yellow dye, brilliant blue dye... q.s. 1 tablet.", "activeIngredients": "Etoricoxib 120mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "Use with caution.", "lactation": "It is unknown whether the medication is excreted in human breast milk. A decision must be made whether to discontinue breastfeeding or discontinue the medication.", "pediatric": "Contraindicated in children under 16 years of age.", "pregnancy": "Avoid use during late pregnancy. Use during the first two trimesters only if the potential benefit outweighs the potential risk to the fetus."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Exercise caution in patients with ischemic heart disease, renal impairment, cirrhosis, left ventricular dysfunction, hypertension, predisposition to fluid retention, elderly patients, dehydrated patients, hyperlipidemia, and diabetes mellitus. When using the high dose of 1