31	Diane-35 Tablets, Cyproterone Acetate 2 mg / Ethinylestradiol 0.035 mg, Oral Contraceptive and Anti-Androgenic Agent (1 Blister Pack x 21 Tablets)	P00118	\N	\N	Bayer	Germany	161310.00	135500.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/ecommerce/20250520034601-0-P00118.png?versionId=yCzoTN.wmf535x5aYb1hi209_dbfJyEs	Diane-35 Tablets (1 blister pack x 21 tablets) containing cyproterone acetate and ethinylestradiol for oral contraception, treatment of severe acne, and management of hirsutism in women.	{"indications": ["Treatment of severe acne and excessive hair growth (hirsutism) in women of reproductive age, as well as providing oral contraception."], "sideEffects": ["Nausea, abdominal pain", "Vomiting, diarrhea", "Contact lens intolerance", "Hypersensitivity reactions", "Weight gain", "Weight loss", "Fluid retention, edema", "Headache", "Migraine", "Depressive moods, mood alterations", "Decreased libido", "Increased libido", "Breast pain, breast tenderness", "Breast enlargement", "Vaginal discharge, breast discharge", "Rash, urticaria", "Erythema nodosum, erythema multiforme", "Venous thromboembolism", "Arterial thromboembolism", "Cerebrovascular accident", "Hypertension", "Hypertriglyceridemia", "Changes in glucose tolerance and peripheral insulin resistance", "Liver tumors (benign and malignant)", "Liver function disorders, cholestatic jaundice", "Chloasma (melasma)"], "drugInteractions": [{"drug": "Hepatic enzyme inducers (e.g., phenytoin, barbiturates, primidone, carbamazepine, rifampicin, oxcarbazepine, topiramate, felbamate, ritonavir, griseofulvin, and herbal preparations containing St. John's wort)", "effect": "May increase the clearance of sex hormones, resulting in breakthrough bleeding, menstrual irregularities, and/or potential loss of contraceptive efficacy."}, {"drug": "HIV/HCV protease inhibitors and non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors", "effect": "May clinically significantly increase or decrease plasma concentrations of estrogens or progestins."}, {"drug": "Cyclosporin", "effect": "Combination estrogens and progestogens like Diane-35 may increase plasma and tissue concentrations of cyclosporin."}, {"drug": "Lamotrigine", "effect": "Combination estrogens and progestogens like Diane-35 may induce the clearance of lamotrigine, resulting in clinically relevant reductions in plasma lamotrigine concentrations."}], "effectsOnDriving": "No studies on the effects on the ability to drive and use machines have been performed. No adverse effects on driving performance or machinery operation have been observed in users of combined oral contraceptives like Diane-35.", "contraindications": ["Combination estrogen-progestogen preparations should not be used in the presence of any of the conditions listed below. If any of these conditions develops for the first time during the use of Diane-35, the product should be discontinued immediately.", "Presence or history of arterial or venous thrombotic/thromboembolic events (e.g., deep vein thrombosis, pulmonary embolism, myocardial infarction) or cerebrovascular accident.", "Presence or history of prodromal signs of thrombosis (e.g., transient ischemic attack, angina pectoris).", "High risk or multiple risk factors for arterial or venous thrombosis, such as diabetes mellitus with vascular involvement, severe hypertension, or severe dyslipoproteinemia.", "Genetic or acquired predisposition for venous or arterial thrombosis, such as activated protein C (APC) resistance, antithrombin-III deficiency, protein C deficiency, protein S deficiency, hyperhomocysteinemia, and antiphospholipid antibodies (anticardiolipin antibodies, lupus anticoagulant).", "History of migraine with focal neurological symptoms.", "Severe hepatic disease as long as liver function values have not returned to normal.", "Presence or history of liver tumors (benign or malignant).", "Known or suspected sex-hormone-dependent malignancies (e.g., of the genital organs or the breasts).", "Undiagnosed abnormal vaginal bleeding.", "Concomitant use with other hormonal contraceptives.", "Known or suspected pregnancy.", "Breastfeeding.", "Hypersensitivity to ethinylestradiol, cyproterone acetate, or any of the excipients.", "Diane-35 is contraindicated for use in males."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Bayer HealthCare Pharmaceuticals", "origin": "Germany", "storage": "Store below 30°C in a dry place, protected from light and moisture.", "packaging": "Blister pack of 21 tablets. Box of 1 blister pack.", "manufacturer": "Bayer AG (Germany)"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Diane-35 must be taken regularly to ensure both therapeutic efficacy and contraceptive protection. The dosage regimen corresponds to the conventional dosing schedule of most combined oral contraceptives. The duration of treatment depends on the severity of symptoms and clinical response, generally requiring at least 3 months. Acne and seborrhea typically resolve faster than hirsutism. The treating physician should periodically re-evaluate the necessity of continued therapy.", "missedDose": "If the user is less than 12 hours late in taking any tablet, contraceptive protection is not reduced. The missed tablet should be taken as soon as remembered, and subsequent tablets taken at the usual time. If delayed by more than 12 hours, contraceptive protection may be reduced. The management of missed tablets follows two primary rules: 1) Tablet-taking must never be interrupted for more than 7 days; 2) 7 days of uninterrupted tablet intake are required to achieve adequate suppression of the hypothalamic-pituitary-ovarian axis.", "administration": "Take the tablets orally with a small amount of liquid in the exact order indicated on the blister pack at approximately the same time every day. Take one tablet daily for 21 consecutive days. Each subsequent pack is initiated after a 7-day tablet-free interval, during which a withdrawal bleeding typically occurs, usually beginning 2-3 days after taking the last tablet. \\nInitiation of Diane-35:\\n- No preceding hormonal contraception in the past month: Tablet intake must commence on Day 1 of the patient's natural menstrual cycle. Initiation on Days 2-5 is permissible, but an additional barrier method of contraception is recommended for the first 7 days of tablet-taking.\\n- Switching from a combined oral contraceptive (COC), vaginal ring, or transdermal patch: Preferably start Diane-35 on the day following the last active tablet of the previous COC, or at the latest following the usual tablet-free or inactive tablet interval. For a vaginal ring or transdermal patch, start on the day of removal or at the latest when the next application is due.\\n- Switching from a progestogen-only method (minipill, injection, implant) or intrauterine system (IUS): Women may switch on any day from the minipill, on the day of removal for an implant or IUS, or on the day the next injection is due, utilizing an additional barrier method for the first 7 days.\\n- Following first-trimester abortion: May be initiated immediately without additional contraceptive measures.\\n- Following delivery or second-trimester abortion: For postpartum women not breastfeeding, initiate between Days 21 and 28 post-delivery. If started later, use an additional barrier method for the first 7 days, and exclude pregnancy prior to initiation if intercourse has occurred.\\nIn the event of severe gastrointestinal disturbances, absorption may be incomplete, and auxiliary contraceptive measures should be implemented. If vomiting occurs within 3-4 hours of tablet ingestion, the guidance for missed tablets applies.", "overdoseManagement": "There are no reports of serious adverse outcomes from acute overdose. Symptoms of overdose in adults and adolescents may include nausea, vomiting, breast tenderness, dizziness, drowsiness/fatigue, and withdrawal bleeding in young females. There is no specific antidote, and treatment should be entirely symptomatic and supportive."}, "generalDescription": "Diane-35 tablets are a fixed-dose combination oral medication containing the anti-androgen cyproterone acetate and the estrogen ethinylestradiol. It is indicated for the treatment of androgen-dependent diseases in women, such as acne, particularly pronounced forms and those associated with seborrhea or with mild forms of hirsutism, while simultaneously providing effective oral contraception.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Lactose monohydrate, maize starch, povidone 25,000, magnesium stearate, sucrose, povidone 700,000, macrogol 6000, precipitated calcium carbonate, talc, glycerol 85%, titanium dioxide, iron oxide yellow, montan glycol wax.", "activeIngredients": "Ethinylestradiol 0.035 mg and Cyproterone acetate 2 mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "Not applicable. Diane-35 is not indicated for use after menopause.", "lactation": "Contraindicated during lactation. Cyproterone acetate and ethinylestradiol metabolites are excreted in human breast milk in small amounts.", "pediatric": "Diane-35 is indicated exclusively after menarche. Safety and efficacy have been established in women of reproductive age.", "pregnancy": "Contraindicated during pregnancy. If pregnancy occurs during treatment with Diane-35, administration must be halted immediately."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Diane-35 contains the progestogen cyproterone acetate and the estrogen ethinylestradiol, presenting a pharmacological profile similar to combined oral contraceptives (COCs).", "Epidemiological studies indicate an increased relative risk of arterial and venous thrombotic and thromboembolic disorders, such as deep vein thrombosis, pulmonary embolism, myocardial infarction, and cerebrovascular accidents, associated with COC use.", "The risk of venous thromboembolism (VTE) is highest during the first year of use, upon restarting, or switching back after a break of 4 weeks or longer.", "The frequency of VTE in users of Diane-35 is estimated to be 1.5 to 2 times higher than in users of levonorgestrel-containing COCs.", "Women presenting with progressive hirsutism or severe signs of androgenization must undergo differential diagnosis to exclude androgen-producing tumors or adrenal enzyme defects.", "Each tablet contains 31 mg of lactose monohydrate; patients with rare hereditary galactose intolerance, total lactase deficiency, or glucose-galactose malabsorption should consider this dietary load.", "A complete medical history and physical examination should be performed prior to initiating therapy and periodically monitored thereafter.", "Diane-35 does not protect against HIV infection (AIDS) or other sexually transmitted infections (STIs)."], "adverseReactionManagement": "Discontinue treatment immediately if severe adverse reactions or symptoms of thromboembolism occur, and consult a physician or seek emergency medical care."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:15:23.754	diane-35-tablets-cyproterone-acetate-2-mg-ethinylestradiol-0-035-mg-oral-contraceptive-and-anti	117
36	Axe Brand White Flower Analgesic Oil (Menthol 20g, Eucalyptus Oil 15g, Methyl Salicylate 15g, Camphor 5g) Topical Liquid for Cold, Dizziness, and Motion Sickness (10 mL Glass Bottle)	P00891	\N	\N	Leung Kai Fook Pharmaceutical Vietnam Co., Ltd. (Vietnam)	Vietnam	33735.00	28000.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/ecommerce/20250415090616-0-P00891.jpg?versionId=rD_edl3g4IR1H3qSS2hCis5xhUmMwJUF	Axe Brand White Flower Analgesic Oil is a topical medication indicated for the symptomatic relief of common cold, rhinitis, dizziness, motion sickness, nausea, abdominal pain, flatulence, backache, musculoskeletal fatigue, and insect bites. Contains Menthol, Eucalyptus Oil, Methyl Salicylate, and Camphor.	{"indications": ["Symptomatic treatment of common cold, rhinitis, dizziness, motion sickness, nausea, abdominal pain, flatulence, backache, musculoskeletal aches and pains, and insect bites."], "sideEffects": ["Systemic: Increased diaphoresis, decreased core body temperature.", "Local reactions: Erythematous irritation, burning sensation, and contact dermatitis at the application site."], "drugInteractions": [{"drug": "Warfarin and oral anticoagulants", "effect": "Excessive topical application of Axe Brand White Flower Analgesic Oil over large surface areas may enhance the percutaneous absorption of methyl salicylate, potentially increasing the risk of ecchymosis, subcutaneous hemorrhage, or elevated International Normalized Ratio (INR) in patients receiving anticoagulant therapy."}], "effectsOnDriving": "There is no clinical evidence or reports indicating that Axe Brand White Flower Analgesic Oil impairs the ability to drive or operate machinery.", "contraindications": ["Pregnant or lactating women, and neonates and infants under 30 months of age.", "Pediatric patients with a documented history of epilepsy, febrile seizures, or neurological disorders.", "Individuals with known hypersensitivity or allergic reactions to salicylates, aspirin, or any active or inactive excipients contained in the product."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Axe Brand", "origin": "Vietnam", "storage": "Store at controlled room temperatures below 30°C, protect from direct sunlight, and maintain in a dry environment.", "packaging": "White glass container enclosed in a paper carton with an accompanying package insert. Net volume: 10 mL of topical solution per bottle.", "manufacturer": "Leung Kai Fook Pharmaceutical Vietnam Co., Ltd. (Vietnam)"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "For acute symptoms such as common cold, dry cough, headache, rhinitis, motion sickness, nausea, abdominal pain, and flatulence: Apply and gently massage the medication onto both temples, nuchal region, abdomen, soles of the feet, and palms until a localized warming sensation is achieved. A minimal quantity may be applied near the external nares for inhalation. For backache, musculoskeletal fatigue, and insect bites: Apply sparingly to the affected dermatological area 2 to 3 times daily.", "missedDose": "If an application is missed, omit the missed dose and resume the standard application schedule as directed. Do not apply a double or excessive dose to compensate for a forgotten application.", "administration": "For external topical application only; strictly do not ingest.", "overdoseManagement": "In the event of systemic toxicity manifesting as nausea, emesis, central nervous system depression, or lethargy, immediately transfer the patient to the nearest medical emergency facility. Accidental ingestion of camphor and menthol can precipitate acute neurotoxicity. Notify attending medical personnel promptly for immediate supportive intervention. Management of salicylate toxicity: Perform gastric lavage or gastric aspiration accompanied by the administration of activated charcoal to minimize systemic toxin absorption. Alkalinize the urine via intravenous sodium bicarbonate infusion and administer supplemental potassium chloride as clinically indicated. Execute hemodialysis or exchange transfusion in severe poisoning cases. Management of camphor, menthol, and eucalyptus oil toxicity: Administer gastric lavage utilizing liquid paraffin followed by a saline cathartic. Provide symptomatic supportive care: Administer intravenous diazepam for seizure control, utilize atropine to diminish excessive bronchial secretions, and institute mechanical ventilatory support in the event of respiratory depression."}, "generalDescription": "Axe Brand White Flower Analgesic Oil is formulated for external topical application to manage symptoms associated with upper respiratory infections, minor musculoskeletal discomfort, motion sickness, and localized pruritus from insect bites. Active constituents include Menthol, Eucalyptus Oil, Methyl Salicylate, and Camphor, which act synergistically to induce local vasodilation, cooling sensations, and mild analgesia.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Essential Oils 12g, Liquid Paraffin quantity sufficient to 100g", "activeIngredients": "Menthol 20g, Eucalyptus Oil 15g, Methyl Salicylate 15g, Camphor 5g."}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "Use with caution in geriatric patients, applying moderate amounts to avoid excessive percutaneous absorption.", "lactation": "Contraindicated during lactation due to potential adverse effects on the nursing infant.", "pediatric": "Strictly contraindicated in infants and pediatric patients under 30 months of age. Precaution: Prevent nasal inhalation in infants.", "pregnancy": "Contraindicated during pregnancy due to systemic risks associated with methyl salicylate and camphor absorption."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Avoid accidental contact with the ocular structures, oral cavity, and mucosal membranes.", "Do not apply the medicinal preparation onto broken skin, lacerations, burns, or open wounds.", "Pediatric Precaution: Do not permit infants to inhale the product directly through the nares to avoid acute reflex apnea or laryngospasm.", "The formulation is not provided in single-dose packaging; apply conservatively in moderate quantities and avoid widespread application over extensive body surface areas."], "adverseReactionManagement": "If moderate to severe adverse dermatological or systemic reactions manifest, discontinue topical application immediately, cleanse the site thoroughly, and consult a physician or seek immediate medical evaluation at the nearest healthcare facility."}	f	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:15:30.457	axe-brand-white-flower-analgesic-oil-menthol-20g-eucalyptus-oil-15g-methyl-salicylate-15g-camphor	384
