], "effectsOnDriving": "Driving or operating machinery should be avoided after administration until it is established that performance is not impaired. The risk of impairment is increased when taken concomitantly with alcohol.", "pharmacodynamics": {"mechanismOfAction": "Acts indirectly to enhance the activity of gamma-aminobutyric acid (GABA) in the brain by binding to benzodiazepine receptors of the GABA receptor complex at a site distinct from that of benzodiazepine derivatives.", "pharmacologicalClass": "Cyclopyrrolone derivative"}, "pharmacokinetics": {"absorption": "Zopiclone is rapidly absorbed and widely distributed following oral administration.", "metabolism": "Zopiclone is extensively metabolized in the liver. The two major metabolites are zopiclone N-oxide and N-desmethyl-zopiclone.", "elimination": "Approximately 50% of the dose is metabolized into inactive metabolites eliminated via the lungs as carbon dioxide. Only about 5% of the unchanged dose appears in the urine and approximately 16% in the feces. The drug is excreted in saliva and breast milk."}, "contraindications": ["Hypersensitivity to zopiclone or any of the excipients.", "Myasthenia gravis, respiratory failure, severe sleep apnea syndrome, severe hepatic impairment.", "Pediatric patients."], "manufacturingInfo": {"storage": "Store in a tight container, in a dry place, protected from light. Temperature not exceeding 30°C."}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Adults: 7.5 mg. Elderly: 3.75 mg. Patients with renal impairment or mild-to-moderate hepatic impairment: 3.75 mg. Duration of therapy: Transient insomnia 2-5 days, short-term insomnia 2-3 weeks, not exceeding 4 weeks.", "missedDose": "Take as soon as possible. If it is almost time for the next dose, skip the missed dose and resume the regular dosing schedule. Do not double doses.", "administration": "The lowest effective dose should be used. Administer immediately before bedtime, while in an upright posture.", "overdoseManagement": "Symptoms: Somnolence, coma, ataxia. Management: Supportive care, administration of activated charcoal, gastric lavage (if necessary), intravenous flumazenil in cases of severe central nervous system depression."}, "generalDescription": "Zopistad 7.5 contains the active ingredient zopiclone, belonging to the cyclopyrrolone group, which possesses sedative, anxiolytic, skeletal muscle relaxant, and anticonvulsant properties. It is utilized for the short-term treatment of insomnia.", "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Zopiclone 7.5mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "Treatment should be initiated at a dose of 3.75 mg.", "lactation": "Use should be avoided as the drug is excreted in breast milk.", "pediatric": "Contraindicated.", "pregnancy": "Not recommended during pregnancy."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["The risk of drug dependence increases with dose and duration of therapy.", "Not indicated for the treatment of depression.", "Caution should be exercised regarding complex behaviors such as sleepwalking, sleep-driving, preparing and eating food, or making phone calls.", "Amnesia may occur, particularly if sleep is interrupted.", "The medication contains lactose; it should not be used in patients with galactose intolerance, total lactase deficiency, or glucose-galactose malabsorption."], "adverseReactionManagement": "Discontinue use and notify a physician or report to the nearest medical facility for prompt management."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:52:06.764	zopistad-7-5mg-tablets-for-short-term-treatment-of-insomnia-1-blister-x-10-tablets	\N
