oncentrations, increasing or decreasing absorption."}, {"drug": "Calcium channel blockers (Verapamil, Diltiazem, Nifedipine)", "effect": "Increases digoxin concentrations, raising the risk of toxicity and atrioventricular block."}, {"drug": "Diuretics", "effect": "May induce hypokalemia, increasing sensitivity to digoxin toxicity."}, {"drug": "NSAIDs", "effect": "May increase digoxin concentrations due to reduced renal clearance."}], "effectsOnDriving": "The medication may cause visual disturbances and central nervous system effects (somnolence, headache, fatigue, dizziness, disorientation). Patients should avoid driving and operating machinery if these effects occur.", "contraindications": ["Patients with hypersensitivity to digoxin, other digitalis glycosides, or any component of the medication.", "Patients with arrhythmias caused by digitalis glycoside toxicity.", "Patients with hypertrophic obstructive cardiomyopathy (unless coexisting with atrial fibrillation and heart failure).", "Patients with supraventricular arrhythmias associated with accessory atrioventricular pathways (such as Wolff-Parkinson-White syndrome).", "Patients with intermittent complete heart block or second-degree atrioventricular block, especially with a history of Stokes-Adams attacks.", "Patients with ventricular tachycardia or ventricular fibrillation."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "3/2 PHARMACEUTICAL JOINT STOCK COMPANY (F.T.PHARMA)", "origin": "VIETNAM", "storage": "Store below 30°C, protect from moisture and light.", "packaging": "Box of 1 blister x 30 Tablets", "manufacturer": "3/2 PHARMACEUTICAL JOINT STOCK COMPANY (F.T.PHARMA)"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Dosage must be individualized according to age, body weight, and renal function. Adults and children over 10 years of age: Rapid digitalization dose 0.75 - 1.5 mg; slow digitalization dose 0.25 - 0.75 mg/daily; maintenance dose typically ranges from 0.125 - 0.25 mg/daily. Children under 10 years of age: Dosage is based on body weight and body surface area, requiring appropriate pharmaceutical formulations for precise dose division.", "administration": "Administered via oral route."}, "generalDescription": "Digoxin Qualy, manufactured by 3/2 Pharmaceutical Joint Stock Company, contains digoxin as the active pharmaceutical ingredient. The medication is indicated for the treatment of congestive heart failure and certain supraventricular arrhythmias, particularly atrial fibrillation.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "lactose monohydrate, wheat starch, talc, magnesium stearate, sodium starch glycolate", "activeIngredients": "Digoxin 0.25mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "Prone to toxicity due to age-related decline in renal function and lower body mass; frequent monitoring of serum digoxin concentrations is recommended.", "lactation": "Digoxin is excreted in breast milk, but it is not formally contraindicated during lactation.", "pediatric": "Pediatric patients are particularly sensitive to digoxin. Dosage must be adjusted based on body weight and body surface area.", "pregnancy": "Use only when the clinical benefits outweigh the potential risks to the fetus. Not strictly contraindicated, but requires caution."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Periodic monitoring of serum electrolytes and renal function is required.", "Use with caution in patients with cardiac arrhythmias, sinus node dysfunction, amyloid heart disease, myocarditis, beriberi heart disease, constrictive pericarditis, and severe respiratory disease.", "Exercise caution in conditions of hypokalemia, hypomagnesemia, and hypercalcemia.", "Exercise caution when performing direct current cardioversion (discontinue the medication 24 hours prior to the procedure).", "Contains lactose excipients; should not be administered to patients with rare hereditary problems of galactose intolerance, total lactase deficiency, or glucose-galactose malabsorption."], "adverseReactionManagement": "If adverse reactions occur, discontinue use of the medication and notify a physician or report to the nearest medical facility for timely management."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:52:46.697	digoxin-qualy-0-25mg-tablets-for-treatment-of-congestive-heart-failure-and-atrial-fibrillation-1	156
