al treatment: 1 - 2 drops per application every hour. Maintenance treatment: 1 - 2 drops per application 4 - 6 times daily. Ears: Adults: 1 - 5 drops per application, twice daily, for 6 - 10 days. Children: 1 - 2 drops per application, twice daily depending on age, for 6 - 10 days. Alternatively, allow the solution to contact the ear for a few minutes by inserting a cotton or gauze plug moistened with Mepoly solution, applied twice daily. Do not use pressure to instill the medication into the ear canal.", "administration": "The Mepoly container must be tightly closed after use."}, "generalDescription": "Mepoly, manufactured by Merap Group Joint Stock Company, contains neomycin, polymyxin B sulfate, and dexamethasone formulated as an ophthalmic, nasal, and otic solution.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Citric acid, sodium hydroxide, sodium chloride, thimerosal, purified water q.s. 10 ml.", "activeIngredients": "Neomycin (as Neomycin sulfate) 35mg, Polymyxin B sulfate 100,000 IU, Dexamethasone (as Dexamethasone sodium phosphate) 10mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "There is a potential risk of adverse effects in nursing infants. The decision whether to discontinue nursing or to discontinue Mepoly should take into account the importance of the drug to the mother and the risks to the infant.", "pediatric": "Safety and efficacy in pediatric patients have not been established. Consult a physician before use in children under 2 years of age.", "pregnancy": "Adequate and well-controlled studies regarding the use of the medication in pregnant women have not been conducted. Therefore, the medication should not be used unless clearly necessary."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Do not inject intraocularly.", "Prolonged use may suppress the host response, thereby increasing the hazard of secondary bacterial infections, fungal and viral infections, and masking clinical signs of infection.", "Do not use the medication continuously for extended periods. Intraocular pressure and the lens should be monitored when the drug is used for ocular indications for more than 10 days or in quantities exceeding 20 ml.", "Use with caution in pregnant and breastfeeding women.", "Safety and efficacy in pediatric patients have not been established. Consult a physician before use in children under 2 years of age."], "adverseReactionManagement": "If adverse reactions occur, discontinue use and notify a physician or go to the nearest medical facility for prompt management."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:52:56.595	merap-mepoly-neomycin-polymyxin-b-sulfate-dexamethasone-35mg-100-000iu-10mg-ophthalmic-nasal-and	383
1772	Glotadol Cold Tablets for Common Cold and Cough Symptoms (10 Blisters x 10 Tablets)	P11142	\N	\N	Glomed Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd. (Vietnam)	Vietnam	133333.00	120000.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/product/20241022082933-0-P11142_1.jpg?versionId=OoPTh7zGgXeCm17rX.eyNw8vaW5WhxT9	Glotadol Cold is a combination medication indicated for the relief of common cold and flu symptoms, including sneezing, runny nose, sore throat, cough, fever, headache, and body aches.	{"indications": ["Indicated for the treatment of symptoms associated with common colds and flu, such as sneezing, runny nose, sore throat, cough, fever, headache, and body aches."], "sideEffects": ["Paracetamol: Common: Rash, erythema, urticaria, nausea, vomiting, blood dyscrasias. Uncommon: Anemia, nephropathy, hypersensitivity reactions.", "Loratadine: Common: Headache, dry mouth, fatigue, somnolence. Uncommon: Dizziness, dry nose, sneezing, conjunctivitis, depression, tachycardia, nausea, abnormal liver function, rash, urticaria.", "Dextromethorphan: Common: Fatigue, dizziness, tachycardia, nausea, flushing. Uncommon: Urticaria, mild somnolence. Risk: Central nervous system depression and respiratory depression may occur in cases of overdose."], "drugInteractions": [{"drug": "Paracetamol", "effect": "Interacts with anticoagulants, alcohol, anticonvulsants, and isoniazid, increasing the risk of hepatotoxicity or altering drug efficacy."}, {"drug": "Loratadine", "effect": "Interacts with inhibitors or substrates metabolized via CYP3A4 and CYP2D6 (cimetidine, ketoconazole, erythromycin), altering loratadine plasma concentrations."}, {"drug": "Dextromethorphan", "effect": "Interacts with monoamine oxidase inhibitors (MAOIs), central nervous system depressants, valdecoxib, linezolid, and memantine, potentially causing adverse reactions or serotonin syndrome."}], "effectsOnDriving": "Exercise caution when driving or operating machinery, as dextromethorphan may cause dizziness and mild somnolence.", "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Glomed-Abbott", "origin": "Vietnam", "storage": "Store in a dry place, protected from light. Temperature not exceeding 30°C.", "packaging": "Box of 10 blisters x 10 film-coated tablets.", "manufacturer": "Glomed Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd. (Vietnam)"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Adults and children over 12 years old: Take 1 tablet per dose, twice daily. Children aged 6 to 12 years: Use according to physician's instructions.", "administration": "The medication should be administered with or after meals. Swallow the tablets whole with a glass of water; do not chew or crush the tablets."}, "generalDescription": "Glotadol Cold is a medication formulated for the treatment of common cold and flu symptoms. The medication combines active pharmaceutical ingredients to provide rapid relief from sneezing, rhinorrhea, pharyngitis, cough, pyrexia, cephalalgia, and myalgia.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Microcrystalline cellulose 101, pregelatinized starch, sodium starch glycolate A, colloidal silicon dioxide, povidone K30, talc, magnesium stearate, Opadry II white, brilliant blue, quinoline yellow lake.", "activeIngredients": "Paracetamol 500mg, Loratadine 5mg, Dextromethorphan hydrobromide 15mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "No adverse effects have been observed with paracetamol. Loratadine may excrete into breast milk and affect nursing infants. A decision should be made whether to discontinue nursing or discontinue the medication, taking into account the importance of the drug to the mother.", "pregnancy": "Safety during pregnancy has not been established. Use only when clearly necessary."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Paracetamol: Exercise caution in chronic alcoholics and patients with impaired hepatic or renal function. Do not consume alcohol while taking this medication.", "Loratadine: Use with caution in patients with hepatic impairment, renal insufficiency, those developing abnormal rashes, and the elderly.", "Dextromethorphan: Avoid alcohol consumption during treatment. Abuse or dependence may occur with high doses and prolonged use.", "Warning: Monitor for signs of severe cutaneous adverse reactions, such as Stevens-Johnson Syndrome (SJS), Toxic Epidermal Necrolysis (TEN) or Lyell's syndrome, and Acute Generalized Exanthematous Pustulosis (AGEP)."], "adverseReactionManagement": "Discontinue use and consult a physician if any abnormal signs, edema, rash, swelling, dizziness, insomnia occur, or if symptoms do not improve after 7 days, or if accompanied by a fever."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:53:03.357	glotadol-cold-tablets-for-common-cold-and-cough-symptoms-10-blisters-x-10-tablets	260
101	Guaiazulene 0.004g and Dimethicone 3g (Pepsane) Oral Gel for Gastric Ulcer and Inflammation (Box of 30 Sachets)	P00693	\N	\N	\N	Vietnam	6487.00	5384.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/ecommerce/20250508070554-0-P00693.jpg?versionId=tEtbc5hS8Y7oJDl2sw.6T5yl4D8ON0jh	Pepsane Oral Gel contains Guaiazulene 0.004g and Dimethicone 3g, indicated for the treatment of gastric ulcer and mucosal inflammation. Each package contains 30 oral sachets.	{"sideEffects": ["Hypersensitivity reactions: Rash and pruritus (Rare)"], "drugInteractions": [{"drug": "Other medications and dietary supplements", "effect": "May affect drug absorption or activity. Patients should inform their physician or pharmacist of all prescription, non-prescription medications, and supplements they are currently using."}], "effectsOnDriving": "There are no specific clinical studies evaluating the effects of the drug on the ability to drive and operate machinery. Based on the pharmacodynamic properties of the drug, the combination of dimethicone and guaiazulene is unlikely to impair this ability.", "contraindications": ["Hypersensitivity to any of the active ingredients or excipients of the drug.", "Patients with hereditary fructose intolerance (due to the presence of sorbitol)."], "manufacturingInfo": {"storage": "Store at controlled room temperature below 25°C, in a dry place protected from direct light."}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Standard adult dosage: Take 1 to 2 sachets per administration, 2 to 3 times daily.", "missedDose": "If a dose is missed, take it as soon as remembered. However, if it is almost time for the next scheduled dose, skip the missed dose and resume the normal dosing schedule. Do not take a double dose to make up for a forgotten dose.", "administration": "For oral administration. Take the gel directly from the sachet, preferably before meals or immediately upon the onset of acute pain.", "overdoseManagement": "No cases of acute overdose have been reported in clinical practice. In the event of an overdose, patients should be closely monitored and receive supportive symptomatic treatment."}, "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Sorbitol 70% non-crystallizing, carrageenan, sodium cyclamate, methyl parahydroxybenzoate (E 218), peppermint oil, purified water per 10g sachet.", "activeIngredients": "Guaiazulene 0.004g, Dimethicone 3g"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "Dimethicone can be safely used by nursing mothers. The product may be administered during breastfeeding as clinically warranted.", "pregnancy": "Dimethicone is considered safe for use during pregnancy. While adequate clinical data on guaiazulene exposure during pregnancy are limited, no specific teratogenic or malformative effects have been reported. The drug may be used during pregnancy when clearly indicated."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["This product contains methyl parahydroxybenzoate, which may trigger allergic reactions (potentially delayed type).", "If gastrointestinal symptoms persist, recur, or worsen after treatment, consult a physician for further evaluation."], "adverseReactionManagement": "Discontinue use and report any adverse reactions or unexpected symptoms encountered during therapy to your healthcare provider or pharmacist."}	f	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:19:06.31	guaiazulene-0-004g-and-dimethicone-3g-pepsane-oral-gel-for-gastric-ulcer-and-inflammation-box-of-30	\N
102	Budesonide/Formoterol Fumarate Dihydrate (Symbicort Turbuhaler) 160/4.5mcg Inhalation Powder for Asthma and COPD (1 Inhaler x 120 Doses)	P00690	\N	\N	\N	Vietnam	602179.00	469700.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/ecommerce/20250728074544-0-P00690.png?versionId=hXeh0ZYzJh2ANeaneOUjnXwGU3m_2vgn	Symbicort Turbuhaler 160/4.5mcg is a metered-dose inhalation powder containing budesonide and formoterol fumarate dihydrate, indicated for the regular treatment of asthma and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). Each device delivers 120 doses.	{"detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Budesonide 160mcg/dose, Formoterol Fumarate Dihydrate 4.5mcg/dose"}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["<h2>Adverse Reactions</h2>", "<p>When administering <strong>Symbicort</strong>, patients may experience adverse drug reactions (ADRs): </p>", "<p><em>Common: 1% to 10% (1/100 < ADR < 1/10)</em></p>", "<ul>", "<li>Cardiac disorders: Palpitations.</li>", "<li>Nervous system disorders: <strong>Headache</strong>, tremor.</li>", "<li>Respiratory, thoracic, and mediastinal disorders: Mild throat irritation, cough, dysphonia (hoarseness).</li>", "<li>Infections and infestations: Oropharyngeal <strong>candidiasis</strong>, pneumonia (in patients with COPD).</li>", "</ul>", "<p><em>Uncommon: 0.1% to 1% (1/1000 < ADR < 1/100)</em></p>", "<ul>", "<li>Cardiac disorders: Tachycardia.</li>", "<li>Gastrointestinal disorders: Nausea.</li>", "<li>Musculoskeletal and connective tissue disorders: Muscle cramps.</li>", "<li>Nervous system disorders: <strong>Dizziness</strong>.</li>", "<li>Eye disorders: Blurred vision.</li>", "<li>Psychiatric disorders: Psychomotor hyperactivity, sleep disturbances, anxiety.</li>", "<li>Skin and subcutaneous tissue disorders: Ecchymosis (bruising).</li>", "</ul>", "<p><em>Rare: 0.01% to 0.1% (1/10000 < ADR < 1/1000)</em></p>", "<ul>", "<li>Cardiac disorders: Cardiac arrhythmias, including atrial fibrillation, supraventricular tachycardia, and extrasystoles.</li>", "<li>Immune system disorders: Immediate and delayed hypersensitivity reactions, such as exanthema, dermatitis, <strong>urticaria</strong>, angioedema, and anaphylactic reactions.</li>", "<li>Metabolism and nutrition disorders: Hypokalemia.</li>", "<li>Respiratory, thoracic, and mediastinal disorders: Bronchospasm.</li>", "</ul>", "<p><em>Very rare: < 0.01% (ADR < 1/10000)</em></p>", "<ul>", "<li>Cardiac disorders: Angina pectoris, QT interval prolongation.</li>", "<li>Endocrine disorders: Cushing's syndrome, decreased bone mineral density, adrenal suppression, growth retardation in pediatric patients.</li>", "<li>Metabolism and nutrition disorders: Hyperglycemia.</li>", "<li>Nervous system disorders: Dysgeusia (taste disturbance).</li>", "<li>Eye disorders: <strong>Cataract</strong> and glaucoma.</li>", "<li>Psychiatric disorders: Depression, behavioral disturbances (predominantly in children).</li>", "<li>Vascular disorders: Blood pressure fluctuations.</li>", "</ul>", "<p><em>Instructions for ADR Management</em></p>", "<p>Patients must promptly notify their prescribing physician or healthcare provider of any adverse reactions encountered during therapy.</p>", "<h2>Warnings and Precautions</h2>", "<p>Prior to initiating treatment, read the patient information leaflet carefully and heed the precautions outlined below.</p>", "<h3>Contraindications</h3>", "<p><strong>Symbicort</strong> is contraindicated in the following clinical scenarios:</p>", "<ul>", "<li>", "<p>Hypersensitivity to budesonide, formoterol, or lactose excipients (which contain trace amounts of milk proteins).</p>", "</li>", "</ul>", "<h3>Precautions for Use</h3>", "<p>Dosage tapering should be implemented when discontinuing therapy, and treatment should not be abruptly withdrawn.</p>", "<p>If a patient perceives the treatment as ineffective or exceeds the maximum recommended dose of Symbicort, medical supervision is required (refer to Dosage and Administration). Sudden or progressive deterioration in the control of asthma or COPD is potentially life-threatening, necessitating immediate medical evaluation. In such clinical situations, the necessity for increased corticosteroid therapy (e.g., a course of oral corticosteroids) or antibiotic treatment for concomitant infection must be considered.</p>", "<p>Patients should be advised to maintain a separate rapid-acting rescue bronchodilator at all times, or use Symbicort as maintenance and reliever therapy where applicable.</p>", "<p>Patients must adhere to their prescribed Symbicort maintenance dosing regimen even during asymptomatic periods. Prophylactic administration of Symbicort prior to specific triggers (e.g., exercise) has not been studied. Symbicort reliever inhalations are intended for acute symptom relief rather than routine prophylaxis. A separate rapid-acting bronchodilator should be considered for exercise-induced bronchospasm prophylaxis.</p>", "<p>Once asthma symptoms are controlled, gradual dose reduction of Symbicort should be considered, with regular monitoring of lung function and symptom control. The lowest effective dose should always be maintained.</p>", "<p>Symbicort should not be initiated during an acute asthma exacerbation or during acute, severe deteriorations of COPD.</p>", "<p>Serious asthma-related adverse events and exacerbations may occur during treatment. Patients should continue therapy but seek medical evaluation if symptoms remain uncontrolled or worsen.</p>", "<p>Clinical data regarding Symbicort Turbuhaler in COPD patients with pre-bronchodilator FEV1 > 50% of predicted and post-bronchodilator FEV1 < 70% of predicted are limited.</p>", "<p>As with other inhalation therapies, paradoxical bronchospasm may occur, manifested by an immediate and marked increase in wheezing and shortness of breath post-inhalation. This requires the immediate discontinuation of Symbicort, clinical assessment, and initiation of alternative therapy or rapid-acting inhaled bronchodilators.</p>", "<p>Systemic effects may occur with any inhaled corticosteroid, particularly at high doses prescribed for prolonged periods. Such effects are significantly less frequent than with oral corticosteroids and may include Cushing's syndrome, adrenal suppression, growth retardation, decreased bone mineral density, cataract, glaucoma, and psychiatric manifestations.</p>", "<p>Bone mineral density should be monitored in patients with major risk factors for osteoporosis who receive long-term high-dose therapy.</p>", "<p>Caution is warranted when transferring patients from systemic corticosteroids to Symbicort due to potential latent adrenal insufficiency. Hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal (HPA) axis function must be monitored regularly in these patients.</p>", "<p>Prolonged treatment with high doses of inhaled corticosteroids may result in clinically significant adrenal suppression; consequently, systemic corticosteroid supplementation should be considered during periods of physiological stress or elective surgery. Abrupt cessation may precipitate an acute adrenal crisis.</p>", "<p>During transition from oral steroids to Symbicort, unmasked allergic or arthritic symptoms (e.g., rhinitis, eczema, myalgia, arthralgia) may emerge, requiring targeted treatment.</p>", "<p>To minimize oropharyngeal candidiasis, patients must be instructed to rinse their mouths thoroughly with water and spit it out after each maintenance inhalation.</p>", "<p>Concomitant administration with potent CYP3A4 inhibitors (e.g., ketoconazole, itraconazole, ritonavir) should be avoided. If unavoidable, the time interval between interacting drugs should be maximized.</p>", "<p>Symbicort should be administered with caution in patients with thyrotoxicosis, pheochromocytoma, diabetes mellitus, untreated hypokalemia, hypertrophic obstructive cardiomyopathy, severe hypertension, aneurysm, or other severe cardiovascular disorders.</p>", "<p>Caution is required when treating patients with a prolonged QTc interval, as formoterol may prolong cardiac repolarization.</p>", "<p>Pulmonary tuberculosis and fungal or viral respiratory infections require careful clinical re-evaluation of corticosteroid requirements.</p>", "<p>Beta2-agonists can induce potentially dangerous hypokalemia; serum potassium levels should be monitored closely, especially in acute severe asthma and when coadministered with xanthine derivatives, steroids, or diuretics.</p>", "<p>Blood glucose monitoring should be enhanced in diabetic patients due to the intrinsic glycemic effects of beta2-agonists.</p>", "<p>Visual disturbances (including blurred vision, cataract, glaucoma, or central serous chorioretinopathy) reported with corticosteroid use warrant ophthalmological evaluation.</p>", "<p>Symbicort Turbuhaler contains lactose monohydrate (< 1 mg per inhalation), which generally does not affect lactose-intolerant patients, though trace milk protein content may rarely trigger hypersensitivity.</p>", "<p><em>Pediatric Population</em></p>", "<p>Linear growth in pediatric patients receiving long-term inhaled corticosteroids should be monitored regularly. If growth deceleration occurs, the dosing regimen should be re-evaluated.</p>", "<p><em>Pneumonia in COPD Patients</em></p>", "<p>An increased incidence of pneumonia has been observed in COPD patients receiving inhaled corticosteroids. Clinicians must remain vigilant for clinical signs of pneumonia, which often overlap with COPD exacerbation symptoms.</p>", "<h3>Effects on Driving and Operating Machinery</h3>", "<p>Symbicort has no or negligible influence on the ability to drive and use machines.</p>", "<h3>Pregnancy</h3>", "<p>Clinical data on the use of Symbicort during pregnancy are lacking. Animal reproduction studies with budesonide and formoterol combinations have shown no evidence of teratogenic synergy. Use during pregnancy should be restricted to cases where the anticipated clinical benefit clearly outweighs potential fetal risks, utilizing the lowest effective budesonide dose.</p>", "<h3>Lactation</h3>", "<p>Budesonide is excreted in breast milk, but therapeutic doses are unlikely to affect the nursing infant. It remains unknown whether formoterol passes into human breast milk. Administration during breastfeeding should be considered only if the expected benefit to the mother outweighs any potential risk to the infant.</p>", "<h3>Drug Interactions</h3>", "<p><em>Pharmacokinetic Interactions</em></p>", "<p>Potent CYP3A4 inhibitors (such as ketoconazole, itraconazole, <strong>voriconazole</strong>, posaconazole, clarithromycin, <strong>telithromycin</strong>, nefazodone, and HIV protease inhibitors) markedly increase plasma budesonide concentrations and should be coadministered with extreme caution or avoided.</p>", "<p><em>Pharmacodynamic Interactions</em></p>", "<p>Beta-adrenergic receptor blockers can weaken or antagonize the therapeutic effect of formoterol; hence, non-selective beta-blockers should be avoided unless medically mandatory.</p>", "<p>Concomitant administration with quinidine, disopyramide, procainamide, <strong>phenothiazines</strong>, antihistamines (e.g., terfenadine), and tricyclic antidepressants may prolong the QTc interval and elevate ventricular arrhythmia risks.</p>", "<p>MAO inhibitors and agents with similar properties (e.g., furazolidone, procarbazine) may precipitate hypertensive crises when coadministered with formoterol.</p>"]}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:19:10.256	budesonide-formoterol-fumarate-dihydrate-symbicort-turbuhaler-160-4-5mcg-inhalation-powder-for	\N
