coagulants", "effect": "Parenteral and oral penicillins may alter platelet aggregation and coagulation tests, potentially potentiating the effects of concomitant anticoagulant therapy."}, {"drug": "Bacteriostatic agents (Chloramphenicol, Erythromycin, Sulfonamides, and Tetracyclines)", "effect": "Bacteriostatic drugs may interfere with the bactericidal action of penicillins; concurrent administration should generally be avoided."}, {"drug": "Estrogen-containing oral contraceptives", "effect": "May reduce the efficacy of estrogen-containing oral contraceptives, leading to breakthrough bleeding or unintended pregnancy; alternative or additional contraceptive methods are advised."}, {"drug": "Methotrexate", "effect": "Concomitant use decreases the renal clearance of methotrexate, resulting in elevated plasma concentrations and increased risk of methotrexate toxicity."}, {"drug": "Probenecid", "effect": "Probenecid decreases the renal tubular secretion of both ampicillin and sulbactam, leading to prolonged and elevated serum antibiotic concentrations and an increased risk of toxicity."}], "effectsOnDriving": "Adverse effects such as dizziness, somnolence, or convulsions may occur. Patients experiencing these symptoms should exercise caution when driving or operating machinery.", "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Pfizer PBG", "storage": "Store at controlled room temperature, protected from excessive moisture and direct sunlight.", "packaging": "Carton containing 2 blister packs, with each blister pack containing 4 film-coated tablets.", "manufacturer": "Borgo S. Michele S.S 156 Km 47,600-04100 Latina (LT), Italy"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Adults and adolescents: 375mg to 750mg orally twice daily. Uncomplicated gonorrhea: 2.25g (six 375mg tablets) administered as a single oral dose (with 1g probenecid if clinically indicated). Pediatric patients weighing less than 30 kg: 25 to 50 mg/kg/day administered in two divided doses. Pediatric patients weighing 30 kg or more: receive the recommended adult dosage.", "administration": "Administer orally with or without food as directed by a healthcare professional. Therapy should be continued for at least 48 hours after the patient becomes asymptomatic or fever-free, with a standard treatment duration ranging from 5 to 14 days."}, "generalDescription": "Unasyn 375mg film-coated tablets contain sultamicillin tosylate, which hydrolyzes to yield ampicillin and sulbactam in an active 1:1 molar ratio during absorption. Ampicillin provides bactericidal activity against susceptible organisms by inhibiting bacterial cell wall synthesis, while sulbactam irreversibly inhibits beta-lactamase enzymes, effectively expanding ampicillin's antibacterial spectrum against penicillin-resistant strains.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Anhydrous lactose, dried corn starch, sodium starch glycolate, hydroxypropyl cellulose, magnesium stearate, polyethylene glycol 6000, hypromellose (hydroxypropyl methylcellulose), titanium dioxide, and talc.", "activeIngredients": "Sultamicillin tosylate equivalent to 375mg sultamicillin base (yielding 147mg sulbactam and 220mg ampicillin per tablet)"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "Administer standard adult dosage, with careful monitoring for age-related renal function decline.", "lactation": "Low concentrations of ampicillin and sulbactam are excreted in breast milk. Caution should be exercised when administering to nursing mothers, and breastfed infants should be monitored for potential gastrointestinal flora disruption or sensitization.", "pediatric": "Use with caution in neonates and young infants, taking into account immature renal clearance mechanisms.", "pregnancy": "Adequate and well-controlled studies have not been conducted in pregnant women. Sulbactam crosses the placental barrier; use only if clearly needed and prescribed by a physician."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Serious and occasionally fatal hypersensitivity (anaphylactic) reactions have been reported in patients receiving beta-lactam therapy. Careful inquiry regarding prior hypersensitivity reactions to penicillins, cephalosporins, or other allergens is mandatory prior to initiation.", "Prolonged use may result in the overgrowth of non-susceptible organisms, including fungi and resistant bacteria, requiring discontinuation or appropriate alternative therapy if superinfection occurs.", "Clostridium difficile-associated diarrhea (CDAD) has been reported with nearly all antibacterial agents and may range in severity from mild diarrhea to fatal colitis.", "Do not administer to patients with infectious mononucleosis due to the high incidence of maculopapular rash associated with ampicillin use in these patients.", "Periodic assessment of organ system functions, including renal, hepatic, and hematopoietic systems, is advisable during prolonged therapy.", "Exercise extreme caution when administering to neonates and infants due to incompletely developed renal function affecting drug elimination."]}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:21:05.473	unasyn-sultamicillin-375mg-film-coated-tablets-for-bacterial-infections-2-blister-packs-x-4-tablets	\N
