agnostic radioiodine scintigraphy.", "Neonates with a birth weight of less than 1.5 kg."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Betadine", "origin": "Republic of Cyprus", "storage": "Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C.", "packaging": "Carton containing 1 dropper bottle of 30 mL solution.", "manufacturer": "Mundipharma Pharmaceuticals Ltd."}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Hygienic hand disinfection: Apply 3 mL of undiluted solution for 1 minute. Surgical hand disinfection: Apply 2 x 5 mL of undiluted solution for 5 minutes. Skin antisepsis: For skin with low sebaceous gland density, apply for at least 1 minute; for skin with high sebaceous gland density, apply for at least 10 minutes, ensuring the operative field remains continuously moist throughout the procedure.", "missedDose": "Apply the topical dose as soon as remembered. If the scheduled time for the next application is near, omit the missed dose and resume the standard dosing regimen. Do not apply a double dose to compensate for a missed application.", "administration": "For external topical application only. Apply the undiluted stock solution evenly to the target treatment area. Allow to dry to form an air-permeable protective film that can be easily rinsed off with water. May be applied repeatedly at designated intervals as required.", "overdoseManagement": "Acute iodine toxicity manifests clinically with symptoms such as abdominal pain, anuria, circulatory collapse, laryngeal edema leading to acute respiratory distress, pulmonary edema, and severe metabolic derangements. Immediate discontinuation, symptomatic management, and supportive medical care are required."}, "generalDescription": "Betadine Antiseptic Solution 30 mL, manufactured by Mundipharma Pharmaceuticals Ltd, contains Povidone-Iodine 10% w/v as the active pharmaceutical ingredient. It is widely utilized as a standard antiseptic preparation for surgical antisepsis, wound management, and infection prophylaxis.", "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Povidone-Iodine 10% w/v"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "Should be used during lactation only when strictly indicated and at the minimum effective dose, as absorbed iodine is excreted into breast milk and may affect the nursing infant's thyroid function.", "pediatric": "Neonates and young children should receive only the minimum effective dose, with close monitoring of thyroid function parameters.", "pregnancy": "Should be used during pregnancy only when clinically indicated, restricted to the minimum effective dose, and extensive surface application should be avoided."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["For external use only. Prevent pooling of the liquid under the patient during prolonged procedures to avoid chemical skin irritation or caustic burns.", "Discontinue use immediately if signs of local skin irritation, contact dermatitis, or hypersensitivity develop.", "Do not heat the solution prior to topical application.", "Patients with latent goiter, nodular goiter, or other non-toxic thyroid disorders require careful clinical risk-benefit evaluation prior to prolonged or extensive surface application.", "Neonates and infants are at high risk for developing hypothyroidism or hyperthyroidism; use the minimum effective dose and prevent accidental ingestion."], "adverseReactionManagement": "In the event of adverse drug reactions or hypersensitivity symptoms, discontinue application immediately, notify your attending physician or pharmacist, and seek prompt medical evaluation at the nearest healthcare facility."}	f	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:22:02.905	betadine-antiseptic-solution-povidone-iodine-10percent-w-v-topical-disinfectant-and-infection	386
