e is one tablet once daily, taken in the morning. The maximum recommended dose is 10 mg/320 mg/25 mg daily.", "missedDose": "Take the missed dose as soon as you remember. If it is almost time for your next dose, skip the missed dose and resume your regular dosing schedule. Do not double the dose to make up for a forgotten dose.", "administration": "Oral administration. Tablets should be swallowed whole with adequate fluid (e.g., a glass of water), with or without food.", "overdoseManagement": "Overdose may lead to marked systemic hypotension, dizziness, excessive peripheral vasodilation, and reflex tachycardia. Cases of profound and prolonged hypotension, including shock and fatal outcomes, have been reported. Management includes induction of emesis, gastric lavage, or administration of activated charcoal. Supportive cardiovascular care is essential, including continuous cardiac and respiratory monitoring, elevation of extremities, and monitoring of circulating fluid volume and urine output. Vasopressors may be indicated for vascular tone support, and intravenous calcium gluconate may help reverse calcium channel blockade. Valsartan and amlodipine are not dialyzable; hydrochlorothiazide can be eliminated via hemodialysis."}, "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Amlodipine 10mg (as amlodipine besylate), Valsartan 160mg, Hydrochlorothiazide 12.5mg"}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Use with caution in patients with hepatic impairment or obstructive biliary disorders. In patients with mild to moderate hepatic impairment without cholestasis, the maximum recommended dose of valsartan is 80 mg; since amlodipine dosage recommendations have not been established for this population, the lowest available dose of amlodipine should be utilized. Monitor serum electrolytes periodically for signs of electrolyte imbalance."]}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:23:11.974	exforge-hct-10mg-160mg-12-5mg-tablets-for-hypertension-4-blisters-x-7-tablets	\N
