, Beh - et's disease.", "Second-degree burns or higher."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Shinpoong Pharma (South Korea)", "origin": "South Korea", "storage": "Store in a cool place, protected from light, at temperatures below 30°C (86°F). Keep out of reach of children.", "manufacturer": "Shinpoong Daewoo Pharma Co., Ltd."}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Duration of treatment depends on the severity and location of the condition, and patient response. If no clinical improvement is observed after 1-2 weeks of treatment, the diagnosis should be re-evaluated. Do not use for more than 5 days in children. Do not apply for more than 5 days on the face, intertriginous areas, or extensive skin areas.", "missedDose": "Apply the missed dose as soon as remembered. If the interval to the next dose is too short, skip the missed dose and continue with the regular dosing schedule. Do not apply a double dose.", "administration": "Apply a small amount of Gentrisone cream to the affected area once or several times daily. Apply a thin layer of cream and gently rub into the affected skin area twice daily. Do not occlude the treated area. Avoid contact with eyes.", "overdoseManagement": "Acute overdose with topical application is highly unlikely. If systemic absorption occurs, symptomatic treatment should be administered. If ingested, symptomatic treatment should be provided."}, "generalDescription": "Shinpoong Gentri-Sone 20g Cream, manufactured by ShinPoong Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd. (part of Daewoo International Group), is indicated for the treatment of cutaneous fungal infections caused by Candida albicans and tinea versicolor caused by Malassezia furfur. It is also indicated for the treatment of tinea corporis (ringworm), tinea cruris (jock itch), and tinea pedis (athlete's foot) caused by Trichophyton rubrum, T. mentagrophytes, Epidermophyton floccosum, or Microsporum canis; or superficial skin infections caused by susceptible bacterial strains.", "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Gentamicin 0.05% (as Gentamicin sulfate), Betamethasone dipropionate 0.032% (equivalent to Betamethasone), Clotrimazole 0.5%."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Systemic and local toxicity may occur with prolonged use, on extensive damaged skin, intertriginous areas, or under occlusive dressings. HPA axis suppression, Cushing's syndrome, and visual disturbances should be monitored. Pediatric patients are more susceptible to systemic toxicity. This product contains propylparaben and methylparaben, which may cause delayed allergic reactions."], "adverseReactionManagement": "Discontinue use and inform your physician or seek immediate medical attention at the nearest healthcare facility for timely management."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:34:55.89	shinpoong-gentri-sone-topical-cream-betamethasone-dipropionate-0-032percent-clotrimazole-0-5percent	391
