nts using hepatic enzyme-inducing drugs, a double dose (3000 mcg) may be required as clinically directed.", "missedDose": "The medication is intended for single-dose administration; therefore, missed-dose scenarios do not apply.", "administration": "For oral administration. Swallow the tablet whole with water if necessary.", "overdoseManagement": "No reports of severe adverse effects following overdose. Overdose may cause nausea and withdrawal bleeding. There is no specific antidote; management should be symptomatic."}, "generalDescription": "Postinor 1 is an emergency contraceptive medication that can be used within 72 hours following unprotected intercourse or the failure of a primary contraceptive method.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Colloidal anhydrous silica, potato starch, magnesium stearate, talc, maize starch, lactose monohydrate", "activeIngredients": "Levonorgestrel 1.5mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "A small amount of the active substance passes into breast milk. It is recommended to take the tablet immediately after breastfeeding and avoid subsequent breastfeeding for at least 8 hours thereafter to reduce infant exposure.", "pregnancy": "Should not be administered to pregnant women. The medication is not an abortifacient. In the event of treatment failure and pregnancy continuation, ectopic pregnancy must be ruled out by a physician."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Not recommended for use as a routine contraceptive method", "Use of emergency contraception more than once within the same menstrual cycle increases the likelihood of menstrual irregularities", "Does not protect against pregnancy in the event of subsequent unprotected intercourse", "Medical evaluation should be considered if menstruation is delayed, abnormal menstrual bleeding occurs, unprotected intercourse occurred more than 72 hours prior, in patients with severe malabsorption syndromes (such as Crohn's disease), or severe hepatic impairment", "Contains 142.5 mg of la