ue to the bitter properties of berberine, leading to reduced digestive capacity. Management should be symptomatic and supportive."}, "generalDescription": "Berberal 10mg sugar-coated tablets are manufactured by 2/9 Pharmaceutical Joint Stock Company (Nadyphar), with Berberine chloride as the primary active ingredient. This medication exerts principal therapeutic effects for the treatment of dysentery and diarrhea. Berberal demonstrates antimicrobial activity against strains such as Staphylococcus aureus, hemolytic streptococci, Bordetella pertussis, Salmonella typhi, paratyphoid bacilli, Shigella (dysentery), and Mycobacterium tuberculosis.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Excipients q.s. 1 tablet", "activeIngredients": "Berberine Chloride 10mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "Safe for use.", "pregnancy": "Contraindicated due to the potential of berberine to induce uterine contractions, which may adversely affect the fetus."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Drink plenty of water during the course of treatment with Berberal.", "Discontinue the medication if signs of intolerance occur.", "Individuals with severe hepatic, renal, cardiovascular, or blood pressure disorders should consult a physician prior to initiating treatment."]}	f	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:45:55.89	berberal-10mg-sugar-coated-tablets-for-bacillary-dysentery-amoebic-dysentery-enteritis-and-diarrhea	16
