uence on the ability to drive and use machines.", "pharmacodynamics": {"mechanismOfAction": "Perindopril arginine inhibits ACE, leading to a reduction in angiotensin II and aldosterone production, thereby decreasing blood pressure. Amlodipine inhibits calcium ion influx across cell membranes of vascular smooth muscle and cardiac muscle, causing peripheral arterial vasodilation and a reduction in blood pressure.", "pharmacologicalClass": "Angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitors and calcium channel blockers."}, "pharmacokinetics": {"absorption": "Perindopril is rapidly absorbed and converted into its active metabolite, perindoprilat. Amlodipine is slowly absorbed following oral administration.", "metabolism": "Perindopril is metabolized in the liver to perindoprilat, the active ACE inhibitor moiety.", "elimination": "Amlodipine has a long terminal elimination half-life, providing sustained antihypertensive efficacy over a 24-hour period."}, "contraindications": ["Related to Perindopril: Hypersensitivity to perindopril or any other ACE inhibitors. History of angioedema associated with previous ACE inhibitor therapy. Hereditary or idiopathic angioedema. Second and third trimesters of pregnancy. Concomitant use with aliskiren-containing products in patients with diabetes mellitus or renal impairment (GFR < 60 mL/min/1.73m - ).", "Related to Amlodipine: Severe hypotension. Hypersensitivity to amlodipine or dihydropyridine derivatives. Shock, including cardiogenic shock. Obstruction of the outflow tract of the left ventricle (e.g., severe aortic stenosis). Hemodynamically unstable heart failure following acute myocardial infarction.", "Related to Coveram: Contraindications associated with each individual component. Hypersensitivity to any of the excipients."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Servier", "origin": "Ireland", "storage": "Keep out of the sight and reach of children. Store in the original package, keep the container tightly closed, store below 30°C in a dry place, and protect from light.", "packaging": "Box of 30 Tablets", "manufacturer": "Servier Industries Ltd"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "The fixed-dose combination is not suitable for initial therapy. If titration is required, dosage adjustment should be made with Coveram or with individual components administered as free combinations.", "administration": "Administer one tablet orally once daily, preferably in the morning before a meal.", "overdoseManagement": "[object Object]"}, "generalDescription": "Coveram 10mg/10mg tablets are a cardiovascular medication indicated for the treatment of hypertension and stable coronary artery disease, comprising two active pharmaceutical ingredients: Perindopril arginine and Amlodipine.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Lactose monohydrate, magnesium stearate (E470B), microcrystalline cellulose (E460), colloidal anhydrous silica (E551)", "activeIngredients": "Perindopril arginine (10mg) and Amlodipine (10mg)"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "Regular medical monitoring, including routine evaluation of serum creatinine and potassium levels, is required. Caution should be exercised when increasing the amlodipine dose.", "lactation": "Not recommended. A decision must be made whether to discontinue breastfeeding or to discontinue Coveram therapy, taking into account the importance of the drug to the mother.", "pediatric": "Not recommended for use in children and adolescents.", "pregnancy": "Not recommended during the first trimester of pregnancy and strictly contraindicated during the second and third trimesters of pregnancy."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Fertility, pregnancy, and lactation: Not recommended during the first trimester of pregnancy; strictly contraindicated during the second and third trimesters of pregnancy. Use during breastfeeding is not recommended."]}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:46:09.209	coveram-10mg-10mg-tablets-for-treatment-of-hypertension-and-stable-coronary-artery-disease-box-of	17
